{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:56:22.251Z","ordinal":10532,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a5d850ac487d0aa131acbd23e4ecf","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’m continuing from the evidence-backed point: the concurrent run proved Copilot’s stop hook carries the child UUID, while the parent transcript supplies the stable task ID and child-scoped file/token data. I’m tightening that mapping now, then I’ll update the spec and implement the smallest durable path—without inventing child transcript files or duplicating the shared subagent machinery."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788501381121,"completed_at_ms":1788501382251}}
