{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:57:40.122Z","ordinal":10590,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a5dd0cd0c87d0ad0516551681e47e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_NxKPFBVV1rGoqO5qh4KUkQNx","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"sed -n '1,230p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/types.go; sed -n '1,380p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go; sed -n '1,620p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go; rg -n \\\"type SessionStore|func OpenSessionStore|func \\\\(.*SessionStore\\\" cmd/entire/cli/agent -g '*.go'; sed -n '1,260p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go 2>/dev/null || true; sed -n '1,260p' docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md; sed -n '1,300p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":50000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788501455.68294}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:57:40.223Z","ordinal":10591,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a3f0096c-ae56-406a-8965-ba8ae2626b70","process_id":"4717","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,230p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/types.go; sed -n '1,380p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go; sed -n '1,620p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go; rg -n \"type SessionStore|func OpenSessionStore|func \\(.*SessionStore\" cmd/entire/cli/agent -g '*.go'; sed -n '1,260p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go 2>/dev/null || true; sed -n '1,260p' docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md; sed -n '1,300p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,230p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/types.go; sed -n '1,380p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go; sed -n '1,620p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go; rg -n \"type SessionStore|func OpenSessionStore|func \\(.*SessionStore\" cmd/entire/cli/agent -g '*.go'; sed -n '1,260p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go 2>/dev/null || true; sed -n '1,260p' docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md; sed -n '1,300p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"package copilotcli\n\n// CopilotHooksFile represents the .github/hooks/entire.json structure.\n// Copilot CLI uses a flat JSON file with version and hooks sections.\n// All JSON files in .github/hooks/ are auto-discovered by the Copilot CLI.\n//\n\ntype CopilotHooksFile struct {\n\tVersion int          `json:\"version\"`\n\tHooks   CopilotHooks `json:\"hooks\"`\n}\n\n// CopilotHooks contains all hook configurations using camelCase keys.\n//\n\ntype CopilotHooks struct {\n\tUserPromptSubmitted []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"userPromptSubmitted,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionStart        []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"sessionStart,omitempty\"`\n\tAgentStop           []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"agentStop,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionEnd          []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"sessionEnd,omitempty\"`\n\tSubagentStop        []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"subagentStop,omitempty\"`\n\tPreToolUse          []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"preToolUse,omitempty\"`\n\tPostToolUse         []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"postToolUse,omitempty\"`\n\tErrorOccurred       []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"errorOccurred,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// CopilotHookEntry represents a single hook command.\n// Copilot CLI hooks have a type field (\"command\") and a bash field for the command string.\n// Optional fields (cwd, timeoutSec, env, comment) are preserved on round-trip.\n\ntype CopilotHookEntry struct {\n\tType       string            `json:\"type\"`\n\tBash       string            `json:\"bash\"`\n\tComment    string            `json:\"comment,omitempty\"`\n\tCwd        string            `json:\"cwd,omitempty\"`\n\tTimeoutSec int               `json:\"timeoutSec,omitempty\"`\n\tEnv        map[string]string `json:\"env,omitempty\"`\n}\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n)\n\n// HooksFileName is the hooks file managed by Entire for Copilot CLI.\nconst HooksFileName = \"entire.json\"\n\n// hooksDir is the directory within the repo where Copilot CLI looks for hook configs.\nconst hooksDir = \".github/hooks\"\n\n// hookConfigKey maps our kebab-case hook names to camelCase JSON keys.\nvar hookConfigKey = map[string]string{\n\tHookNameUserPromptSubmitted: \"userPromptSubmitted\",\n\tHookNameSessionStart:        \"sessionStart\",\n\tHookNameAgentStop:           \"agentStop\",\n\tHookNameSessionEnd:          \"sessionEnd\",\n\tHookNameSubagentStop:        \"subagentStop\",\n\tHookNamePreToolUse:          \"preToolUse\",\n\tHookNamePostToolUse:         \"postToolUse\",\n\tHookNameErrorOccurred:       \"errorOccurred\",\n}\n\n// copilotHookConfig returns .github/hooks/entire.json for the current worktree,\n// opened through the worktree's root. That directory lives in the working tree,\n// which arrives by clone, so a checked-in symlink at `.github` or\n// `.github/hooks` must not be something Entire creates directories under and\n// writes through. See agent.HookConfigFile.\nfunc copilotHookConfig(ctx context.Context) (*agent.HookConfigFile, error) {\n\tworktreeRoot, err := paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\t// Not a repository (tests, and `enable` before `git init`): the process\n\t\t// directory is the only candidate, and it is a directory the caller\n\t\t// chose rather than one derived from anything read off disk.\n\t\tworktreeRoot = \".\"\n\t}\n\treturn agent.OpenHookConfig(worktreeRoot, (&CopilotCLIAgent{}).HookConfigRelPath()) //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n}\n\n// InstallHooks installs Copilot CLI hooks in .github/hooks/entire.json.\n// If force is true, removes existing Entire hooks before installing.\n// Returns the number of hooks installed.\n// Unknown top-level fields and hook types are preserved on round-trip.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) InstallHooks(ctx context.Context, force bool) (int, error) {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\n\t// Use raw maps to preserve unknown fields on round-trip\n\tvar rawFile map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tvar rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage\n\n\texistingData, readErr := cfg.Read()\n\tswitch {\n\tcase readErr == nil:\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(existingData, &rawFile); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse existing %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif hooksRaw, ok := rawFile[\"hooks\"]; ok {\n\t\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(hooksRaw, &rawHooks); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse hooks in %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, ok := rawFile[\"version\"]; !ok {\n\t\t\trawFile[\"version\"] = json.RawMessage(`1`)\n\t\t}\n\tcase errors.Is(readErr, os.ErrNotExist):\n\t\trawFile = map[string]json.RawMessage{\n\t\t\t\"version\": json.RawMessage(`1`),\n\t\t}\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read %s: %w\", HooksFileName, readErr)\n\t}\n\n\tif rawHooks == nil {\n\t\trawHooks = make(map[string]json.RawMessage)\n\t}\n\n\t// Parse existing entries for each hook type we manage\n\thookEntries := make(map[string][]CopilotHookEntry)\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tvar entries []CopilotHookEntry\n\t\tif err := parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, &entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\thookEntries[hookName] = entries\n\t}\n\n\t// If force, remove existing Entire hooks first\n\tif force {\n\t\tfor hookName, entries := range hookEntries {\n\t\t\thookEntries[hookName] = removeEntireHooks(entries)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Define command prefix\n\tconst cmdPrefix = \"entire hooks copilot-cli \"\n\n\tcount := 0\n\n\t// Sync each hook to its desired command. Entire-owned entries carrying any\n\t// other command are dropped first, even without --force: a hook written by\n\t// an older version would otherwise survive alongside the one added below and\n\t// keep firing, which for the removed local-dev mode means a script inside\n\t// the working tree still runs on every agent turn.\n\tstaleDropped := false\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tcmd := agent.WrapProductionSilentHookCommand(cmdPrefix + hookName)\n\t\tentries := hookEntries[hookName]\n\n\t\t// Keep the matching entry rather than remove-and-re-add: entry-level\n\t\t// fields (cwd, timeoutSec, env) live on the existing entry and a freshly\n\t\t// constructed one would discard them.\n\t\tkept, dropped := agent.DropStaleManagedHooks(entries, hookEntryBash, []string{cmd})\n\t\tif dropped {\n\t\t\tstaleDropped = true\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries = kept\n\n\t\tif !hookBashExists(entries, cmd) {\n\t\t\tentries = append(entries, CopilotHookEntry{\n\t\t\t\tType:    \"command\",\n\t\t\t\tBash:    cmd,\n\t\t\t\tComment: \"Entire CLI\",\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t\tcount++\n\t\t}\n\t\thookEntries[hookName] = entries\n\t}\n\n\t// staleDropped forces a write even when nothing was added: a file holding\n\t// both a stale and a current hook adds nothing, and returning early here\n\t// would leave the stale hook on disk.\n\tif count == 0 && !staleDropped {\n\t\treturn 0, nil\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal modified hook types back into rawHooks\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tif err := marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, hookEntries[hookName]); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal hooks and update raw file\n\thooksJSON, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(rawHooks)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hooks: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\trawFile[\"hooks\"] = hooksJSON\n\n\t// Write to file\n\toutput, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(rawFile, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tif err := cfg.Write(output, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n\t}\n\n\treturn count, nil\n}\n\n// UninstallHooks removes Entire hooks from Copilot CLI's entire.json.\n// Unknown top-level fields and hook types are preserved on round-trip.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) UninstallHooks(ctx context.Context) error {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := cfg.Read()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treturn nil // No hooks file means nothing to uninstall\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar rawFile map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &rawFile); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tif hooksRaw, ok := rawFile[\"hooks\"]; ok {\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(hooksRaw, &rawHooks); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse hooks in %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif rawHooks == nil {\n\t\trawHooks = make(map[string]json.RawMessage)\n\t}\n\n\t// Parse and remove Entire hooks from each hook type we manage\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tvar entries []CopilotHookEntry\n\t\tif err := parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, &entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries = removeEntireHooks(entries)\n\t\tif err := marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal hooks back (preserving unknown hook types)\n\tif len(rawHooks) > 0 {\n\t\thooksJSON, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(rawHooks)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hooks: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\trawFile[\"hooks\"] = hooksJSON\n\t} else {\n\t\tdelete(rawFile, \"hooks\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Write back\n\toutput, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(rawFile, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tif err := cfg.Write(output, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// AreHooksInstalled checks if Entire hooks are installed in the Copilot CLI\n// config.\n//\n// A missing config file is an answer — no hooks — while an unreadable or\n// malformed one is an error: \"we could not tell\" and \"there are none\" are\n// different things to a caller deciding whether hooks can be left alone.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) AreHooksInstalled(ctx context.Context) (bool, error) {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn false, err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := cfg.Read()\n\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn false, nil\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"copilot-cli: failed to read hooks file\", \"path\", cfg.Path(), \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %w\", cfg.Path(), err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar hooksFile CopilotHooksFile\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &hooksFile); err != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"copilot-cli: failed to parse hooks file\", \"path\", cfg.Path(), \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"parse %s: %w\", cfg.Path(), err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn hasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.UserPromptSubmitted) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SessionStart) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.AgentStop) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SessionEnd) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SubagentStop) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.PreToolUse) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.PostToolUse) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.ErrorOccurred), nil\n}\n\n// GetSupportedHooks returns the normalized lifecycle events this agent supports.\n// Note: HookNames() returns 8 hooks but GetSupportedHooks() returns only 6.\n// The two not listed here are:\n//   - subagentStop: handled by ParseHookEvent (returns SubagentEnd), but there is no\n//     HookType constant for subagent events (they use EventType instead).\n//   - errorOccurred: pass-through hook with no lifecycle action (ParseHookEvent returns nil).\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) GetSupportedHooks() []agent.HookType {\n\treturn []agent.HookType{\n\t\tagent.HookSessionStart,\n\t\tagent.HookSessionEnd,\n\t\tagent.HookUserPromptSubmit,\n\t\tagent.HookStop,\n\t\tagent.HookPreToolUse,\n\t\tagent.HookPostToolUse,\n\t}\n}\n\n// parseCopilotHookType parses a specific hook type from rawHooks into the target slice.\nfunc parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage, hookType string, target *[]CopilotHookEntry) error {\n\tif data, ok := rawHooks[hookType]; ok {\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, target); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid JSON for hook type %s: %w\", hookType, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// marshalCopilotHookType marshals a hook type back into rawHooks.\n// If the slice is empty, removes the key from rawHooks.\nfunc marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage, hookType string, entries []CopilotHookEntry) error {\n\tif len(entries) == 0 {\n\t\tdelete(rawHooks, hookType)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tdata, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(entries)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hook type %s: %w\", hookType, err)\n\t}\n\trawHooks[hookType] = data\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// hookBashExists checks if a hook with the given bash command already exists.\nfunc hookBashExists(entries []CopilotHookEntry, bash string) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif entry.Bash == bash {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// isEntireHook checks if a hook entry's bash command belongs to Entire.\n// hookEntryBash reads the command off a hook entry for the shared helpers.\n// Copilot CLI stores it under `bash`, not `command`.\nfunc hookEntryBash(e CopilotHookEntry) string { return e.Bash }\n\nfunc isEntireHook(bash string) bool {\n\treturn agent.IsManagedHookCommand(bash)\n}\n\n// hasEntireHook checks if any entry in the slice is an Entire hook.\nfunc hasEntireHook(entries []CopilotHookEntry) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif isEntireHook(entry.Bash) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// removeEntireHooks removes all Entire hooks from the slice.\nfunc removeEntireHooks(entries []CopilotHookEntry) []CopilotHookEntry {\n\tresult := make([]CopilotHookEntry, 0, len(entries))\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif !isEntireHook(entry.Bash) {\n\t\t\tresult = append(result, entry)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn result\n}\n\n// HookConfigRelPath implements agent.HookConfigLocator.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) HookConfigRelPath() string { return hooksDir + \"/\" + HooksFileName }\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n)\n\n// testSessionID is the UUID used in captured Copilot CLI hook payloads.\nconst testSessionID = \"b0ff98c0-8e01-4b73-bf92-9649b139931b\"\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Prompt != \"hi\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected prompt 'hi', got %q\", event.Prompt)\n\t}\n\tif event.Timestamp.IsZero() {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected non-zero timestamp\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted_TranscriptRef(t *testing.T) {\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tt.Setenv(\"ENTIRE_TEST_COPILOT_SESSION_DIR\", \"/test/sessions\")\n\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"test-sess-id\",\"prompt\":\"hello\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\texpected := \"/test/sessions/test-sess-id/events.jsonl\"\n\tif event.SessionRef != expected {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected SessionRef %q, got %q\", expected, event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"transcript_path\":\"/tmp/transcript.json\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Prompt != \"hi\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected prompt 'hi', got %q\", event.Prompt)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != \"/tmp/transcript.json\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionStart(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081383,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"source\":\"new\",\"initialPrompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Timestamp.IsZero() {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected non-zero timestamp\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionStart_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\ttranscriptPath := \"/home/user/.copilot/session-state/\" + testSessionID + \"/events.jsonl\"\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"transcriptPath\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != transcriptPath {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\ttranscriptPath := \"/tmp/transcript.json\"\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"Stop\",\"transcript_path\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != transcriptPath {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop_ExtractsModel(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\t// Create a temp transcript with tool.execution_complete containing model field\n\t// (Copilot CLI v0.0.421+ includes model per tool call, not via session.model_change)\n\tdir := t.TempDir()\n\ttranscriptPath := filepath.Join(dir, \"events.jsonl\")\n\ttranscriptContent := strings.Join([]string{\n\t\t`{\"type\":\"session.start\",\"data\":{\"sessionId\":\"model-sess\"},\"id\":\"1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-03T00:00:00Z\",\"parentId\":null}`,\n\t\t`{\"type\":\"user.message\",\"data\":{\"content\":\"hello\"},\"id\":\"2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-03T00:00:01Z\",\"parentId\":\"\"}`,\n\t\t`{\"type\":\"tool.execution_complete\",\"data\":{\"toolCallId\":\"tc1\",\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4.6\",\"toolTelemetry\":{\"properties\":{},\"metrics\":{}}},\"id\":\"3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-03T00:00:02Z\",\"parentId\":\"\"}`,\n\t}, \"\\n\") + \"\\n\"\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(transcriptPath, []byte(transcriptContent), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"failed to write test transcript: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"model-sess\",\"transcriptPath\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Model != \"claude-sonnet-4.6\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected model 'claude-sonnet-4.6', got %q\", event.Model)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop_NoTranscript_EmptyModel(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t// transcriptPath points to a nonexistent file — model should be empty, not error\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"no-model-sess\",\"transcriptPath\":\"/nonexistent/events.jsonl\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Model != \"\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected empty model for nonexistent transcript, got %q\", event.Model)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionEnd(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085425,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"reason\":\"complete\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionEnd, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionEnd_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t// VS Code uses \"Stop\" for both agent-stop and session-end hooks.\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"Stop\",\"reason\":\"complete\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionEnd, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionEnd_VSCodeNonTerminalStop_ReturnsNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"Stop\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionEnd, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif event != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for non-terminal VS Code Stop payload, got %+v\", event)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_VSCodeMismatchedHookEventName_ReturnsNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t// VS Code sends \"SessionStart\" but the CLI subcommand is \"agent-stop\" — mismatch.\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"transcript_path\":\"/tmp/t.json\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif event != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for mismatched hookEventName, got %+v\", event)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_VSCodeUnknownHookEventName_ReturnsNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"FutureEvent\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif event != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for unknown hookEventName, got %+v\", event)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_PassthroughHooks_VSCodePayload_ReturnNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tpassthroughHooks := []string{\n\t\tHookNamePreToolUse,\n\t\tHookNamePostToolUse,\n\t\tHookNameErrorOccurred,\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, hookName := range passthroughHooks {\n\t\tt.Run(hookName, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\t\t\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\"}`\n\t\t\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), hookName, strings.NewReader(input))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error for %s: %v\", hookName, err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif event != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for pass-through hook %s, got %+v\", hookName, event)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSubagentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SubagentEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SubagentEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession_LifecycleHooksReturnNil verifies that the\n// per-turn/session lifecycle hooks are dropped when Copilot fires them for a\n// subagent turn (sessionId is a Task tool-use id, e.g. \"toolu_…\"). Otherwise a\n// phantom top-level session is created that never ends and pins its shadow\n// branch open after the user commits.\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession_LifecycleHooksReturnNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tconst subagentSessionID = \"REDACTED\"\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\n\tlifecycleHooks := []string{\n\t\tHookNameUserPromptSubmitted,\n\t\tHookNameSessionStart,\n\t\tHookNameAgentStop,\n\t\tHookNameSessionEnd,\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, hookName := range lifecycleHooks {\n\t\tt.Run(hookName, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\t\t\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + subagentSessionID + `\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\t\t\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), hookName, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\t\t\trequire.Nil(t, event, \"expected nil event for subagent-session lifecycle hook %s\", hookName)\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession_SubagentStopStillFires verifies the\n// subagent-stop hook is NOT dropped — it always carries the main session id and\n// drives the task-checkpoint path.\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession_SubagentStopStillFires(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSubagentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"subagent-stop must still produce an event\")\n\trequire.Equal(t, agent.SubagentEnd, event.Type)\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_PassthroughHooks_ReturnNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tpassthroughHooks := []string{\n\t\tHookNamePreToolUse,\n\t\tHookNamePostToolUse,\n\t\tHookNameErrorOccurred,\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, hookName := range passthroughHooks {\n\t\tt.Run(hookName, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\t\t\t// Pass-through hooks should return nil event without reading stdin\n\t\t\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), hookName, strings.NewReader(\"\"))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error for %s: %v\", hookName, err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif event != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for pass-through hook %s, got %+v\", hookName, event)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UnknownHook_ReturnsNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), \"unknown-hook-name\", strings.NewReader(`{\"sessionId\":\"s1\"}`))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif event != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for unknown hook, got %+v\", event)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_EmptyInput_ReturnsError(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t_, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(\"\"))\n\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error for empty input, got nil\")\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"empty hook input\") {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected 'empty hook input' error, got: %v\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_MalformedJSON(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t_, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(`{\"sessionId\": INVALID}`))\n\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error for malformed JSON, got nil\")\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"failed to parse hook input\") {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected 'failed to parse hook input' error, got: %v\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AllHookTypes(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\ttestCases := []struct {\n\t\thookName      string\n\t\texpectedType  agent.EventType\n\t\texpectNil     bool\n\t\tinputTemplate string\n\t}{\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameUserPromptSubmitted,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.TurnStart,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s1\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameSessionStart,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.SessionStart,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s2\",\"source\":\"new\",\"initialPrompt\":\"hi\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameAgentStop,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.TurnEnd,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s3\",\"transcriptPath\":\"/t\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameSessionEnd,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.SessionEnd,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s4\",\"reason\":\"complete\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameSubagentStop,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.SubagentEnd,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s5\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNamePreToolUse,\n\t\t\texpectNil:     true,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNamePostToolUse,\n\t\t\texpectNil:     true,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameErrorOccurred,\n\t\t\texpectNil:     true,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{}`,\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, tc := range testCases {\n\t\tt.Run(tc.hookName, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\n\t\t\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t\t\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), tc.hookName, strings.NewReader(tc.inputTemplate))\n\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tif tc.expectNil {\n\t\t\t\tif event != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event, got %+v\", event)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\t\t\tif event.Type != tc.expectedType {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", tc.expectedType, event.Type)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestHookNames_ReturnsAllHooks(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tnames := ag.HookNames()\n\n\tif len(names) != 8 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"HookNames() returned %d hooks, want 8\", len(names))\n\t}\n\n\texpected := map[string]bool{\n\t\tHookNameUserPromptSubmitted: false,\n\t\tHookNameSessionStart:        false,\n\t\tHookNameAgentStop:           false,\n\t\tHookNameSessionEnd:          false,\n\t\tHookNameSubagentStop:        false,\n\t\tHookNamePreToolUse:          false,\n\t\tHookNamePostToolUse:         false,\n\t\tHookNameErrorOccurred:       false,\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, name := range names {\n\t\tif _, ok := expected[name]; !ok {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"unexpected hook name: %q\", name)\n\t\t}\n\t\texpected[name] = true\n\t}\n\n\tfor name, found := range expected {\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"missing hook name: %q\", name)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:27:type SessionStore struct {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:54:func OpenSessionStore(ag SessionLocator, repoPath string) (*SessionStore, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:68:func OpenSessionStoreAt(ag SessionLocator, dir string) (*SessionStore, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:83:func (s *SessionStore) Dir() string { return s.dir }\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:103:func (s *SessionStore) openRoot() (*os.Root, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:110:func (s *SessionStore) openRootForWrite() (*os.Root, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:125:func (s *SessionStore) SessionFile(agentSessionID string) (name, absPath string, err error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:137:func (s *SessionStore) Name(p string) (string, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:164:func (s *SessionStore) ReadFile(name string) ([]byte, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:176:func (s *SessionStore) WriteFile(name string, data []byte, perm os.FileMode) error {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:198:func (s *SessionStore) Exists(name string) bool {\npackage agent\n\nimport (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/types\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/osroot\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n)\n\n// SessionStore is one agent's own session directory, held as an *os.Root.\n//\n// Every agent keeps its transcripts somewhere Entire does not own —\n// ~/.claude/projects/<hash>/, ~/.codex/sessions/, Cursor's SQLite store,\n// ~/.pi/agent/sessions/<encoded-repo>/, a temp dir for OpenCode — and Entire\n// reads and writes into all of them. The session ID that selects a file inside\n// one comes from an agent hook payload, so this is where an untrusted name\n// becomes a path, and a store gives each agent one handle to resolve it through.\n//\n// It deliberately does NOT try to contain the agent's own writes: the agent is a\n// separate process writing its own store. What it contains is Entire's reads and\n// writes, which is the half Entire is responsible for.\ntype SessionStore struct {\n\tagent SessionLocator\n\tdir   string\n}\n\n// SessionLocator is the slice of Agent a session store needs: where the agent\n// keeps sessions for a repo, and how it names a session's file inside that\n// directory. Narrow on purpose — a store has no business with transcripts,\n// chunking, or hooks, and depending on three methods instead of thirty is what\n// lets a test supply one without implementing the whole agent contract.\ntype SessionLocator interface {\n\tName() types.AgentName\n\tGetSessionDir(repoPath string) (string, error)\n\tResolveSessionFile(sessionDir, agentSessionID string) string\n}\n\n// ErrOutsideSessionStore reports a session file that does not lie inside the\n// agent's session directory. Callers match it with errors.Is.\nvar ErrOutsideSessionStore = errors.New(\"path is outside the agent's session directory\")\n\n// OpenSessionStore returns ag's session store for repoPath.\n//\n// The directory need NOT exist yet: resolving a session file is path arithmetic\n// plus a containment check, and callers legitimately ask where a transcript\n// *would* live before anything has created the directory. Only the I/O methods\n// need the directory, and they open a root at that point and close it again —\n// see openRoot for why a store is not one of the memoized anchors.\nfunc OpenSessionStore(ag SessionLocator, repoPath string) (*SessionStore, error) {\n\tif ag == nil {\n\t\treturn nil, errors.New(\"agent is required to open a session store\")\n\t}\n\tdir, err := ag.GetSessionDir(repoPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"resolve %s session directory: %w\", ag.Name(), err)\n\t}\n\treturn OpenSessionStoreAt(ag, dir)\n}\n\n// OpenSessionStoreAt is OpenSessionStore for a session directory the caller\n// already resolved — the cross-project fallbacks that scan sibling directories,\n// and agentimport, which is handed one.\nfunc OpenSessionStoreAt(ag SessionLocator, dir string) (*SessionStore, error) {\n\tif dir == \"\" {\n\t\treturn nil, errors.New(\"session directory is required\")\n\t}\n\tabs, err := filepath.Abs(dir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"resolve %s: %w\", dir, err)\n\t}\n\treturn &SessionStore{agent: ag, dir: abs}, nil\n}\n\n// Dir returns the store's absolute directory. It is for messages and for the\n// paths Entire hands to other processes (an agent's own resume command, a\n// transcript path recorded as a checkpoint's SessionRef); it is not an\n// invitation to do I/O on the result.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) Dir() string { return s.dir }\n\n// openRoot returns an *os.Root over the store directory. The CALLER closes it.\n//\n// Deliberately not osroot.Shared. That registry is for the handful of long-lived\n// anchors a process holds — .entire, the git common dir, the worktree — and it\n// never evicts, by design. A session store is not one of them: transcript\n// fallback search (searchTranscriptInProjectDirs) opens a store for EVERY\n// candidate directory it walks under ~/.claude/projects, and memoizing those\n// retained one directory fd per candidate for the life of the process. Measured\n// at exactly one fd per directory probed, against zero for the os.Stat this\n// replaced; a few hundred project directories is enough to reach the usual 1024\n// RLIMIT_NOFILE, at which point os.OpenRoot starts failing for every OTHER\n// anchor too, since they all come from the same registry.\n//\n// The cost of not sharing is one openat per store operation, against reading a\n// transcript that is routinely megabytes.\n//\n// A directory that does not exist is reported unwrapped so callers can classify\n// it with os.IsNotExist.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) openRoot() (*os.Root, error) {\n\treturn os.OpenRoot(s.dir) //nolint:wrapcheck // see doc comment\n}\n\n// openRootForWrite is openRoot with the store directory created first. The\n// directory is the root itself, so it cannot be created through it — this is the\n// one place that reaches it from the outside. The caller closes the result.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) openRootForWrite() (*os.Root, error) {\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(s.dir, 0o750); err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create session directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn s.openRoot()\n}\n\n// SessionFile resolves agentSessionID to a name inside the store, and to the\n// absolute path of the same file.\n//\n// This is the check the whole type exists for. The agent decides its own file\n// layout via ResolveSessionFile — some nest, some append an extension — and the\n// ID reaching it came from a hook payload. Converting the result back into a\n// name relative to the store rejects an ID that walked out of the directory,\n// which a plain filepath.Join would have produced silently.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) SessionFile(agentSessionID string) (name, absPath string, err error) {\n\tresolved := s.agent.ResolveSessionFile(s.dir, agentSessionID)\n\tname, err = s.Name(resolved)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", err\n\t}\n\treturn name, resolved, nil\n}\n\n// Name converts a path into a name inside the store, reporting\n// ErrOutsideSessionStore for one that is not. A path already relative to the\n// store is accepted as-is.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) Name(p string) (string, error) {\n\tif p == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: empty path\", ErrOutsideSessionStore)\n\t}\n\t// VolumeName alongside IsAbs, the pairing validation.ValidateSessionID and\n\t// gitrepo's alternates checks already use. A Windows drive-relative path\n\t// like \"C:foo\" contains no separator and IsAbs reports false, so it would\n\t// otherwise be taken as a name inside the store — while filepath.Join drops\n\t// the base directory when the appended element carries a volume. Sending it\n\t// down the absolute branch makes filepath.Rel reject it across volumes,\n\t// which is the answer this containment check exists to give. No-op on Unix,\n\t// where VolumeName is always empty.\n\tif !filepath.IsAbs(p) && filepath.VolumeName(p) == \"\" {\n\t\tcleaned := filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(filepath.FromSlash(p)))\n\t\tif cleaned == \".\" || paths.IsRelativeTraversal(cleaned) {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", ErrOutsideSessionStore, p)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn cleaned, nil\n\t}\n\trel, err := filepath.Rel(s.dir, p)\n\tif err != nil || rel == \".\" || paths.IsRelativeTraversal(rel) {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s is not inside %s\", ErrOutsideSessionStore, p, s.dir)\n\t}\n\treturn filepath.ToSlash(rel), nil\n}\n\n// ReadFile reads name from the store.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) ReadFile(name string) ([]byte, error) {\n\troot, err := s.openRoot()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\tdefer root.Close()\n\treturn osroot.ReadFileNoFollow(root, name) //nolint:wrapcheck // preserved for os.IsNotExist at call sites\n}\n\n// WriteFile writes name in the store, creating parent directories. Session\n// layouts nest (Gemini keys by project hash, Pi by encoded repo path), so the\n// parents are made here rather than at each call site.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) WriteFile(name string, data []byte, perm os.FileMode) error {\n\troot, err := s.openRootForWrite()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdefer root.Close()\n\tif dir := filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Dir(filepath.FromSlash(name))); dir != \".\" {\n\t\tif err := osroot.MkdirAllNoSymlink(root, dir, 0o750); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"create session directory: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif info, err := osroot.LstatNoSymlinks(root, name); err == nil && info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write session file: %w\", osroot.ErrSymlinkedPath)\n\t} else if err != nil && !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"inspect session file: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn(root, name, data, perm) //nolint:wrapcheck // preserved for os.IsNotExist at call sites\n}\n\n// Exists reports whether name is present in the store. Lstat, not Stat: a\n// dangling symlink is still a file that exists and must not be overwritten\n// silently (see the rewind restore path, which distinguishes the two).\nfunc (s *SessionStore) Exists(name string) bool {\n\troot, err := s.openRoot()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tdefer root.Close()\n\t_, err = osroot.LstatNoSymlinks(root, name)\n\treturn err == nil\n}\n\n// WriteSessionFile writes data to s.SessionRef through ag's own session store,\n// creating parent directories.\n//\n// It exists because every agent's WriteSession was the same four lines —\n// os.MkdirAll of the parent, then os.WriteFile of an absolute SessionRef — eight\n// times over, each one taking the path on trust. Routing them through the store\n// makes the containment one decision instead of eight, and the parent-directory\n// create stops being something each agent has to remember.\n//\n// The store is anchored on s.RepoPath when it is set, which is the agent's real\n// session directory for that repo. When it is not (callers that only carry a\n// path, such as a restore driven from checkpoint metadata), the SessionRef's own\n// directory anchors it: that contains nothing by itself, but it keeps the write\n// on the same code path, and SessionRef there came from Entire's own resolution\n// rather than from an agent payload.\nfunc WriteSessionFile(ag SessionLocator, s *AgentSession, data []byte, perm os.FileMode) error {\n\tif s == nil {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"session is nil\")\n\t}\n\tif s.SessionRef == \"\" {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"session reference (transcript path) is required\")\n\t}\n\n\tstore, err := sessionStoreForWrite(ag, s)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tname, err := store.Name(s.SessionRef)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write session: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := store.WriteFile(name, data, perm); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write transcript: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// sessionStoreForWrite resolves the store a session write lands in.\n//\n// With a RepoPath, that is the agent's session directory for it, and a\n// SessionRef outside that directory is an ERROR rather than a reason to anchor\n// somewhere else. It used to fall through to SessionRef's own parent, which made\n// the containment check its own off switch: the one input that fails it was the\n// one input that disabled it. The comment justifying that said some agents\n// resolve a restored session to a sibling directory — they do not.\n// RestoredSessionPathResolver's only implementation (Codex) returns\n// <sessionDir>/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-*.jsonl, which nests INSIDE the store, so the\n// branch was unreachable as well as unsound.\n//\n// Without a RepoPath the SessionRef's own directory is the only candidate there\n// is. That anchor contains nothing by itself, and it is kept because the\n// alternative is refusing to write at all; what makes it acceptable is that\n// SessionRef there came from Entire's own resolution rather than from an agent\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Design\n\n## Goal\n\nGive GitHub Copilot CLI the same normalized subagent lifecycle used by Claude\nCode and Codex: one correctly correlated durable task record per native child,\nincluding child metadata, files, transcript when available, and exact token\nusage when Copilot exposes it.\n\n## Current behavior\n\nEntire's Copilot adapter reflects an older CLI contract:\n\n- it installs `subagentStop` but not `subagentStart`;\n- it discards `preToolUse` and `postToolUse` payloads;\n- it converts `subagentStop` into `SubagentEnd` with only the parent session ID;\n- shared lifecycle code therefore merges all uncorrelated Copilot children into\n  the task record keyed by the empty string; and\n- its subordinate-session guard recognizes only the historical `toolu_` prefix.\n\nThis preserves parent-level file capture but is not per-child tracking.\n\nCurrent Copilot CLI documentation exposes both `subagentStart` and\n`subagentStop` for YAML-based built-in agents and custom agents. The start\npayload contains `sessionId`, `transcriptPath`, and agent metadata but no\n`agentId`; the stop payload adds `agentId`, `agentType`, and the final response.\nThe built-in `general-purpose` agent deliberately emits neither event.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Install, detect, preserve, and remove the native `subagentStart` hook.\n- Parse current camelCase Copilot CLI payloads and compatible snake_case\n  payloads without weakening existing VS Code compatibility checks.\n- Prove and use a collision-free value shared by start and stop as Entire's\n  `ToolUseID`.\n- Map stop `agentId` to `SubagentID` and retain the native child transcript path\n  only when a real current capture proves that `transcriptPath` identifies the\n  child rather than the parent.\n- Reuse the existing `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`, task-record, condensation,\n  sanitization, externalization, redaction, and `tasks/` materialization paths.\n- Preserve phantom-session prevention for historical child lifecycle IDs,\n  including both observed `toolu_` and `tooluse_` spellings.\n- Validate the behavior with simulated hooks, one focused integration test,\n  the existing E2E scenario, and an end-user real Copilot smoke test.\n- Document the `general-purpose` exception truthfully.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Rebuilding shared task-record or checkpoint persistence.\n- Guessing child identity from task descriptions, timestamps, directory order,\n  or \"most recent\" state.\n- Claiming exact per-child tokens when Copilot exposes only a session aggregate.\n- Treating the final response text as a canonical child transcript.\n- Solving `general-purpose` through heuristic attribution. If the evidence\n  phase finds a deterministic native signal, it may be added through the same\n  tests; otherwise it remains an explicit upstream limitation and follow-up.\n- Merging any pull request.\n\n## Design\n\n### Evidence gate\n\nBefore production changes, and only after explicit authorization for a real\nCopilot invocation, run Copilot CLI 1.0.82 or newer in an isolated repository\nwith capture-only hooks. Exercise two same-type native subagents concurrently,\none writing and one read-only, and one `general-purpose` child. Record only\npayload structure, identifiers, event order, transcript locations, and token\nfields. Parallel evidence is mandatory whenever transcript-path identity is a\ncandidate correlation source.\n\nThe native implementation proceeds only if start and stop expose a stable,\none-to-one correlation source. The preferred mapping is the native child ID if\nit is present in both events. Otherwise a canonical child transcript path may\nbe converted to a path-safe deterministic digest, but only after the capture\nproves that path is stable across start/stop and unique across parallel\nchildren. Canonical store-relative layout validation must precede digesting at\nboth boundaries: equivalent spellings of one path map to one identity, while\ndistinct concurrent canonical paths remain distinct. An outside-store,\nwrong-layout, symlinked, missing, or otherwise unvalidated path creates no\nevent or marker. If neither condition holds, stop and revise the design rather\nthan ship ambiguous attribution.\n\nThe same capture must prove the ordering of child start/stop relative to parent\n`agentStop` and `sessionEnd`, when child transcript bytes become readable, and\nwhether the child transcript survives until condensation. If parent session\ntermination can precede native child stop, stop and revise the lifecycle design:\nthe current SessionEnd sweep would otherwise complete and condense a live marker\nwithout the stop's child metadata.\n\nIf transcript path is the correlation source, the capture must additionally\nshow that the canonical non-symlink child file is present and verifiable at\nboth start and stop. If child file attribution depends on transcript bytes, the\nfile must be readable at stop; otherwise the implementation pauses for a design\nthat can safely defer attribution instead of silently producing incomplete\nrecords.\n\n### Hook adapter\n\nAdd `subagent-start` beside the existing Copilot hook verbs and include the\n`subagentStart` key in installation, uninstall, idempotency, and presence/drift\ncoverage. Copilot gains a read-only `CheckHookConfig`: absent/user-only files are\nabsent, the exact managed set is current, and any managed-but-incomplete,\nstale, malformed, or unreadable configuration is outdated. Extend the\ncompatibility envelope only with fields required by the documented subagent\npayloads.\n\n`subagentStart` maps to `agent.SubagentStart` with:\n\n- the parent Copilot session as `SessionID`;\n- the proven stable correlation value as `ToolUseID`;\n- native agent name/type and description when present; and\n- the canonical child transcript as `SubagentTranscriptPath` only after\n  store-confined, no-follow validation.\n\n`subagentStop` maps to `agent.SubagentEnd` with the same `ToolUseID`, stop\n`agentId` as `SubagentID`, the parent transcript as `SessionRef`, native labels,\nand the verified child transcript path. It remains `Final: false` because\nCopilot supplies one true-completion end signal rather than Claude Code's\nlaunch-stub-plus-final pair. A narrow normalized-event marker distinguishes\nthis native start/stop lifecycle from the existing foreground PostToolUse\ncompletion path. The same marker declares that any supplied child transcript\npath is authoritative: Copilot records never probe the generic Claude-style\nsubagent layout when that path is absent, disappears, or cannot be read.\n\n### Durable capture\n\nNo new storage model is introduced. For the marked native lifecycle, generic\nstart handling adds a live `session.TaskRecord` only to an existing parent\nsession. Generic end handling requires that live record, uses only hook- or\nchild-transcript-authoritative file evidence, bypasses the no-file skip for a\nread-only child, and completes it exactly once. An unmatched, duplicate, or\nmissing/ended-parent stop is a no-op and never creates or resurrects state.\nThis path is separate from the existing Final=false foreground PostToolUse\npath, whose whole-worktree scan is unsafe for concurrent children.\n\nThe task record persists an explicit authoritative-transcript/no-fallback bit.\nCompletion merges start and stop metadata field-by-field: stop values win when\npresent, while an omitted stop field retains the start value. This includes\n`SubagentType`, `TaskDescription`, `AgentID`, the declared transcript, and its\nprovenance. Consequently, a start that lacks a description can still retain a\ndescription supplied by stop, without erasing a name learned at start.\nThe verified start transcript path is stored on the live record immediately,\nsurvives a JSON state round trip, remains when stop omits it, and is replaced\nonly by a non-empty verified stop path.\n\nCondensation writes\n`tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` and, when available,\n`agent-<agent-id>.jsonl`. Missing child transcripts retain a metadata record\nwith an existing path-free unavailability reason. For an authoritative Copilot\nrecord, a missing or unreadable declared path never falls through to either\n`ResolveAgentTranscriptPath` during completion or\n`resolveTaskTranscriptPath` during condensation, even if a coincidental file\nexists at the generic layout.\n\nConfinement applies to every read, not just initial hook parsing. The Copilot\nadapter performs one `SessionStore`-anchored, no-follow read at stop and derives\nboth `Event.ModifiedFiles` and exact usage from those bytes, so shared lifecycle\ncode does not reopen the path through `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset`.\nCondensation independently revalidates and reopens an authoritative path\nthrough `SessionStore.ReadFile`; it never sends that path to unrestricted\n`ReadTranscriptFile`/`readFirstTranscript`. A file replaced by a symlink after\nparsing or immediately before condensation therefore yields transcript\nunavailability rather than reading outside the store.\n\nExact child token usage is stored only if a canonical child transcript or\nmachine-readable per-agent usage record supplies an exact total. The Copilot\nadapter accepts usage only when the verified child transcript already contains\nthe authoritative `session.shutdown` aggregate with non-empty `modelMetrics`.\nIt uses an exact-only extractor rather than the existing calculator's partial\nassistant-message fallback, and places the result on `Event.TokenUsage` before\ndispatch. The hook path is accepted only when it resolves to the captured\ncanonical file layout beneath Copilot's session store; outside-store paths,\nsymlinks, and layout mismatches yield neither a declared child transcript nor\nchild usage. Otherwise the record's child token usage remains unavailable;\nparent session totals continue through the existing Copilot calculator and are\nnot replaced or double-counted by partial child data.\n\n### General-purpose behavior\n\nThe probe must confirm the documented absence of native start/stop hooks. The\nexisting subordinate lifecycle filter remains in place so a child cannot open\na phantom top-level Entire session. Supporting `general-purpose` requires a\nstable parent/child/call relationship under parallel execution; descriptions\nand recency are expressly insufficient.\n\nIf current Copilot re-emits a deterministic child task ID and canonical child\nsession evidence, add a narrowly scoped adapter using that identity. Otherwise\nthe PR documents the exception and does not imply parity for that built-in.\n\n## Error handling and privacy\n\n- Malformed subagent payloads return ordinary parse errors and never create a\n  partial task record.\n- Missing optional metadata degrades field-by-field.\n- Invalid or ambiguous correlation fails closed for per-child capture while\n  preserving parent-session checkpoint behavior.\n- A native stop after parent SessionEnd is skipped unless the evidence phase\n  proves and the design explicitly handles a safe retained-state ordering.\n- Logs contain identifiers, key names, counts, and paths already permitted by\n  current operational logging; never prompts, responses, or transcript text.\n- Hook output remains empty/pass-through so Entire cannot block Copilot work.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Fresh installation includes exactly one managed `subagentStart` and one\n  managed `subagentStop`; upgrade, reinstall, and uninstall are idempotent and\n  preserve user hooks and unknown fields.\n- Two native children with the same agent type receive different stable task\n  IDs and cannot complete each other's records.\n- A writing child contributes its file and native child transcript to its own\n  durable `tasks/` subtree after a normal user commit.\n- A read-only child still produces its own durable metadata/transcript record.\n- Duplicate stop delivery does not duplicate or overwrite another child.\n- Unmatched stops and stops after missing/ended parent state create nothing.\n- Metadata present only at stop is merged into the start-created record.\n- Missing authoritative child transcripts never fall back to a generic\n  agent-layout file.\n- Partial message-only usage, unsafe paths, and symlinks (including paths\n  replaced by symlinks after parsing) never become child transcript, child-file,\n  or exact child-token evidence.\n- Historical subordinate session IDs do not create phantom sessions.\n- Parent checkpoint behavior, VS Code compatibility, and non-subagent Copilot\n  lifecycle behavior remain unchanged.\n- The real E2E repository provisions and commits a named\n  `.github/agents/entire-e2e-subagent.agent.md` fixture before hook installation\n  and before `HeadBefore`/`CheckpointBefore` are captured, then explicitly asks\n  for that agent; prompt inference is not accepted as proof that a hook-emitting\n  child ran.\n- Focused tests, `mise run check`, the Copilot E2E subagent flow, and a real\n  current-Copilot smoke test pass before push.\n\n## Size target\n\nTarget 450-700 additions and 50-100 deletions, including tests and docs. Reuse\nexisting tables and integration helpers. If the implementation exceeds roughly\n800 additions, pause and revisit the adapter boundary before continuing.\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Implementation Plan\n\n> **Execution constraint:** Implement this plan sequentially in the primary session. Do not launch implementation subagents. Follow the red/green checkpoints task-by-task; checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax records progress.\n\n**Goal:** Track each hook-emitting Copilot CLI subagent as its own durable Entire task with correct identity, files, transcript availability, and exact token usage when natively available.\n\n**Architecture:** Upgrade the Copilot adapter to consume native `subagentStart` and the complete `subagentStop` payload, then feed those events into a narrow marker-backed path in Entire's existing task-record lifecycle. A real-current-Copilot evidence gate must prove collision-free correlation, event ordering, and transcript availability before production mapping is chosen; ambiguous `general-purpose` behavior stays fail-closed rather than heuristic.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, Cobra hook commands, Copilot CLI JSON hooks/JSONL sessions, testify, Entire integration harness, mise.\n\n**Design:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md`\n\n---\n\n### Task 0: Refresh the clean feature branch\n\n**Files:** None\n\n- [ ] Confirm `git status --short` has no tracked changes and record `git rev-parse HEAD` plus `git rev-parse origin/main`.\n- [ ] Run `git fetch origin main`. If this feature branch still has no unique commits, fast-forward it with `git merge --ff-only origin/main`; if it has diverged, stop and inspect rather than rewriting history.\n- [ ] Re-run the relevant Copilot adapter tests on the refreshed base before starting the evidence capture.\n\n### Task 1: Capture the current Copilot subagent contract\n\n**Files:**\n- Use: `/tmp` disposable repository and capture directory only\n- Reference: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md`\n- Reference: historical `scripts/test-copilot-cli-agent-integration.sh`\n\n- [ ] Obtain explicit user authorization for the real Copilot invocations in this task; do not treat plan approval as paid-E2E approval.\n- [ ] Record the candidate and installed Copilot versions; use an isolated official Copilot CLI 1.0.82-or-newer binary without replacing the user's installed binary.\n- [ ] Create a disposable git repository with isolated Entire config/cache/token-store paths. Keep Copilot authentication available without modifying the user's Copilot configuration; if an isolated `COPILOT_HOME` cannot authenticate, stop rather than copy credentials into artifacts.\n- [ ] Register capture-only `subagentStart`, `subagentStop`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `agentStop`, `sessionEnd`, and subordinate session lifecycle hooks; restrict tool hooks to the task tool when matchers support it.\n- [ ] Provision and commit `.github/agents/entire-evidence-subagent.agent.md` with a lowercase stable name, required `description`, and minimal instructions. Create it before the measured session so it is not attributed to a child.\n- [ ] Run two same-type native children concurrently: one creates a distinctive file and one is read-only. Concurrency is mandatory if transcript path is considered as correlation evidence.\n- [ ] Run one built-in `general-purpose` child to confirm the documented hook exception and observe subordinate lifecycle/event evidence.\n- [ ] Capture only hook names, payload key names/types, IDs, timestamps, event ordering, transcript paths, transcript event types, file existence/identity, and usage field structure; do not preserve prompts, responses, file contents, credentials, or tokens.\n- [ ] Prove start/stop order relative to parent `agentStop` and `sessionEnd`, when child transcript bytes become readable, and whether they remain readable through normal commit-time condensation.\n- [ ] Prove whether `transcriptPath` is parent or child, stable across start/stop, and unique across the concurrent same-type children.\n- [ ] Select the correlation mapping and record it in `AGENT.md` before production code:\n  - native child ID present at both boundaries: use it directly for `ToolUseID`;\n  - stable unique child transcript path at both boundaries: use a deterministic path-safe digest and retain stop `agentId` as `SubagentID`;\n  - no one-to-one invariant: stop and revise the design; never match by description, timestamp proximity, or latest state.\n- [ ] If parent `sessionEnd` can precede native child stop, stop and revise the lifecycle design before Task 4; the current SessionEnd sweep cannot safely synthesize missing stop metadata.\n- [ ] Determine whether a canonical child transcript or exact per-agent machine-readable usage persists without requiring Entire to launch Copilot with special flags.\n- [ ] Remove the disposable repository and retain only a credential-free structural report outside the product diff.\n\n### Task 2: Install, preserve, and diagnose `subagentStart`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/types.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend existing hook-name/install table tests to expect `subagent-start`; run them red because only eight hooks are installed.\n- [ ] Add upgrade coverage proving a pre-feature `entire.json` remains recognized as installed while reinstall adds exactly the missing managed hook and preserves user entries/unknown fields.\n- [ ] Add `CheckHookConfig` tests for absent and user-only files (`HooksAbsent`), exact current configuration (`HooksCurrent`), missing `subagentStart`, stale managed commands, malformed JSON, and unreadable files (`HooksOutdated` once any managed ownership is present or currentness cannot be proven).\n- [ ] Run the new upgrade/freshness tests red.\n- [ ] Add `HookNameSubagentStart`, the `subagentStart` config key/field, and the managed hook entry through the existing install/uninstall loops.\n- [ ] Implement read-only `agent.HookFreshness` behavior without changing `AreHooksInstalled`'s ownership/presence semantics.\n- [ ] Include native and compatible `SubagentStart` in event validation without weakening VS Code mismatch rejection.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestInstallHooks|TestUninstallHooks|TestHookNames|TestCheckHookConfig' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 3: Parse complete native subagent payloads\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add one table-driven test covering captured camelCase start/stop and compatible snake_case start/stop, asserting session, stable correlation, child ID, labels, and transcript roles.\n- [ ] Add only distinct failure contracts: missing/ambiguous correlation, nullable transcript, and mismatched compatible event name.\n- [ ] Run the new tests red and confirm failures come from discarded fields/missing start handling.\n- [ ] Extend `hookEnvelope` with only captured/documented fields required for normalized events (`agentId`, agent type/name/display/description, and the proven correlation input).\n- [ ] Implement one correlation helper from Task 1's proven invariant and validate its result through existing tool-use ID rules. If identity is path-derived, first normalize and validate the path as the exact canonical store-relative child layout at both start and stop, then digest that canonical name—never the raw hook string.\n- [ ] Add path-derived correlation tests proving equivalent absolute/relative/cleaned spellings map identically, distinct same-type concurrent child paths remain distinct, and outside-store, wrong-layout, missing, or symlinked paths return no normalized event and create no marker.\n- [ ] Map start to `agent.SubagentStart` and stop to `agent.SubagentEnd` with identical `ToolUseID`; map stop `agentId` to `SubagentID`.\n- [ ] Keep Copilot stop `Final: false`; it is a single true-completion end event, not Claude Code's launch-stub-plus-later-final pair.\n- [ ] Set `SessionRef` and `SubagentTranscriptPath` according to captured parent/child path roles; never treat response text as a canonical transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent|TestParseHookEnvelope' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 4: Add marker-backed native lifecycle completion\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/event.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_git.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add failing lifecycle tests named `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentStart_MarkerBackedRegistersLiveRecord`, `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentEnd_MarkerBackedReadOnlyCompletes`, `...ConcurrentReverseStopsStayDisjoint`, `...DuplicateStopIsNoOp`, `...UnmatchedStopIsNoOp`, and `...MissingOrEndedParentIsNoOp`.\n- [ ] In the concurrent test, use two same-type tasks, reverse completion order, distinct child transcripts/files, and assert neither record receives the other's evidence.\n- [ ] Add a red metadata-merge test where start supplies the type but omits the description, stop supplies the description and agent ID, and the completed record retains all three. Stop values win when non-empty; each missing stop field falls back independently to start.\n- [ ] Add a red authoritative-path test where the declared child path disappears before condensation while a coincidental generic-layout `agent-<id>.jsonl` exists; assert the payload records transcript unavailability and never stores the generic file.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1` and verify the tests fail against the existing foreground path.\n- [ ] Add one narrowly named normalized-event marker for native start/stop lifecycles whose completion must claim a start-created record. Set it only on Copilot's proven native events.\n- [ ] Add `TaskRecord.DeclaredTranscriptAuthoritative` (name may be adjusted for clarity) so the no-fallback contract survives state persistence. Mark every native Copilot task authoritative even when its verified declared path is empty.\n- [ ] On marked start, mutate only an existing active parent state and add a live `TaskRecord` containing the proven `ToolUseID`, labels, start time, verified start `DeclaredTranscriptPath`, and authoritative-transcript bit; do not call `EnsureSessionExists` and do not resurrect ended state. Capture pre-task state only as best-effort fallback, not authoritative parallel file evidence.\n- [ ] Add a state JSON round-trip test proving the verified start path and authoritative bit survive serialization. Add lifecycle tests proving a stop without a path retains the start path and a non-empty verified stop path replaces it.\n- [ ] On marked Final=false end, require the matching live record, reject missing/ended parent state, first fill only the stop event's empty metadata fields from start, and complete exactly once. This makes every non-empty stop value authoritative without losing start-only fields.\n- [ ] Extend `strategy.applyTaskRecordCompletion` to write each non-empty merged completion value (`SubagentType`, `TaskDescription`, `AgentID`, and declared path) onto the live record, plus token usage and the authoritative bit. Keep the existing behavior for unmarked producers whose completion fields are empty.\n- [ ] Reuse/refactor existing completion machinery with `bypassNoChangesSkip: true`, an event-files-only option, and a no-layout-fallback option derived from the marker. For marked Copilot completion, accept only adapter-populated `Event.ModifiedFiles`; do not run the path-based `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset` analyzer or a whole-worktree scan.\n- [ ] In `completeSubagentTaskRecord`, do not call `ResolveAgentTranscriptPath` or reopen the transcript for marked authoritative events. In `materializeTaskRecords`, when the persisted authoritative bit is set, try only `DeclaredTranscriptPath`; if it is empty, missing, or unreadable, emit the existing path-free unavailability reason and do not call `resolveTaskTranscriptPath`.\n- [ ] Add a narrow authoritative-task reader in condensation that opens the agent's store with `agent.OpenSessionStore(ag, state.WorktreePath)`, converts the declared path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the captured Copilot layout, and reads with `SessionStore.ReadFile` (no-follow). Never pass authoritative paths to `readFirstTranscript` or unrestricted `agent.ReadTranscriptFile`.\n- [ ] Add race-regression tests that replace the child file with a symlink after parse/before dispatch and again immediately before condensation. Dispatch may retain files/usage already derived from the safely read original bytes, but it must perform no second read and must not attribute data found only in the symlink target; condensation stores the existing path-free transcript-unavailable reason and never the target bytes.\n- [ ] Keep existing unmarked foreground PostToolUse behavior and existing Final=true background behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`, `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test.*TaskRecord.*(Metadata|Authoritative|Fallback)' -count=1`, and `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_Subagent' -count=1`; make all green.\n\n### Task 5: Preserve subordinate-session safety\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend the existing phantom-session characterization test with both observed historical prefixes, `toolu_` and `tooluse_`, plus a real UUID parent session.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession' -count=1` and verify `tooluse_` fails.\n- [ ] Replace the single-prefix assumption with the narrowest predicate justified by captured current and historical evidence; do not classify arbitrary non-UUID user input as a child unless Copilot guarantees parent IDs are UUIDs.\n- [ ] Verify subordinate session lifecycle hooks remain suppressed while native parent-scoped subagent hooks still produce normalized events.\n- [ ] Re-run the exact focused command and make it green.\n\n### Task 6: Wire exact child files and usage without guessing\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify if evidence supports a canonical child file: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] If Task 1 proves a canonical child JSONL file, add a fixture proving the existing analyzer extracts only that child's files and an exact full-child token total only when that child file contains an authoritative `session.shutdown` record with non-empty `modelMetrics`.\n- [ ] Add an exact-only helper returning `(usage, exact)` (or equivalent) that never invokes the existing assistant-message fallback. Keep the public parent/session `TokenCalculator` behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Add `TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_ExactChildUsage` and `...PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil`, including assertions that parent/session aggregate fields are not copied into the child record and a child transcript containing only `assistant.message.outputTokens` yields nil usage.\n- [ ] Add path-confinement tests for a declared path outside Copilot's session store, a symlink inside the store, and a syntactically plausible but wrong-layout file. Each must yield nil child usage and an empty declared child transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_(ExactChildUsage|PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil)|Test.*ChildTranscript' -count=1` red.\n- [ ] Add one Copilot helper that canonicalizes the hook path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the exact captured `<session-store>/<child-session>/events.jsonl` layout, and reads it with `SessionStore.ReadFile`. The rooted no-follow read rejects symlinks and later replacements; do not call unrestricted `os.ReadFile` on hook input.\n- [ ] From that one safely read byte slice, populate `Event.ModifiedFiles` through the existing Copilot JSONL parsing helpers and set `Event.TokenUsage` only when the authoritative completion aggregate is present. A readable transcript with only fallback message tokens is not exact and leaves usage nil.\n- [ ] If per-agent usage exists only in a requested `--usage-output-file`, do not depend on it because Entire does not launch the user's Copilot process.\n- [ ] If no canonical child transcript exists, retain metadata with the existing unavailable reason, leave child usage nil, and do not reconstruct a transcript from response text.\n- [ ] Run the same focused command green.\n\n### Task 7: Prove durable per-child capture through simulated hooks\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/copilot_subagent_test.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/testenv.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n\n- [ ] Write one integration test that initializes an isolated repo, starts a Copilot parent session, sends two captured-shape native starts with the same agent type, creates one child transcript per native contract, and sends stops in reverse order.\n- [ ] Commit one child-owned file through normal prepare-commit-msg/post-commit hooks and assert two distinct `tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` records in the permanent checkpoint.\n- [ ] Assert each record retains its own `agent_id`, labels, disjoint file list, completion state, exact usage when the child fixture includes an authoritative aggregate, and child transcript or the existing path-free unavailability reason.\n- [ ] Include one read-only child in the same fixture and assert it remains a distinct durable record.\n- [ ] Include duplicate stop, unmatched stop, and post-ended-session stop in the same lifecycle setup only where assertions remain readable; otherwise rely on Task 4's direct tests rather than duplicating them.\n- [ ] Treat this as a green end-to-end characterization after Tasks 2-6, not as a false red TDD step. Tasks 4 and 6 supply the focused red/green proof for shared lifecycle and exact child evidence.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1` and make it green.\n- [ ] Make only adapter-level or narrowly necessary shared changes if the characterization exposes a gap; do not duplicate materialization or add Copilot-specific checkpoint storage.\n\n### Task 8: Pin `general-purpose` and update documentation\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify only if Task 1 proves deterministic fallback evidence: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n\n- [ ] Add a fixture matching Task 1's `general-purpose` evidence and verify it cannot create a phantom top-level session.\n- [ ] If capture exposes a stable parent session, globally unique task ID, true completion, and canonical child evidence, first add a failing parallel same-type correlation test, then implement the narrow fallback.\n- [ ] If any invariant is absent, keep fallback out of production and document the upstream exception and capability boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] Remove stale claims that Copilot has no `subagentStart`; document current payload roles, minimum verified version, native-agent coverage, correlation invariant, ordering, transcript availability, and historical subordinate-session behavior.\n- [ ] Update the agent guide's Copilot event matrix so it matches installed native start/stop behavior.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession|TestParseHookEvent_GeneralPurpose|TestHookNames' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 9: Strengthen the existing E2E scenario without duplicating it\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go`\n- Modify: `e2e/testutil/repo.go`\n- Reuse: `e2e/testutil` checkpoint readers\n\n- [ ] Add a small Copilot fixture helper in `e2e/testutil/repo.go` that writes both `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `.github/agents/entire-e2e-subagent.agent.md`, then commits them before `entire.Enable`, hook installation, and construction of `RepoState` (`HeadBefore`/`CheckpointBefore`). Its agent frontmatter uses `name: entire-e2e-subagent`, a required description, and minimal file-writing instructions.\n- [ ] For `s.Agent.Name() == \"copilot-cli\"`, explicitly prompt the parent to delegate to `entire-e2e-subagent`; do not rely on inference or the built-in `general-purpose` agent.\n- [ ] Keep existing cross-agent file/checkpoint assertions. Add Copilot-specific committed `tasks/` assertions keyed by the discovered single task directory: one task, expected child-created file, non-empty safe `agent_id`, and transcript presence/unavailability matching Task 1's proven contract.\n- [ ] Ensure the committed custom-agent fixture predates capture and is absent from child `files` attribution.\n- [ ] Assert `HeadBefore` already includes the fixture commit and the fixture commit did not advance `CheckpointBefore`; this protects the measured checkpoint baseline from setup contamination.\n- [ ] Update Vogon's prompt parsing only if the minimally changed Copilot wording breaks the existing canary.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow` and make it green.\n- [ ] Do not add a second Copilot-only E2E scenario unless the shared test cannot express a required assertion.\n\n### Task 10: Verify size, correctness, and real end-user behavior\n\n**Files:** All modified files plus a disposable smoke-test repository.\n\n- [ ] Run `mise run fmt` and inspect every rewrite.\n- [ ] Run `mise run lint` after the final format pass.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` against the complete working tree and remove accidental duplication rather than suppressing it.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check`.\n- [ ] Run `git diff --check` and compare production/test additions with the 450-700 line target; pause for redesign if additions exceed roughly 800.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit authorization for each real Copilot validation phase, including the E2E invocation and separate smoke; plan approval alone is insufficient.\n- [ ] With authorization, run `mise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli TestSubagentCommitFlow` using a current Copilot binary.\n- [ ] Before the separate smoke, build a wrapper-free candidate `entire` into a dedicated temporary bin directory with a unique `versioninfo.Version` stamp containing the source commit/dirty marker. Record its SHA-256, construct a fixed `PATH` with that bin directory first, and use `whence -a entire` (or platform equivalent) to prove no other reachable `entire` precedes or shadows it. Record `command -v entire`, `entire version`, and the installed hook command before launch; stop on any mismatch.\n- [ ] In a separate disposable end-user repository, set isolated `COPILOT_HOME`, `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`; pass authentication only through already-present supported environment variables. Do not copy credential files or the user's Copilot/GitHub config, and stop if isolated authentication cannot be supplied.\n- [ ] With that isolated environment, enable Copilot hooks, provision and commit the named custom agent before capture, run a real child that creates a distinctive file, and commit normally. Tie the resulting hook log session ID to the checkpoint, then assert the checkpoint metadata's `cli_version` equals the unique candidate stamp; this proves the task artifact came from that binary without adding runtime logging. Inspect for exactly one correlated child task, exact child evidence when available, and no phantom session/shadow branch.\n- [ ] Preserve only a credential-free structural smoke report and remove disposable artifacts.\n- [ ] Commit only after required local gates pass; push only when authorized, then follow all repository/PR gates to terminal status without merging.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"package copilotcli\n\n// CopilotHooksFile represents the .github/hooks/entire.json structure.\n// Copilot CLI uses a flat JSON file with version and hooks sections.\n// All JSON files in .github/hooks/ are auto-discovered by the Copilot CLI.\n//\n\ntype CopilotHooksFile struct {\n\tVersion int          `json:\"version\"`\n\tHooks   CopilotHooks `json:\"hooks\"`\n}\n\n// CopilotHooks contains all hook configurations using camelCase keys.\n//\n\ntype CopilotHooks struct {\n\tUserPromptSubmitted []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"userPromptSubmitted,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionStart        []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"sessionStart,omitempty\"`\n\tAgentStop           []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"agentStop,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionEnd          []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"sessionEnd,omitempty\"`\n\tSubagentStop        []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"subagentStop,omitempty\"`\n\tPreToolUse          []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"preToolUse,omitempty\"`\n\tPostToolUse         []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"postToolUse,omitempty\"`\n\tErrorOccurred       []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"errorOccurred,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// CopilotHookEntry represents a single hook command.\n// Copilot CLI hooks have a type field (\"command\") and a bash field for the command string.\n// Optional fields (cwd, timeoutSec, env, comment) are preserved on round-trip.\n\ntype CopilotHookEntry struct {\n\tType       string            `json:\"type\"`\n\tBash       string            `json:\"bash\"`\n\tComment    string            `json:\"comment,omitempty\"`\n\tCwd        string            `json:\"cwd,omitempty\"`\n\tTimeoutSec int               `json:\"timeoutSec,omitempty\"`\n\tEnv        map[string]string `json:\"env,omitempty\"`\n}\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n)\n\n// HooksFileName is the hooks file managed by Entire for Copilot CLI.\nconst HooksFileName = \"entire.json\"\n\n// hooksDir is the directory within the repo where Copilot CLI looks for hook configs.\nconst hooksDir = \".github/hooks\"\n\n// hookConfigKey maps our kebab-case hook names to camelCase JSON keys.\nvar hookConfigKey = map[string]string{\n\tHookNameUserPromptSubmitted: \"userPromptSubmitted\",\n\tHookNameSessionStart:        \"sessionStart\",\n\tHookNameAgentStop:           \"agentStop\",\n\tHookNameSessionEnd:          \"sessionEnd\",\n\tHookNameSubagentStop:        \"subagentStop\",\n\tHookNamePreToolUse:          \"preToolUse\",\n\tHookNamePostToolUse:         \"postToolUse\",\n\tHookNameErrorOccurred:       \"errorOccurred\",\n}\n\n// copilotHookConfig returns .github/hooks/entire.json for the current worktree,\n// opened through the worktree's root. That directory lives in the working tree,\n// which arrives by clone, so a checked-in symlink at `.github` or\n// `.github/hooks` must not be something Entire creates directories under and\n// writes through. See agent.HookConfigFile.\nfunc copilotHookConfig(ctx context.Context) (*agent.HookConfigFile, error) {\n\tworktreeRoot, err := paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\t// Not a repository (tests, and `enable` before `git init`): the process\n\t\t// directory is the only candidate, and it is a directory the caller\n\t\t// chose rather than one derived from anything read off disk.\n\t\tworktreeRoot = \".\"\n\t}\n\treturn agent.OpenHookConfig(worktreeRoot, (&CopilotCLIAgent{}).HookConfigRelPath()) //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n}\n\n// InstallHooks installs Copilot CLI hooks in .github/hooks/entire.json.\n// If force is true, removes existing Entire hooks before installing.\n// Returns the number of hooks installed.\n// Unknown top-level fields and hook types are preserved on round-trip.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) InstallHooks(ctx context.Context, force bool) (int, error) {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\n\t// Use raw maps to preserve unknown fields on round-trip\n\tvar rawFile map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tvar rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage\n\n\texistingData, readErr := cfg.Read()\n\tswitch {\n\tcase readErr == nil:\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(existingData, &rawFile); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse existing %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif hooksRaw, ok := rawFile[\"hooks\"]; ok {\n\t\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(hooksRaw, &rawHooks); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse hooks in %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, ok := rawFile[\"version\"]; !ok {\n\t\t\trawFile[\"version\"] = json.RawMessage(`1`)\n\t\t}\n\tcase errors.Is(readErr, os.ErrNotExist):\n\t\trawFile = map[string]json.RawMessage{\n\t\t\t\"version\": json.RawMessage(`1`),\n\t\t}\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read %s: %w\", HooksFileName, readErr)\n\t}\n\n\tif rawHooks == nil {\n\t\trawHooks = make(map[string]json.RawMessage)\n\t}\n\n\t// Parse existing entries for each hook type we manage\n\thookEntries := make(map[string][]CopilotHookEntry)\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tvar entries []CopilotHookEntry\n\t\tif err := parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, &entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\thookEntries[hookName] = entries\n\t}\n\n\t// If force, remove existing Entire hooks first\n\tif force {\n\t\tfor hookName, entries := range hookEntries {\n\t\t\thookEntries[hookName] = removeEntireHooks(entries)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Define command prefix\n\tconst cmdPrefix = \"entire hooks copilot-cli \"\n\n\tcount := 0\n\n\t// Sync each hook to its desired command. Entire-owned entries carrying any\n\t// other command are dropped first, even without --force: a hook written by\n\t// an older version would otherwise survive alongside the one added below and\n\t// keep firing, which for the removed local-dev mode means a script inside\n\t// the working tree still runs on every agent turn.\n\tstaleDropped := false\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tcmd := agent.WrapProductionSilentHookCommand(cmdPrefix + hookName)\n\t\tentries := hookEntries[hookName]\n\n\t\t// Keep the matching entry rather than remove-and-re-add: entry-level\n\t\t// fields (cwd, timeoutSec, env) live on the existing entry and a freshly\n\t\t// constructed one would discard them.\n\t\tkept, dropped := agent.DropStaleManagedHooks(entries, hookEntryBash, []string{cmd})\n\t\tif dropped {\n\t\t\tstaleDropped = true\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries = kept\n\n\t\tif !hookBashExists(entries, cmd) {\n\t\t\tentries = append(entries, CopilotHookEntry{\n\t\t\t\tType:    \"command\",\n\t\t\t\tBash:    cmd,\n\t\t\t\tComment: \"Entire CLI\",\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t\tcount++\n\t\t}\n\t\thookEntries[hookName] = entries\n\t}\n\n\t// staleDropped forces a write even when nothing was added: a file holding\n\t// both a stale and a current hook adds nothing, and returning early here\n\t// would leave the stale hook on disk.\n\tif count == 0 && !staleDropped {\n\t\treturn 0, nil\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal modified hook types back into rawHooks\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tif err := marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, hookEntries[hookName]); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal hooks and update raw file\n\thooksJSON, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(rawHooks)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hooks: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\trawFile[\"hooks\"] = hooksJSON\n\n\t// Write to file\n\toutput, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(rawFile, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tif err := cfg.Write(output, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n\t}\n\n\treturn count, nil\n}\n\n// UninstallHooks removes Entire hooks from Copilot CLI's entire.json.\n// Unknown top-level fields and hook types are preserved on round-trip.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) UninstallHooks(ctx context.Context) error {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := cfg.Read()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treturn nil // No hooks file means nothing to uninstall\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar rawFile map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &rawFile); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tif hooksRaw, ok := rawFile[\"hooks\"]; ok {\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(hooksRaw, &rawHooks); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse hooks in %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif rawHooks == nil {\n\t\trawHooks = make(map[string]json.RawMessage)\n\t}\n\n\t// Parse and remove Entire hooks from each hook type we manage\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tvar entries []CopilotHookEntry\n\t\tif err := parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, &entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries = removeEntireHooks(entries)\n\t\tif err := marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal hooks back (preserving unknown hook types)\n\tif len(rawHooks) > 0 {\n\t\thooksJSON, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(rawHooks)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hooks: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\trawFile[\"hooks\"] = hooksJSON\n\t} else {\n\t\tdelete(rawFile, \"hooks\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Write back\n\toutput, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(rawFile, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tif err := cfg.Write(output, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// AreHooksInstalled checks if Entire hooks are installed in the Copilot CLI\n// config.\n//\n// A missing config file is an answer — no hooks — while an unreadable or\n// malformed one is an error: \"we could not tell\" and \"there are none\" are\n// different things to a caller deciding whether hooks can be left alone.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) AreHooksInstalled(ctx context.Context) (bool, error) {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn false, err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := cfg.Read()\n\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn false, nil\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"copilot-cli: failed to read hooks file\", \"path\", cfg.Path(), \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %w\", cfg.Path(), err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar hooksFile CopilotHooksFile\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &hooksFile); err != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"copilot-cli: failed to parse hooks file\", \"path\", cfg.Path(), \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"parse %s: %w\", cfg.Path(), err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn hasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.UserPromptSubmitted) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SessionStart) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.AgentStop) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SessionEnd) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SubagentStop) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.PreToolUse) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.PostToolUse) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.ErrorOccurred), nil\n}\n\n// GetSupportedHooks returns the normalized lifecycle events this agent supports.\n// Note: HookNames() returns 8 hooks but GetSupportedHooks() returns only 6.\n// The two not listed here are:\n//   - subagentStop: handled by ParseHookEvent (returns SubagentEnd), but there is no\n//     HookType constant for subagent events (they use EventType instead).\n//   - errorOccurred: pass-through hook with no lifecycle action (ParseHookEvent returns nil).\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) GetSupportedHooks() []agent.HookType {\n\treturn []agent.HookType{\n\t\tagent.HookSessionStart,\n\t\tagent.HookSessionEnd,\n\t\tagent.HookUserPromptSubmit,\n\t\tagent.HookStop,\n\t\tagent.HookPreToolUse,\n\t\tagent.HookPostToolUse,\n\t}\n}\n\n// parseCopilotHookType parses a specific hook type from rawHooks into the target slice.\nfunc parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage, hookType string, target *[]CopilotHookEntry) error {\n\tif data, ok := rawHooks[hookType]; ok {\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, target); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid JSON for hook type %s: %w\", hookType, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// marshalCopilotHookType marshals a hook type back into rawHooks.\n// If the slice is empty, removes the key from rawHooks.\nfunc marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage, hookType string, entries []CopilotHookEntry) error {\n\tif len(entries) == 0 {\n\t\tdelete(rawHooks, hookType)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tdata, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(entries)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hook type %s: %w\", hookType, err)\n\t}\n\trawHooks[hookType] = data\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// hookBashExists checks if a hook with the given bash command already exists.\nfunc hookBashExists(entries []CopilotHookEntry, bash string) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif entry.Bash == bash {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// isEntireHook checks if a hook entry's bash command belongs to Entire.\n// hookEntryBash reads the command off a hook entry for the shared helpers.\n// Copilot CLI stores it under `bash`, not `command`.\nfunc hookEntryBash(e CopilotHookEntry) string { return e.Bash }\n\nfunc isEntireHook(bash string) bool {\n\treturn agent.IsManagedHookCommand(bash)\n}\n\n// hasEntireHook checks if any entry in the slice is an Entire hook.\nfunc hasEntireHook(entries []CopilotHookEntry) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif isEntireHook(entry.Bash) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// removeEntireHooks removes all Entire hooks from the slice.\nfunc removeEntireHooks(entries []CopilotHookEntry) []CopilotHookEntry {\n\tresult := make([]CopilotHookEntry, 0, len(entries))\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif !isEntireHook(entry.Bash) {\n\t\t\tresult = append(result, entry)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn result\n}\n\n// HookConfigRelPath implements agent.HookConfigLocator.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) HookConfigRelPath() string { return hooksDir + \"/\" + HooksFileName }\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n)\n\n// testSessionID is the UUID used in captured Copilot CLI hook payloads.\nconst testSessionID = \"b0ff98c0-8e01-4b73-bf92-9649b139931b\"\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Prompt != \"hi\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected prompt 'hi', got %q\", event.Prompt)\n\t}\n\tif event.Timestamp.IsZero() {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected non-zero timestamp\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted_TranscriptRef(t *testing.T) {\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tt.Setenv(\"ENTIRE_TEST_COPILOT_SESSION_DIR\", \"/test/sessions\")\n\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"test-sess-id\",\"prompt\":\"hello\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\texpected := \"/test/sessions/test-sess-id/events.jsonl\"\n\tif event.SessionRef != expected {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected SessionRef %q, got %q\", expected, event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"transcript_path\":\"/tmp/transcript.json\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Prompt != \"hi\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected prompt 'hi', got %q\", event.Prompt)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != \"/tmp/transcript.json\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionStart(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081383,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"source\":\"new\",\"initialPrompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Timestamp.IsZero() {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected non-zero timestamp\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionStart_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\ttranscriptPath := \"/home/user/.copilot/session-state/\" + testSessionID + \"/events.jsonl\"\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"transcriptPath\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != transcriptPath {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\ttranscriptPath := \"/tmp/transcript.json\"\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"Stop\",\"transcript_path\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != transcriptPath {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop_ExtractsModel(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\t// Create a temp transcript with tool.execution_complete containing model field\n\t// (Copilot CLI v0.0.421+ includes model per tool call, not via session.model_change)\n\tdir := t.TempDir()\n\ttranscriptPath := filepath.Join(dir, \"events.jsonl\")\n\ttranscriptContent := strings.Join([]string{\n\t\t`{\"type\":\"session.start\",\"data\":{\"sessionId\":\"model-sess\"},\"id\":\"1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-03T00:00:00Z\",\"parentId\":null}`,\n\t\t`{\"type\":\"user.message\",\"data\":{\"content\":\"hello\"},\"id\":\"2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-03T00:00:01Z\",\"parentId\":\"\"}`,\n\t\t`{\"type\":\"tool.execution_complete\",\"data\":{\"toolCallId\":\"tc1\",\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4.6\",\"toolTelemetry\":{\"properties\":{},\"metrics\":{}}},\"id\":\"3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-03-03T00:00:02Z\",\"parentId\":\"\"}`,\n\t}, \"\\n\") + \"\\n\"\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(transcriptPath, []byte(transcriptContent), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"failed to write test transcript: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"model-sess\",\"transcriptPath\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Model != \"claude-sonnet-4.6\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected model 'claude-sonnet-4.6', got %q\", event.Model)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop_NoTranscript_EmptyModel(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t// transcriptPath points to a nonexistent file — model should be empty, not error\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"no-model-sess\",\"transcriptPath\":\"/nonexistent/events.jsonl\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Model != \"\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected empty model for nonexistent transcript, got %q\", event.Model)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionEnd(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085425,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"reason\":\"complete\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionEnd, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionEnd_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t// VS Code uses \"Stop\" for both agent-stop and session-end hooks.\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"Stop\",\"reason\":\"complete\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionEnd, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionEnd_VSCodeNonTerminalStop_ReturnsNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"Stop\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionEnd, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif event != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for non-terminal VS Code Stop payload, got %+v\", event)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_VSCodeMismatchedHookEventName_ReturnsNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t// VS Code sends \"SessionStart\" but the CLI subcommand is \"agent-stop\" — mismatch.\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"transcript_path\":\"/tmp/t.json\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif event != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for mismatched hookEventName, got %+v\", event)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_VSCodeUnknownHookEventName_ReturnsNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"FutureEvent\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif event != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for unknown hookEventName, got %+v\", event)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_PassthroughHooks_VSCodePayload_ReturnNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tpassthroughHooks := []string{\n\t\tHookNamePreToolUse,\n\t\tHookNamePostToolUse,\n\t\tHookNameErrorOccurred,\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, hookName := range passthroughHooks {\n\t\tt.Run(hookName, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\t\t\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\"}`\n\t\t\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), hookName, strings.NewReader(input))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error for %s: %v\", hookName, err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif event != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for pass-through hook %s, got %+v\", hookName, event)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSubagentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SubagentEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SubagentEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession_LifecycleHooksReturnNil verifies that the\n// per-turn/session lifecycle hooks are dropped when Copilot fires them for a\n// subagent turn (sessionId is a Task tool-use id, e.g. \"toolu_…\"). Otherwise a\n// phantom top-level session is created that never ends and pins its shadow\n// branch open after the user commits.\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession_LifecycleHooksReturnNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tconst subagentSessionID = \"REDACTED\"\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\n\tlifecycleHooks := []string{\n\t\tHookNameUserPromptSubmitted,\n\t\tHookNameSessionStart,\n\t\tHookNameAgentStop,\n\t\tHookNameSessionEnd,\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, hookName := range lifecycleHooks {\n\t\tt.Run(hookName, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\t\t\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + subagentSessionID + `\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\t\t\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), hookName, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\t\t\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\t\t\trequire.Nil(t, event, \"expected nil event for subagent-session lifecycle hook %s\", hookName)\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession_SubagentStopStillFires verifies the\n// subagent-stop hook is NOT dropped — it always carries the main session id and\n// drives the task-checkpoint path.\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession_SubagentStopStillFires(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSubagentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"subagent-stop must still produce an event\")\n\trequire.Equal(t, agent.SubagentEnd, event.Type)\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_PassthroughHooks_ReturnNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tpassthroughHooks := []string{\n\t\tHookNamePreToolUse,\n\t\tHookNamePostToolUse,\n\t\tHookNameErrorOccurred,\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, hookName := range passthroughHooks {\n\t\tt.Run(hookName, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\t\t\t// Pass-through hooks should return nil event without reading stdin\n\t\t\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), hookName, strings.NewReader(\"\"))\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error for %s: %v\", hookName, err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif event != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for pass-through hook %s, got %+v\", hookName, event)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UnknownHook_ReturnsNil(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), \"unknown-hook-name\", strings.NewReader(`{\"sessionId\":\"s1\"}`))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif event != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event for unknown hook, got %+v\", event)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_EmptyInput_ReturnsError(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t_, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(\"\"))\n\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error for empty input, got nil\")\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"empty hook input\") {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected 'empty hook input' error, got: %v\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_MalformedJSON(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t_, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(`{\"sessionId\": INVALID}`))\n\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error for malformed JSON, got nil\")\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"failed to parse hook input\") {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected 'failed to parse hook input' error, got: %v\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AllHookTypes(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\ttestCases := []struct {\n\t\thookName      string\n\t\texpectedType  agent.EventType\n\t\texpectNil     bool\n\t\tinputTemplate string\n\t}{\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameUserPromptSubmitted,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.TurnStart,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s1\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameSessionStart,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.SessionStart,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s2\",\"source\":\"new\",\"initialPrompt\":\"hi\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameAgentStop,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.TurnEnd,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s3\",\"transcriptPath\":\"/t\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameSessionEnd,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.SessionEnd,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s4\",\"reason\":\"complete\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameSubagentStop,\n\t\t\texpectedType:  agent.SubagentEnd,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{\"timestamp\":1,\"cwd\":\"/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"s5\"}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNamePreToolUse,\n\t\t\texpectNil:     true,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNamePostToolUse,\n\t\t\texpectNil:     true,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{}`,\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\thookName:      HookNameErrorOccurred,\n\t\t\texpectNil:     true,\n\t\t\tinputTemplate: `{}`,\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, tc := range testCases {\n\t\tt.Run(tc.hookName, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\n\t\t\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\t\t\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), tc.hookName, strings.NewReader(tc.inputTemplate))\n\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tif tc.expectNil {\n\t\t\t\tif event != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected nil event, got %+v\", event)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\t\t\tif event.Type != tc.expectedType {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", tc.expectedType, event.Type)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestHookNames_ReturnsAllHooks(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tnames := ag.HookNames()\n\n\tif len(names) != 8 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"HookNames() returned %d hooks, want 8\", len(names))\n\t}\n\n\texpected := map[string]bool{\n\t\tHookNameUserPromptSubmitted: false,\n\t\tHookNameSessionStart:        false,\n\t\tHookNameAgentStop:           false,\n\t\tHookNameSessionEnd:          false,\n\t\tHookNameSubagentStop:        false,\n\t\tHookNamePreToolUse:          false,\n\t\tHookNamePostToolUse:         false,\n\t\tHookNameErrorOccurred:       false,\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, name := range names {\n\t\tif _, ok := expected[name]; !ok {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"unexpected hook name: %q\", name)\n\t\t}\n\t\texpected[name] = true\n\t}\n\n\tfor name, found := range expected {\n\t\tif !found {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"missing hook name: %q\", name)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:27:type SessionStore struct {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:54:func OpenSessionStore(ag SessionLocator, repoPath string) (*SessionStore, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:68:func OpenSessionStoreAt(ag SessionLocator, dir string) (*SessionStore, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:83:func (s *SessionStore) Dir() string { return s.dir }\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:103:func (s *SessionStore) openRoot() (*os.Root, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:110:func (s *SessionStore) openRootForWrite() (*os.Root, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:125:func (s *SessionStore) SessionFile(agentSessionID string) (name, absPath string, err error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:137:func (s *SessionStore) Name(p string) (string, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:164:func (s *SessionStore) ReadFile(name string) ([]byte, error) {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:176:func (s *SessionStore) WriteFile(name string, data []byte, perm os.FileMode) error {\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/session_store.go:198:func (s *SessionStore) Exists(name string) bool {\npackage agent\n\nimport (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/types\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/osroot\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n)\n\n// SessionStore is one agent's own session directory, held as an *os.Root.\n//\n// Every agent keeps its transcripts somewhere Entire does not own —\n// ~/.claude/projects/<hash>/, ~/.codex/sessions/, Cursor's SQLite store,\n// ~/.pi/agent/sessions/<encoded-repo>/, a temp dir for OpenCode — and Entire\n// reads and writes into all of them. The session ID that selects a file inside\n// one comes from an agent hook payload, so this is where an untrusted name\n// becomes a path, and a store gives each agent one handle to resolve it through.\n//\n// It deliberately does NOT try to contain the agent's own writes: the agent is a\n// separate process writing its own store. What it contains is Entire's reads and\n// writes, which is the half Entire is responsible for.\ntype SessionStore struct {\n\tagent SessionLocator\n\tdir   string\n}\n\n// SessionLocator is the slice of Agent a session store needs: where the agent\n// keeps sessions for a repo, and how it names a session's file inside that\n// directory. Narrow on purpose — a store has no business with transcripts,\n// chunking, or hooks, and depending on three methods instead of thirty is what\n// lets a test supply one without implementing the whole agent contract.\ntype SessionLocator interface {\n\tName() types.AgentName\n\tGetSessionDir(repoPath string) (string, error)\n\tResolveSessionFile(sessionDir, agentSessionID string) string\n}\n\n// ErrOutsideSessionStore reports a session file that does not lie inside the\n// agent's session directory. Callers match it with errors.Is.\nvar ErrOutsideSessionStore = errors.New(\"path is outside the agent's session directory\")\n\n// OpenSessionStore returns ag's session store for repoPath.\n//\n// The directory need NOT exist yet: resolving a session file is path arithmetic\n// plus a containment check, and callers legitimately ask where a transcript\n// *would* live before anything has created the directory. Only the I/O methods\n// need the directory, and they open a root at that point and close it again —\n// see openRoot for why a store is not one of the memoized anchors.\nfunc OpenSessionStore(ag SessionLocator, repoPath string) (*SessionStore, error) {\n\tif ag == nil {\n\t\treturn nil, errors.New(\"agent is required to open a session store\")\n\t}\n\tdir, err := ag.GetSessionDir(repoPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"resolve %s session directory: %w\", ag.Name(), err)\n\t}\n\treturn OpenSessionStoreAt(ag, dir)\n}\n\n// OpenSessionStoreAt is OpenSessionStore for a session directory the caller\n// already resolved — the cross-project fallbacks that scan sibling directories,\n// and agentimport, which is handed one.\nfunc OpenSessionStoreAt(ag SessionLocator, dir string) (*SessionStore, error) {\n\tif dir == \"\" {\n\t\treturn nil, errors.New(\"session directory is required\")\n\t}\n\tabs, err := filepath.Abs(dir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"resolve %s: %w\", dir, err)\n\t}\n\treturn &SessionStore{agent: ag, dir: abs}, nil\n}\n\n// Dir returns the store's absolute directory. It is for messages and for the\n// paths Entire hands to other processes (an agent's own resume command, a\n// transcript path recorded as a checkpoint's SessionRef); it is not an\n// invitation to do I/O on the result.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) Dir() string { return s.dir }\n\n// openRoot returns an *os.Root over the store directory. The CALLER closes it.\n//\n// Deliberately not osroot.Shared. That registry is for the handful of long-lived\n// anchors a process holds — .entire, the git common dir, the worktree — and it\n// never evicts, by design. A session store is not one of them: transcript\n// fallback search (searchTranscriptInProjectDirs) opens a store for EVERY\n// candidate directory it walks under ~/.claude/projects, and memoizing those\n// retained one directory fd per candidate for the life of the process. Measured\n// at exactly one fd per directory probed, against zero for the os.Stat this\n// replaced; a few hundred project directories is enough to reach the usual 1024\n// RLIMIT_NOFILE, at which point os.OpenRoot starts failing for every OTHER\n// anchor too, since they all come from the same registry.\n//\n// The cost of not sharing is one openat per store operation, against reading a\n// transcript that is routinely megabytes.\n//\n// A directory that does not exist is reported unwrapped so callers can classify\n// it with os.IsNotExist.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) openRoot() (*os.Root, error) {\n\treturn os.OpenRoot(s.dir) //nolint:wrapcheck // see doc comment\n}\n\n// openRootForWrite is openRoot with the store directory created first. The\n// directory is the root itself, so it cannot be created through it — this is the\n// one place that reaches it from the outside. The caller closes the result.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) openRootForWrite() (*os.Root, error) {\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(s.dir, 0o750); err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create session directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn s.openRoot()\n}\n\n// SessionFile resolves agentSessionID to a name inside the store, and to the\n// absolute path of the same file.\n//\n// This is the check the whole type exists for. The agent decides its own file\n// layout via ResolveSessionFile — some nest, some append an extension — and the\n// ID reaching it came from a hook payload. Converting the result back into a\n// name relative to the store rejects an ID that walked out of the directory,\n// which a plain filepath.Join would have produced silently.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) SessionFile(agentSessionID string) (name, absPath string, err error) {\n\tresolved := s.agent.ResolveSessionFile(s.dir, agentSessionID)\n\tname, err = s.Name(resolved)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", \"\", err\n\t}\n\treturn name, resolved, nil\n}\n\n// Name converts a path into a name inside the store, reporting\n// ErrOutsideSessionStore for one that is not. A path already relative to the\n// store is accepted as-is.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) Name(p string) (string, error) {\n\tif p == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: empty path\", ErrOutsideSessionStore)\n\t}\n\t// VolumeName alongside IsAbs, the pairing validation.ValidateSessionID and\n\t// gitrepo's alternates checks already use. A Windows drive-relative path\n\t// like \"C:foo\" contains no separator and IsAbs reports false, so it would\n\t// otherwise be taken as a name inside the store — while filepath.Join drops\n\t// the base directory when the appended element carries a volume. Sending it\n\t// down the absolute branch makes filepath.Rel reject it across volumes,\n\t// which is the answer this containment check exists to give. No-op on Unix,\n\t// where VolumeName is always empty.\n\tif !filepath.IsAbs(p) && filepath.VolumeName(p) == \"\" {\n\t\tcleaned := filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Clean(filepath.FromSlash(p)))\n\t\tif cleaned == \".\" || paths.IsRelativeTraversal(cleaned) {\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", ErrOutsideSessionStore, p)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn cleaned, nil\n\t}\n\trel, err := filepath.Rel(s.dir, p)\n\tif err != nil || rel == \".\" || paths.IsRelativeTraversal(rel) {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s is not inside %s\", ErrOutsideSessionStore, p, s.dir)\n\t}\n\treturn filepath.ToSlash(rel), nil\n}\n\n// ReadFile reads name from the store.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) ReadFile(name string) ([]byte, error) {\n\troot, err := s.openRoot()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\tdefer root.Close()\n\treturn osroot.ReadFileNoFollow(root, name) //nolint:wrapcheck // preserved for os.IsNotExist at call sites\n}\n\n// WriteFile writes name in the store, creating parent directories. Session\n// layouts nest (Gemini keys by project hash, Pi by encoded repo path), so the\n// parents are made here rather than at each call site.\nfunc (s *SessionStore) WriteFile(name string, data []byte, perm os.FileMode) error {\n\troot, err := s.openRootForWrite()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdefer root.Close()\n\tif dir := filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Dir(filepath.FromSlash(name))); dir != \".\" {\n\t\tif err := osroot.MkdirAllNoSymlink(root, dir, 0o750); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"create session directory: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif info, err := osroot.LstatNoSymlinks(root, name); err == nil && info.Mode()&os.ModeSymlink != 0 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write session file: %w\", osroot.ErrSymlinkedPath)\n\t} else if err != nil && !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"inspect session file: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn jsonutil.WriteFileAtomicIn(root, name, data, perm) //nolint:wrapcheck // preserved for os.IsNotExist at call sites\n}\n\n// Exists reports whether name is present in the store. Lstat, not Stat: a\n// dangling symlink is still a file that exists and must not be overwritten\n// silently (see the rewind restore path, which distinguishes the two).\nfunc (s *SessionStore) Exists(name string) bool {\n\troot, err := s.openRoot()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tdefer root.Close()\n\t_, err = osroot.LstatNoSymlinks(root, name)\n\treturn err == nil\n}\n\n// WriteSessionFile writes data to s.SessionRef through ag's own session store,\n// creating parent directories.\n//\n// It exists because every agent's WriteSession was the same four lines —\n// os.MkdirAll of the parent, then os.WriteFile of an absolute SessionRef — eight\n// times over, each one taking the path on trust. Routing them through the store\n// makes the containment one decision instead of eight, and the parent-directory\n// create stops being something each agent has to remember.\n//\n// The store is anchored on s.RepoPath when it is set, which is the agent's real\n// session directory for that repo. When it is not (callers that only carry a\n// path, such as a restore driven from checkpoint metadata), the SessionRef's own\n// directory anchors it: that contains nothing by itself, but it keeps the write\n// on the same code path, and SessionRef there came from Entire's own resolution\n// rather than from an agent payload.\nfunc WriteSessionFile(ag SessionLocator, s *AgentSession, data []byte, perm os.FileMode) error {\n\tif s == nil {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"session is nil\")\n\t}\n\tif s.SessionRef == \"\" {\n\t\treturn errors.New(\"session reference (transcript path) is required\")\n\t}\n\n\tstore, err := sessionStoreForWrite(ag, s)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tname, err := store.Name(s.SessionRef)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write session: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := store.WriteFile(name, data, perm); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to write transcript: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// sessionStoreForWrite resolves the store a session write lands in.\n//\n// With a RepoPath, that is the agent's session directory for it, and a\n// SessionRef outside that directory is an ERROR rather than a reason to anchor\n// somewhere else. It used to fall through to SessionRef's own parent, which made\n// the containment check its own off switch: the one input that fails it was the\n// one input that disabled it. The comment justifying that said some agents\n// resolve a restored session to a sibling directory — they do not.\n// RestoredSessionPathResolver's only implementation (Codex) returns\n// <sessionDir>/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-*.jsonl, which nests INSIDE the store, so the\n// branch was unreachable as well as unsound.\n//\n// Without a RepoPath the SessionRef's own directory is the only candidate there\n// is. That anchor contains nothing by itself, and it is kept because the\n// alternative is refusing to write at all; what makes it acceptable is that\n// SessionRef there came from Entire's own resolution rather than from an agent\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Design\n\n## Goal\n\nGive GitHub Copilot CLI the same normalized subagent lifecycle used by Claude\nCode and Codex: one correctly correlated durable task record per native child,\nincluding child metadata, files, transcript when available, and exact token\nusage when Copilot exposes it.\n\n## Current behavior\n\nEntire's Copilot adapter reflects an older CLI contract:\n\n- it installs `subagentStop` but not `subagentStart`;\n- it discards `preToolUse` and `postToolUse` payloads;\n- it converts `subagentStop` into `SubagentEnd` with only the parent session ID;\n- shared lifecycle code therefore merges all uncorrelated Copilot children into\n  the task record keyed by the empty string; and\n- its subordinate-session guard recognizes only the historical `toolu_` prefix.\n\nThis preserves parent-level file capture but is not per-child tracking.\n\nCurrent Copilot CLI documentation exposes both `subagentStart` and\n`subagentStop` for YAML-based built-in agents and custom agents. The start\npayload contains `sessionId`, `transcriptPath`, and agent metadata but no\n`agentId`; the stop payload adds `agentId`, `agentType`, and the final response.\nThe built-in `general-purpose` agent deliberately emits neither event.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Install, detect, preserve, and remove the native `subagentStart` hook.\n- Parse current camelCase Copilot CLI payloads and compatible snake_case\n  payloads without weakening existing VS Code compatibility checks.\n- Prove and use a collision-free value shared by start and stop as Entire's\n  `ToolUseID`.\n- Map stop `agentId` to `SubagentID` and retain the native child transcript path\n  only when a real current capture proves that `transcriptPath` identifies the\n  child rather than the parent.\n- Reuse the existing `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd`, task-record, condensation,\n  sanitization, externalization, redaction, and `tasks/` materialization paths.\n- Preserve phantom-session prevention for historical child lifecycle IDs,\n  including both observed `toolu_` and `tooluse_` spellings.\n- Validate the behavior with simulated hooks, one focused integration test,\n  the existing E2E scenario, and an end-user real Copilot smoke test.\n- Document the `general-purpose` exception truthfully.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Rebuilding shared task-record or checkpoint persistence.\n- Guessing child identity from task descriptions, timestamps, directory order,\n  or \"most recent\" state.\n- Claiming exact per-child tokens when Copilot exposes only a session aggregate.\n- Treating the final response text as a canonical child transcript.\n- Solving `general-purpose` through heuristic attribution. If the evidence\n  phase finds a deterministic native signal, it may be added through the same\n  tests; otherwise it remains an explicit upstream limitation and follow-up.\n- Merging any pull request.\n\n## Design\n\n### Evidence gate\n\nBefore production changes, and only after explicit authorization for a real\nCopilot invocation, run Copilot CLI 1.0.82 or newer in an isolated repository\nwith capture-only hooks. Exercise two same-type native subagents concurrently,\none writing and one read-only, and one `general-purpose` child. Record only\npayload structure, identifiers, event order, transcript locations, and token\nfields. Parallel evidence is mandatory whenever transcript-path identity is a\ncandidate correlation source.\n\nThe native implementation proceeds only if start and stop expose a stable,\none-to-one correlation source. The preferred mapping is the native child ID if\nit is present in both events. Otherwise a canonical child transcript path may\nbe converted to a path-safe deterministic digest, but only after the capture\nproves that path is stable across start/stop and unique across parallel\nchildren. Canonical store-relative layout validation must precede digesting at\nboth boundaries: equivalent spellings of one path map to one identity, while\ndistinct concurrent canonical paths remain distinct. An outside-store,\nwrong-layout, symlinked, missing, or otherwise unvalidated path creates no\nevent or marker. If neither condition holds, stop and revise the design rather\nthan ship ambiguous attribution.\n\nThe same capture must prove the ordering of child start/stop relative to parent\n`agentStop` and `sessionEnd`, when child transcript bytes become readable, and\nwhether the child transcript survives until condensation. If parent session\ntermination can precede native child stop, stop and revise the lifecycle design:\nthe current SessionEnd sweep would otherwise complete and condense a live marker\nwithout the stop's child metadata.\n\nIf transcript path is the correlation source, the capture must additionally\nshow that the canonical non-symlink child file is present and verifiable at\nboth start and stop. If child file attribution depends on transcript bytes, the\nfile must be readable at stop; otherwise the implementation pauses for a design\nthat can safely defer attribution instead of silently producing incomplete\nrecords.\n\n### Hook adapter\n\nAdd `subagent-start` beside the existing Copilot hook verbs and include the\n`subagentStart` key in installation, uninstall, idempotency, and presence/drift\ncoverage. Copilot gains a read-only `CheckHookConfig`: absent/user-only files are\nabsent, the exact managed set is current, and any managed-but-incomplete,\nstale, malformed, or unreadable configuration is outdated. Extend the\ncompatibility envelope only with fields required by the documented subagent\npayloads.\n\n`subagentStart` maps to `agent.SubagentStart` with:\n\n- the parent Copilot session as `SessionID`;\n- the proven stable correlation value as `ToolUseID`;\n- native agent name/type and description when present; and\n- the canonical child transcript as `SubagentTranscriptPath` only after\n  store-confined, no-follow validation.\n\n`subagentStop` maps to `agent.SubagentEnd` with the same `ToolUseID`, stop\n`agentId` as `SubagentID`, the parent transcript as `SessionRef`, native labels,\nand the verified child transcript path. It remains `Final: false` because\nCopilot supplies one true-completion end signal rather than Claude Code's\nlaunch-stub-plus-final pair. A narrow normalized-event marker distinguishes\nthis native start/stop lifecycle from the existing foreground PostToolUse\ncompletion path. The same marker declares that any supplied child transcript\npath is authoritative: Copilot records never probe the generic Claude-style\nsubagent layout when that path is absent, disappears, or cannot be read.\n\n### Durable capture\n\nNo new storage model is introduced. For the marked native lifecycle, generic\nstart handling adds a live `session.TaskRecord` only to an existing parent\nsession. Generic end handling requires that live record, uses only hook- or\nchild-transcript-authoritative file evidence, bypasses the no-file skip for a\nread-only child, and completes it exactly once. An unmatched, duplicate, or\nmissing/ended-parent stop is a no-op and never creates or resurrects state.\nThis path is separate from the existing Final=false foreground PostToolUse\npath, whose whole-worktree scan is unsafe for concurrent children.\n\nThe task record persists an explicit authoritative-transcript/no-fallback bit.\nCompletion merges start and stop metadata field-by-field: stop values win when\npresent, while an omitted stop field retains the start value. This includes\n`SubagentType`, `TaskDescription`, `AgentID`, the declared transcript, and its\nprovenance. Consequently, a start that lacks a description can still retain a\ndescription supplied by stop, without erasing a name learned at start.\nThe verified start transcript path is stored on the live record immediately,\nsurvives a JSON state round trip, remains when stop omits it, and is replaced\nonly by a non-empty verified stop path.\n\nCondensation writes\n`tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` and, when available,\n`agent-<agent-id>.jsonl`. Missing child transcripts retain a metadata record\nwith an existing path-free unavailability reason. For an authoritative Copilot\nrecord, a missing or unreadable declared path never falls through to either\n`ResolveAgentTranscriptPath` during completion or\n`resolveTaskTranscriptPath` during condensation, even if a coincidental file\nexists at the generic layout.\n\nConfinement applies to every read, not just initial hook parsing. The Copilot\nadapter performs one `SessionStore`-anchored, no-follow read at stop and derives\nboth `Event.ModifiedFiles` and exact usage from those bytes, so shared lifecycle\ncode does not reopen the path through `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset`.\nCondensation independently revalidates and reopens an authoritative path\nthrough `SessionStore.ReadFile`; it never sends that path to unrestricted\n`ReadTranscriptFile`/`readFirstTranscript`. A file replaced by a symlink after\nparsing or immediately before condensation therefore yields transcript\nunavailability rather than reading outside the store.\n\nExact child token usage is stored only if a canonical child transcript or\nmachine-readable per-agent usage record supplies an exact total. The Copilot\nadapter accepts usage only when the verified child transcript already contains\nthe authoritative `session.shutdown` aggregate with non-empty `modelMetrics`.\nIt uses an exact-only extractor rather than the existing calculator's partial\nassistant-message fallback, and places the result on `Event.TokenUsage` before\ndispatch. The hook path is accepted only when it resolves to the captured\ncanonical file layout beneath Copilot's session store; outside-store paths,\nsymlinks, and layout mismatches yield neither a declared child transcript nor\nchild usage. Otherwise the record's child token usage remains unavailable;\nparent session totals continue through the existing Copilot calculator and are\nnot replaced or double-counted by partial child data.\n\n### General-purpose behavior\n\nThe probe must confirm the documented absence of native start/stop hooks. The\nexisting subordinate lifecycle filter remains in place so a child cannot open\na phantom top-level Entire session. Supporting `general-purpose` requires a\nstable parent/child/call relationship under parallel execution; descriptions\nand recency are expressly insufficient.\n\nIf current Copilot re-emits a deterministic child task ID and canonical child\nsession evidence, add a narrowly scoped adapter using that identity. Otherwise\nthe PR documents the exception and does not imply parity for that built-in.\n\n## Error handling and privacy\n\n- Malformed subagent payloads return ordinary parse errors and never create a\n  partial task record.\n- Missing optional metadata degrades field-by-field.\n- Invalid or ambiguous correlation fails closed for per-child capture while\n  preserving parent-session checkpoint behavior.\n- A native stop after parent SessionEnd is skipped unless the evidence phase\n  proves and the design explicitly handles a safe retained-state ordering.\n- Logs contain identifiers, key names, counts, and paths already permitted by\n  current operational logging; never prompts, responses, or transcript text.\n- Hook output remains empty/pass-through so Entire cannot block Copilot work.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Fresh installation includes exactly one managed `subagentStart` and one\n  managed `subagentStop`; upgrade, reinstall, and uninstall are idempotent and\n  preserve user hooks and unknown fields.\n- Two native children with the same agent type receive different stable task\n  IDs and cannot complete each other's records.\n- A writing child contributes its file and native child transcript to its own\n  durable `tasks/` subtree after a normal user commit.\n- A read-only child still produces its own durable metadata/transcript record.\n- Duplicate stop delivery does not duplicate or overwrite another child.\n- Unmatched stops and stops after missing/ended parent state create nothing.\n- Metadata present only at stop is merged into the start-created record.\n- Missing authoritative child transcripts never fall back to a generic\n  agent-layout file.\n- Partial message-only usage, unsafe paths, and symlinks (including paths\n  replaced by symlinks after parsing) never become child transcript, child-file,\n  or exact child-token evidence.\n- Historical subordinate session IDs do not create phantom sessions.\n- Parent checkpoint behavior, VS Code compatibility, and non-subagent Copilot\n  lifecycle behavior remain unchanged.\n- The real E2E repository provisions and commits a named\n  `.github/agents/entire-e2e-subagent.agent.md` fixture before hook installation\n  and before `HeadBefore`/`CheckpointBefore` are captured, then explicitly asks\n  for that agent; prompt inference is not accepted as proof that a hook-emitting\n  child ran.\n- Focused tests, `mise run check`, the Copilot E2E subagent flow, and a real\n  current-Copilot smoke test pass before push.\n\n## Size target\n\nTarget 450-700 additions and 50-100 deletions, including tests and docs. Reuse\nexisting tables and integration helpers. If the implementation exceeds roughly\n800 additions, pause and revisit the adapter boundary before continuing.\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Implementation Plan\n\n> **Execution constraint:** Implement this plan sequentially in the primary session. Do not launch implementation subagents. Follow the red/green checkpoints task-by-task; checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax records progress.\n\n**Goal:** Track each hook-emitting Copilot CLI subagent as its own durable Entire task with correct identity, files, transcript availability, and exact token usage when natively available.\n\n**Architecture:** Upgrade the Copilot adapter to consume native `subagentStart` and the complete `subagentStop` payload, then feed those events into a narrow marker-backed path in Entire's existing task-record lifecycle. A real-current-Copilot evidence gate must prove collision-free correlation, event ordering, and transcript availability before production mapping is chosen; ambiguous `general-purpose` behavior stays fail-closed rather than heuristic.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, Cobra hook commands, Copilot CLI JSON hooks/JSONL sessions, testify, Entire integration harness, mise.\n\n**Design:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md`\n\n---\n\n### Task 0: Refresh the clean feature branch\n\n**Files:** None\n\n- [ ] Confirm `git status --short` has no tracked changes and record `git rev-parse HEAD` plus `git rev-parse origin/main`.\n- [ ] Run `git fetch origin main`. If this feature branch still has no unique commits, fast-forward it with `git merge --ff-only origin/main`; if it has diverged, stop and inspect rather than rewriting history.\n- [ ] Re-run the relevant Copilot adapter tests on the refreshed base before starting the evidence capture.\n\n### Task 1: Capture the current Copilot subagent contract\n\n**Files:**\n- Use: `/tmp` disposable repository and capture directory only\n- Reference: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md`\n- Reference: historical `scripts/test-copilot-cli-agent-integration.sh`\n\n- [ ] Obtain explicit user authorization for the real Copilot invocations in this task; do not treat plan approval as paid-E2E approval.\n- [ ] Record the candidate and installed Copilot versions; use an isolated official Copilot CLI 1.0.82-or-newer binary without replacing the user's installed binary.\n- [ ] Create a disposable git repository with isolated Entire config/cache/token-store paths. Keep Copilot authentication available without modifying the user's Copilot configuration; if an isolated `COPILOT_HOME` cannot authenticate, stop rather than copy credentials into artifacts.\n- [ ] Register capture-only `subagentStart`, `subagentStop`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `agentStop`, `sessionEnd`, and subordinate session lifecycle hooks; restrict tool hooks to the task tool when matchers support it.\n- [ ] Provision and commit `.github/agents/entire-evidence-subagent.agent.md` with a lowercase stable name, required `description`, and minimal instructions. Create it before the measured session so it is not attributed to a child.\n- [ ] Run two same-type native children concurrently: one creates a distinctive file and one is read-only. Concurrency is mandatory if transcript path is considered as correlation evidence.\n- [ ] Run one built-in `general-purpose` child to confirm the documented hook exception and observe subordinate lifecycle/event evidence.\n- [ ] Capture only hook names, payload key names/types, IDs, timestamps, event ordering, transcript paths, transcript event types, file existence/identity, and usage field structure; do not preserve prompts, responses, file contents, credentials, or tokens.\n- [ ] Prove start/stop order relative to parent `agentStop` and `sessionEnd`, when child transcript bytes become readable, and whether they remain readable through normal commit-time condensation.\n- [ ] Prove whether `transcriptPath` is parent or child, stable across start/stop, and unique across the concurrent same-type children.\n- [ ] Select the correlation mapping and record it in `AGENT.md` before production code:\n  - native child ID present at both boundaries: use it directly for `ToolUseID`;\n  - stable unique child transcript path at both boundaries: use a deterministic path-safe digest and retain stop `agentId` as `SubagentID`;\n  - no one-to-one invariant: stop and revise the design; never match by description, timestamp proximity, or latest state.\n- [ ] If parent `sessionEnd` can precede native child stop, stop and revise the lifecycle design before Task 4; the current SessionEnd sweep cannot safely synthesize missing stop metadata.\n- [ ] Determine whether a canonical child transcript or exact per-agent machine-readable usage persists without requiring Entire to launch Copilot with special flags.\n- [ ] Remove the disposable repository and retain only a credential-free structural report outside the product diff.\n\n### Task 2: Install, preserve, and diagnose `subagentStart`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/types.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend existing hook-name/install table tests to expect `subagent-start`; run them red because only eight hooks are installed.\n- [ ] Add upgrade coverage proving a pre-feature `entire.json` remains recognized as installed while reinstall adds exactly the missing managed hook and preserves user entries/unknown fields.\n- [ ] Add `CheckHookConfig` tests for absent and user-only files (`HooksAbsent`), exact current configuration (`HooksCurrent`), missing `subagentStart`, stale managed commands, malformed JSON, and unreadable files (`HooksOutdated` once any managed ownership is present or currentness cannot be proven).\n- [ ] Run the new upgrade/freshness tests red.\n- [ ] Add `HookNameSubagentStart`, the `subagentStart` config key/field, and the managed hook entry through the existing install/uninstall loops.\n- [ ] Implement read-only `agent.HookFreshness` behavior without changing `AreHooksInstalled`'s ownership/presence semantics.\n- [ ] Include native and compatible `SubagentStart` in event validation without weakening VS Code mismatch rejection.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestInstallHooks|TestUninstallHooks|TestHookNames|TestCheckHookConfig' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 3: Parse complete native subagent payloads\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add one table-driven test covering captured camelCase start/stop and compatible snake_case start/stop, asserting session, stable correlation, child ID, labels, and transcript roles.\n- [ ] Add only distinct failure contracts: missing/ambiguous correlation, nullable transcript, and mismatched compatible event name.\n- [ ] Run the new tests red and confirm failures come from discarded fields/missing start handling.\n- [ ] Extend `hookEnvelope` with only captured/documented fields required for normalized events (`agentId`, agent type/name/display/description, and the proven correlation input).\n- [ ] Implement one correlation helper from Task 1's proven invariant and validate its result through existing tool-use ID rules. If identity is path-derived, first normalize and validate the path as the exact canonical store-relative child layout at both start and stop, then digest that canonical name—never the raw hook string.\n- [ ] Add path-derived correlation tests proving equivalent absolute/relative/cleaned spellings map identically, distinct same-type concurrent child paths remain distinct, and outside-store, wrong-layout, missing, or symlinked paths return no normalized event and create no marker.\n- [ ] Map start to `agent.SubagentStart` and stop to `agent.SubagentEnd` with identical `ToolUseID`; map stop `agentId` to `SubagentID`.\n- [ ] Keep Copilot stop `Final: false`; it is a single true-completion end event, not Claude Code's launch-stub-plus-later-final pair.\n- [ ] Set `SessionRef` and `SubagentTranscriptPath` according to captured parent/child path roles; never treat response text as a canonical transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent|TestParseHookEnvelope' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 4: Add marker-backed native lifecycle completion\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/event.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_git.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add failing lifecycle tests named `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentStart_MarkerBackedRegistersLiveRecord`, `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentEnd_MarkerBackedReadOnlyCompletes`, `...ConcurrentReverseStopsStayDisjoint`, `...DuplicateStopIsNoOp`, `...UnmatchedStopIsNoOp`, and `...MissingOrEndedParentIsNoOp`.\n- [ ] In the concurrent test, use two same-type tasks, reverse completion order, distinct child transcripts/files, and assert neither record receives the other's evidence.\n- [ ] Add a red metadata-merge test where start supplies the type but omits the description, stop supplies the description and agent ID, and the completed record retains all three. Stop values win when non-empty; each missing stop field falls back independently to start.\n- [ ] Add a red authoritative-path test where the declared child path disappears before condensation while a coincidental generic-layout `agent-<id>.jsonl` exists; assert the payload records transcript unavailability and never stores the generic file.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1` and verify the tests fail against the existing foreground path.\n- [ ] Add one narrowly named normalized-event marker for native start/stop lifecycles whose completion must claim a start-created record. Set it only on Copilot's proven native events.\n- [ ] Add `TaskRecord.DeclaredTranscriptAuthoritative` (name may be adjusted for clarity) so the no-fallback contract survives state persistence. Mark every native Copilot task authoritative even when its verified declared path is empty.\n- [ ] On marked start, mutate only an existing active parent state and add a live `TaskRecord` containing the proven `ToolUseID`, labels, start time, verified start `DeclaredTranscriptPath`, and authoritative-transcript bit; do not call `EnsureSessionExists` and do not resurrect ended state. Capture pre-task state only as best-effort fallback, not authoritative parallel file evidence.\n- [ ] Add a state JSON round-trip test proving the verified start path and authoritative bit survive serialization. Add lifecycle tests proving a stop without a path retains the start path and a non-empty verified stop path replaces it.\n- [ ] On marked Final=false end, require the matching live record, reject missing/ended parent state, first fill only the stop event's empty metadata fields from start, and complete exactly once. This makes every non-empty stop value authoritative without losing start-only fields.\n- [ ] Extend `strategy.applyTaskRecordCompletion` to write each non-empty merged completion value (`SubagentType`, `TaskDescription`, `AgentID`, and declared path) onto the live record, plus token usage and the authoritative bit. Keep the existing behavior for unmarked producers whose completion fields are empty.\n- [ ] Reuse/refactor existing completion machinery with `bypassNoChangesSkip: true`, an event-files-only option, and a no-layout-fallback option derived from the marker. For marked Copilot completion, accept only adapter-populated `Event.ModifiedFiles`; do not run the path-based `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset` analyzer or a whole-worktree scan.\n- [ ] In `completeSubagentTaskRecord`, do not call `ResolveAgentTranscriptPath` or reopen the transcript for marked authoritative events. In `materializeTaskRecords`, when the persisted authoritative bit is set, try only `DeclaredTranscriptPath`; if it is empty, missing, or unreadable, emit the existing path-free unavailability reason and do not call `resolveTaskTranscriptPath`.\n- [ ] Add a narrow authoritative-task reader in condensation that opens the agent's store with `agent.OpenSessionStore(ag, state.WorktreePath)`, converts the declared path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the captured Copilot layout, and reads with `SessionStore.ReadFile` (no-follow). Never pass authoritative paths to `readFirstTranscript` or unrestricted `agent.ReadTranscriptFile`.\n- [ ] Add race-regression tests that replace the child file with a symlink after parse/before dispatch and again immediately before condensation. Dispatch may retain files/usage already derived from the safely read original bytes, but it must perform no second read and must not attribute data found only in the symlink target; condensation stores the existing path-free transcript-unavailable reason and never the target bytes.\n- [ ] Keep existing unmarked foreground PostToolUse behavior and existing Final=true background behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`, `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test.*TaskRecord.*(Metadata|Authoritative|Fallback)' -count=1`, and `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_Subagent' -count=1`; make all green.\n\n### Task 5: Preserve subordinate-session safety\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend the existing phantom-session characterization test with both observed historical prefixes, `toolu_` and `tooluse_`, plus a real UUID parent session.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession' -count=1` and verify `tooluse_` fails.\n- [ ] Replace the single-prefix assumption with the narrowest predicate justified by captured current and historical evidence; do not classify arbitrary non-UUID user input as a child unless Copilot guarantees parent IDs are UUIDs.\n- [ ] Verify subordinate session lifecycle hooks remain suppressed while native parent-scoped subagent hooks still produce normalized events.\n- [ ] Re-run the exact focused command and make it green.\n\n### Task 6: Wire exact child files and usage without guessing\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify if evidence supports a canonical child file: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] If Task 1 proves a canonical child JSONL file, add a fixture proving the existing analyzer extracts only that child's files and an exact full-child token total only when that child file contains an authoritative `session.shutdown` record with non-empty `modelMetrics`.\n- [ ] Add an exact-only helper returning `(usage, exact)` (or equivalent) that never invokes the existing assistant-message fallback. Keep the public parent/session `TokenCalculator` behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Add `TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_ExactChildUsage` and `...PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil`, including assertions that parent/session aggregate fields are not copied into the child record and a child transcript containing only `assistant.message.outputTokens` yields nil usage.\n- [ ] Add path-confinement tests for a declared path outside Copilot's session store, a symlink inside the store, and a syntactically plausible but wrong-layout file. Each must yield nil child usage and an empty declared child transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_(ExactChildUsage|PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil)|Test.*ChildTranscript' -count=1` red.\n- [ ] Add one Copilot helper that canonicalizes the hook path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the exact captured `<session-store>/<child-session>/events.jsonl` layout, and reads it with `SessionStore.ReadFile`. The rooted no-follow read rejects symlinks and later replacements; do not call unrestricted `os.ReadFile` on hook input.\n- [ ] From that one safely read byte slice, populate `Event.ModifiedFiles` through the existing Copilot JSONL parsing helpers and set `Event.TokenUsage` only when the authoritative completion aggregate is present. A readable transcript with only fallback message tokens is not exact and leaves usage nil.\n- [ ] If per-agent usage exists only in a requested `--usage-output-file`, do not depend on it because Entire does not launch the user's Copilot process.\n- [ ] If no canonical child transcript exists, retain metadata with the existing unavailable reason, leave child usage nil, and do not reconstruct a transcript from response text.\n- [ ] Run the same focused command green.\n\n### Task 7: Prove durable per-child capture through simulated hooks\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/copilot_subagent_test.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/testenv.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n\n- [ ] Write one integration test that initializes an isolated repo, starts a Copilot parent session, sends two captured-shape native starts with the same agent type, creates one child transcript per native contract, and sends stops in reverse order.\n- [ ] Commit one child-owned file through normal prepare-commit-msg/post-commit hooks and assert two distinct `tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` records in the permanent checkpoint.\n- [ ] Assert each record retains its own `agent_id`, labels, disjoint file list, completion state, exact usage when the child fixture includes an authoritative aggregate, and child transcript or the existing path-free unavailability reason.\n- [ ] Include one read-only child in the same fixture and assert it remains a distinct durable record.\n- [ ] Include duplicate stop, unmatched stop, and post-ended-session stop in the same lifecycle setup only where assertions remain readable; otherwise rely on Task 4's direct tests rather than duplicating them.\n- [ ] Treat this as a green end-to-end characterization after Tasks 2-6, not as a false red TDD step. Tasks 4 and 6 supply the focused red/green proof for shared lifecycle and exact child evidence.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1` and make it green.\n- [ ] Make only adapter-level or narrowly necessary shared changes if the characterization exposes a gap; do not duplicate materialization or add Copilot-specific checkpoint storage.\n\n### Task 8: Pin `general-purpose` and update documentation\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify only if Task 1 proves deterministic fallback evidence: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n\n- [ ] Add a fixture matching Task 1's `general-purpose` evidence and verify it cannot create a phantom top-level session.\n- [ ] If capture exposes a stable parent session, globally unique task ID, true completion, and canonical child evidence, first add a failing parallel same-type correlation test, then implement the narrow fallback.\n- [ ] If any invariant is absent, keep fallback out of production and document the upstream exception and capability boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] Remove stale claims that Copilot has no `subagentStart`; document current payload roles, minimum verified version, native-agent coverage, correlation invariant, ordering, transcript availability, and historical subordinate-session behavior.\n- [ ] Update the agent guide's Copilot event matrix so it matches installed native start/stop behavior.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession|TestParseHookEvent_GeneralPurpose|TestHookNames' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 9: Strengthen the existing E2E scenario without duplicating it\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go`\n- Modify: `e2e/testutil/repo.go`\n- Reuse: `e2e/testutil` checkpoint readers\n\n- [ ] Add a small Copilot fixture helper in `e2e/testutil/repo.go` that writes both `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `.github/agents/entire-e2e-subagent.agent.md`, then commits them before `entire.Enable`, hook installation, and construction of `RepoState` (`HeadBefore`/`CheckpointBefore`). Its agent frontmatter uses `name: entire-e2e-subagent`, a required description, and minimal file-writing instructions.\n- [ ] For `s.Agent.Name() == \"copilot-cli\"`, explicitly prompt the parent to delegate to `entire-e2e-subagent`; do not rely on inference or the built-in `general-purpose` agent.\n- [ ] Keep existing cross-agent file/checkpoint assertions. Add Copilot-specific committed `tasks/` assertions keyed by the discovered single task directory: one task, expected child-created file, non-empty safe `agent_id`, and transcript presence/unavailability matching Task 1's proven contract.\n- [ ] Ensure the committed custom-agent fixture predates capture and is absent from child `files` attribution.\n- [ ] Assert `HeadBefore` already includes the fixture commit and the fixture commit did not advance `CheckpointBefore`; this protects the measured checkpoint baseline from setup contamination.\n- [ ] Update Vogon's prompt parsing only if the minimally changed Copilot wording breaks the existing canary.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow` and make it green.\n- [ ] Do not add a second Copilot-only E2E scenario unless the shared test cannot express a required assertion.\n\n### Task 10: Verify size, correctness, and real end-user behavior\n\n**Files:** All modified files plus a disposable smoke-test repository.\n\n- [ ] Run `mise run fmt` and inspect every rewrite.\n- [ ] Run `mise run lint` after the final format pass.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` against the complete working tree and remove accidental duplication rather than suppressing it.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check`.\n- [ ] Run `git diff --check` and compare production/test additions with the 450-700 line target; pause for redesign if additions exceed roughly 800.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit authorization for each real Copilot validation phase, including the E2E invocation and separate smoke; plan approval alone is insufficient.\n- [ ] With authorization, run `mise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli TestSubagentCommitFlow` using a current Copilot binary.\n- [ ] Before the separate smoke, build a wrapper-free candidate `entire` into a dedicated temporary bin directory with a unique `versioninfo.Version` stamp containing the source commit/dirty marker. Record its SHA-256, construct a fixed `PATH` with that bin directory first, and use `whence -a entire` (or platform equivalent) to prove no other reachable `entire` precedes or shadows it. Record `command -v entire`, `entire version`, and the installed hook command before launch; stop on any mismatch.\n- [ ] In a separate disposable end-user repository, set isolated `COPILOT_HOME`, `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`; pass authentication only through already-present supported environment variables. Do not copy credential files or the user's Copilot/GitHub config, and stop if isolated authentication cannot be supplied.\n- [ ] With that isolated environment, enable Copilot hooks, provision and commit the named custom agent before capture, run a real child that creates a distinctive file, and commit normally. Tie the resulting hook log session ID to the checkpoint, then assert the checkpoint metadata's `cli_version` equals the unique candidate stamp; this proves the task artifact came from that binary without adding runtime logging. Inspect for exactly one correlated child task, exact child evidence when available, and no phantom session/shadow branch.\n- [ ] Preserve only a credential-free structural smoke report and remove disposable artifacts.\n- [ ] Commit only after required local gates pass; push only when authorized, then follow all repository/PR gates to terminal status without merging.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3084},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 21020)\nTotal output lines: 1708\n\npackage copilotcli\n\n// CopilotHooksFile represents the .github/hooks/entire.json structure.\n// Copilot CLI uses a flat JSON file with version and hooks sections.\n// All JSON files in .github/hooks/ are auto-discovered by the Copilot CLI.\n//\n\ntype CopilotHooksFile struct {\n\tVersion int          `json:\"version\"`\n\tHooks   CopilotHooks `json:\"hooks\"`\n}\n\n// CopilotHooks contains all hook configurations using camelCase keys.\n//\n\ntype CopilotHooks struct {\n\tUserPromptSubmitted []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"userPromptSubmitted,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionStart        []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"sessionStart,omitempty\"`\n\tAgentStop           []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"agentStop,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionEnd          []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"sessionEnd,omitempty\"`\n\tSubagentStop        []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"subagentStop,omitempty\"`\n\tPreToolUse          []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"preToolUse,omitempty\"`\n\tPostToolUse         []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"postToolUse,omitempty\"`\n\tErrorOccurred       []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"errorOccurred,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// CopilotHookEntry represents a single hook command.\n// Copilot CLI hooks have a type field (\"command\") and a bash field for the command string.\n// Optional fields (cwd, timeoutSec, env, comment) are preserved on round-trip.\n\ntype CopilotHookEntry struct {\n\tType       string            `json:\"type\"`\n\tBash       string            `json:\"bash\"`\n\tComment    string            `json:\"comment,omitempty\"`\n\tCwd        string            `json:\"cwd,omitempty\"`\n\tTimeoutSec int               `json:\"timeoutSec,omitempty\"`\n\tEnv        map[string]string `json:\"env,omitempty\"`\n}\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n)\n\n// HooksFileName is the hooks file managed by Entire for Copilot CLI.\nconst HooksFileName = \"entire.json\"\n\n// hooksDir is the directory within the repo where Copilot CLI looks for hook configs.\nconst hooksDir = \".github/hooks\"\n\n// hookConfigKey maps our kebab-case hook names to camelCase JSON keys.\nvar hookConfigKey = map[string]string{\n\tHookNameUserPromptSubmitted: \"userPromptSubmitted\",\n\tHookNameSessionStart:        \"sessionStart\",\n\tHookNameAgentStop:           \"agentStop\",\n\tHookNameSessionEnd:          \"sessionEnd\",\n\tHookNameSubagentStop:        \"subagentStop\",\n\tHookNamePreToolUse:          \"preToolUse\",\n\tHookNamePostToolUse:         \"postToolUse\",\n\tHookNameErrorOccurred:       \"errorOccurred\",\n}\n\n// copilotHookConfig returns .github/hooks/entire.json for the current worktree,\n// opened through the worktree's root. That directory lives in the working tree,\n// which arrives by clone, so a checked-in symlink at `.github` or\n// `.github/hooks` must not be something Entire creates directories under and\n// writes through. See agent.HookConfigFile.\nfunc copilotHookConfig(ctx context.Context) (*agent.HookConfigFile, error) {\n\tworktreeRoot, err := paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\t// Not a repository (tests, and `enable` before `git init`): the process\n\t\t// directory is the only candidate, and it is a directory the caller\n\t\t// chose rather than one derived from anything read off disk.\n\t\tworktreeRoot = \".\"\n\t}\n\treturn agent.OpenHookConfig(worktreeRoot, (&CopilotCLIAgent{}).HookConfigRelPath()) //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n}\n\n// InstallHooks installs Copilot CLI hooks in .github/hooks/entire.json.\n// If force is true, removes existing Entire hooks before installing.\n// Returns the number of hooks installed.\n// Unknown top-level fields and hook types are preserved on round-trip.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) InstallHooks(ctx context.Context, force bool) (int, error) {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\n\t// Use raw maps to preserve unknown fields on round-trip\n\tvar rawFile map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tvar rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage\n\n\texistingData, readErr := cfg.Read()\n\tswitch {\n\tcase readErr == nil:\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(existingData, &rawFile); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse existing %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif hooksRaw, ok := rawFile[\"hooks\"]; ok {\n\t\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(hooksRaw, &rawHooks); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse hooks in %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, ok := rawFile[\"version\"]; !ok {\n\t\t\trawFile[\"version\"] = json.RawMessage(`1`)\n\t\t}\n\tcase errors.Is(readErr, os.ErrNotExist):\n\t\trawFile = map[string]json.RawMessage{\n\t\t\t\"version\": json.RawMessage(`1`),\n\t\t}\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read %s: %w\", HooksFileName, readErr)\n\t}\n\n\tif rawHooks == nil {\n\t\trawHooks = make(map[string]json.RawMessage)\n\t}\n\n\t// Parse existing entries for each hook type we manage\n\thookEntries := make(map[string][]CopilotHookEntry)\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tvar entries []CopilotHookEntry\n\t\tif err := parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, &entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\thookEntries[hookName] = entries\n\t}\n\n\t// If force, remove existing Entire hooks first\n\tif force {\n\t\tfor hookName, entries := range hookEntries {\n\t\t\thookEntries[hookName] = removeEntireHooks(entries)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Define command prefix\n\tconst cmdPrefix = \"entire hooks copilot-cli \"\n\n\tcount := 0\n\n\t// Sync each hook to its desired command. Entire-owned entries carrying any\n\t// other command are dropped first, even without --force: a hook written by\n\t// an older version would otherwise survive alongside the one added below and\n\t// keep firing, which for the removed local-dev mode means a script inside\n\t// the working tree still runs on every agent turn.\n\tstaleDropped := false\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tcmd := agent.WrapProductionSilentHookCommand(cmdPrefix + hookName)\n\t\tentries := hookEntries[hookName]\n\n\t\t// Keep the matching entry rather than remove-and-re-add: entry-level\n\t\t// fields (cwd, timeoutSec, env) live on the existing entry and a freshly\n\t\t// constructed one would discard them.\n\t\tkept, dropped := agent.DropStaleManagedHooks(entries, hookEntryBash, []string{cmd})\n\t\tif dropped {\n\t\t\tstaleDropped = true\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries = kept\n\n\t\tif !hookBashExists(entries, cmd) {\n\t\t\tentries = append(entries, CopilotHookEntry{\n\t\t\t\tType:    \"command\",\n\t\t\t\tBash:    cmd,\n\t\t\t\tComment: \"Entire CLI\",\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t\tcount++\n\t\t}\n\t\thookEntries[hookName] = entries\n\t}\n\n\t// staleDropped forces a write even when nothing was added: a file holding\n\t// both a stale and a current hook adds nothing, and returning early here\n\t// would leave the stale hook on disk.\n\tif count == 0 && !staleDropped {\n\t\treturn 0, nil\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal modified hook types back into rawHooks\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tif err := marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, hookEntries[hookName]); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal hooks and update raw file\n\thooksJSON, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(rawHooks)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hooks: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\trawFile[\"hooks\"] = hooksJSON\n\n\t// Write to file\n\toutput, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(rawFile, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tif err := cfg.Write(output, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n\t}\n\n\treturn count, nil\n}\n\n// UninstallHooks removes Entire hooks from Copilot CLI's entire.json.\n// Unknown top-level fields and hook types are preserved on round-trip.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) UninstallHooks(ctx context.Context) error {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := cfg.Read()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treturn nil // No hooks file means nothing to uninstall\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar rawFile map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &rawFile); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tif hooksRaw, ok := rawFile[\"hooks\"]; ok {\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(hooksRaw, &rawHooks); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse hooks in %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif rawHooks == nil {\n\t\trawHooks = make(map[string]json.RawMessage)\n\t}\n\n\t// Parse and remove Entire hooks from each hook type we manage\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tvar entries []CopilotHookEntry\n\t\tif err := parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, &entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries = removeEntireHooks(entries)\n\t\tif err := marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal hooks back (preserving unknown hook types)\n\tif len(rawHooks) > 0 {\n\t\thooksJSON, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(rawHooks)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hooks: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\trawFile[\"hooks\"] = hooksJSON\n\t} else {\n\t\tdelete(rawFile, \"hooks\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Write back\n\toutput, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(rawFile, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tif err := cfg.Write(output, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// AreHooksInstalled checks if Entire hooks are installed in the Copilot CLI\n// config.\n//\n// A missing config file is an answer — no hooks — while an unreadable or\n// malformed one is an error: \"we could not tell\" and \"there are none\" are\n// different things to a caller deciding whether hooks can be left alone.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) AreHooksInstalled(ctx context.Context) (bool, error) {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn false, err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := cfg.Read()\n\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn false, nil\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"copilot-cli: failed to read hooks file\", \"path\", cfg.Path(), \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %w\", cfg.Path(), err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar hooksFile CopilotHooksFile\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &hooksFile); err != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"copilot-cli: failed to parse hooks file\", \"path\", cfg.Path(), \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"parse %s: %w\", cfg.Path(), err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn hasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.UserPromptSubmitted) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SessionStart) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.AgentStop) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SessionEnd) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SubagentStop) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.PreToolUse) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.PostToolUse) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.ErrorOccurred), nil\n}\n\n// GetSupportedHooks returns the normalized lifecycle events this agent supports.\n// Note: HookNames() returns 8 hooks but GetSupportedHooks() returns only 6.\n// The two not listed here are:\n//   - subagentStop: handled by ParseHookEvent (returns SubagentEnd), but there is no\n//     HookType constant for subagent events (they use EventType instead).\n//   - errorOccurred: pass-through hook with no lifecycle action (ParseHookEvent returns nil).\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) GetSupportedHooks() []agent.HookType {\n\treturn []agent.HookType{\n\t\tagent.HookSessionStart,\n\t\tagent.HookSessionEnd,\n\t\tagent.HookUserPromptSubmit,\n\t\tagent.HookStop,\n\t\tagent.HookPreToolUse,\n\t\tagent.HookPostToolUse,\n\t}\n}\n\n// parseCopilotHookType parses a specific hook type from rawHooks into the target slice.\nfunc parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage, hookType string, target *[]CopilotHookEntry) error {\n\tif data, ok := rawHooks[hookType]; ok {\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, target); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid JSON for hook type %s: %w\", hookType, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// marshalCopilotHookType marshals a hook type back into rawHooks.\n// If the slice is empty, removes the key from rawHooks.\nfunc marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage, hookType string, entries []CopilotHookEntry) error {\n\tif len(entries) == 0 {\n\t\tdelete(rawHooks, hookType)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tdata, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(entries)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hook type %s: %w\", hookType, err)\n\t}\n\trawHooks[hookType] = data\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// hookBashExists checks if a hook with the given bash command already exists.\nfunc hookBashExists(entries []CopilotHookEntry, bash string) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif entry.Bash == bash {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// isEntireHook checks if a hook entry's bash command belongs to Entire.\n// hookEntryBash reads the command off a hook entry for the shared helpers.\n// Copilot CLI stores it under `bash`, not `command`.\nfunc hookEntryBash(e CopilotHookEntry) string { return e.Bash }\n\nfunc isEntireHook(bash string) bool {\n\treturn agent.IsManagedHookCommand(bash)\n}\n\n// hasEntireHook checks if any entry in the slice is an Entire hook.\nfunc hasEntireHook(entries []CopilotHookEntry) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif isEntireHook(entry.Bash) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// removeEntireHooks removes all Entire hooks from the slice.\nfunc removeEntireHooks(entries []CopilotHookEntry) []CopilotHookEntry {\n\tresult := make([]CopilotHookEntry, 0, len(entries))\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif !isEntireHook(entry.Bash) {\n\t\t\tresult = append(result, entry)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn result\n}\n\n// HookConfigRelPath implements agent.HookConfigLocator.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) HookConfigRelPath() string { return hooksDir + \"/\" + HooksFileName }\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n)\n\n// testSessionID is the UUID used in captured Copilot CLI hook payloads.\nconst testSessionID = \"b0ff98c0-8e01-4b73-bf92-9649b139931b\"\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Prompt != \"hi\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected prompt 'hi', got %q\", event.Prompt)\n\t}\n\tif event.Timestamp.IsZero() {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected non-zero timestamp\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted_TranscriptRef(t *testing.T) {\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tt.Setenv(\"ENTIRE_TEST_COPILOT_SESSION_DIR\", \"/test/sessions\")\n\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"test-sess-id\",\"prompt\":\"hello\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\texpected := \"/test/sessions/test-sess-id/events.jsonl\"\n\tif event.SessionRef != expected {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected SessionRef %q, got %q\", expected, event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"transcript_path\":\"/tmp/transcript.json\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Prompt != \"hi\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected prompt 'hi', got %q\", event.Prompt)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != \"/tmp/transcript.json\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionStart(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081383,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"source\":\"new\",\"initialPrompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Timestamp.IsZero() {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected non-zero timestamp\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionStart_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\ttranscriptPath := \"/home/user/.copilot/session-state/\" + testSessionID + \"/events.jsonl\"\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"transcriptPath\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != transcriptPath {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\ttranscriptPath := \"/tmp/transcript.json\"\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"Stop\",\"transcript_path\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef !=…11020 tokens truncated…t/copilotcli/hooks.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend existing hook-name/install table tests to expect `subagent-start`; run them red because only eight hooks are installed.\n- [ ] Add upgrade coverage proving a pre-feature `entire.json` remains recognized as installed while reinstall adds exactly the missing managed hook and preserves user entries/unknown fields.\n- [ ] Add `CheckHookConfig` tests for absent and user-only files (`HooksAbsent`), exact current configuration (`HooksCurrent`), missing `subagentStart`, stale managed commands, malformed JSON, and unreadable files (`HooksOutdated` once any managed ownership is present or currentness cannot be proven).\n- [ ] Run the new upgrade/freshness tests red.\n- [ ] Add `HookNameSubagentStart`, the `subagentStart` config key/field, and the managed hook entry through the existing install/uninstall loops.\n- [ ] Implement read-only `agent.HookFreshness` behavior without changing `AreHooksInstalled`'s ownership/presence semantics.\n- [ ] Include native and compatible `SubagentStart` in event validation without weakening VS Code mismatch rejection.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestInstallHooks|TestUninstallHooks|TestHookNames|TestCheckHookConfig' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 3: Parse complete native subagent payloads\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add one table-driven test covering captured camelCase start/stop and compatible snake_case start/stop, asserting session, stable correlation, child ID, labels, and transcript roles.\n- [ ] Add only distinct failure contracts: missing/ambiguous correlation, nullable transcript, and mismatched compatible event name.\n- [ ] Run the new tests red and confirm failures come from discarded fields/missing start handling.\n- [ ] Extend `hookEnvelope` with only captured/documented fields required for normalized events (`agentId`, agent type/name/display/description, and the proven correlation input).\n- [ ] Implement one correlation helper from Task 1's proven invariant and validate its result through existing tool-use ID rules. If identity is path-derived, first normalize and validate the path as the exact canonical store-relative child layout at both start and stop, then digest that canonical name—never the raw hook string.\n- [ ] Add path-derived correlation tests proving equivalent absolute/relative/cleaned spellings map identically, distinct same-type concurrent child paths remain distinct, and outside-store, wrong-layout, missing, or symlinked paths return no normalized event and create no marker.\n- [ ] Map start to `agent.SubagentStart` and stop to `agent.SubagentEnd` with identical `ToolUseID`; map stop `agentId` to `SubagentID`.\n- [ ] Keep Copilot stop `Final: false`; it is a single true-completion end event, not Claude Code's launch-stub-plus-later-final pair.\n- [ ] Set `SessionRef` and `SubagentTranscriptPath` according to captured parent/child path roles; never treat response text as a canonical transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent|TestParseHookEnvelope' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 4: Add marker-backed native lifecycle completion\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/event.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_git.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add failing lifecycle tests named `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentStart_MarkerBackedRegistersLiveRecord`, `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentEnd_MarkerBackedReadOnlyCompletes`, `...ConcurrentReverseStopsStayDisjoint`, `...DuplicateStopIsNoOp`, `...UnmatchedStopIsNoOp`, and `...MissingOrEndedParentIsNoOp`.\n- [ ] In the concurrent test, use two same-type tasks, reverse completion order, distinct child transcripts/files, and assert neither record receives the other's evidence.\n- [ ] Add a red metadata-merge test where start supplies the type but omits the description, stop supplies the description and agent ID, and the completed record retains all three. Stop values win when non-empty; each missing stop field falls back independently to start.\n- [ ] Add a red authoritative-path test where the declared child path disappears before condensation while a coincidental generic-layout `agent-<id>.jsonl` exists; assert the payload records transcript unavailability and never stores the generic file.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1` and verify the tests fail against the existing foreground path.\n- [ ] Add one narrowly named normalized-event marker for native start/stop lifecycles whose completion must claim a start-created record. Set it only on Copilot's proven native events.\n- [ ] Add `TaskRecord.DeclaredTranscriptAuthoritative` (name may be adjusted for clarity) so the no-fallback contract survives state persistence. Mark every native Copilot task authoritative even when its verified declared path is empty.\n- [ ] On marked start, mutate only an existing active parent state and add a live `TaskRecord` containing the proven `ToolUseID`, labels, start time, verified start `DeclaredTranscriptPath`, and authoritative-transcript bit; do not call `EnsureSessionExists` and do not resurrect ended state. Capture pre-task state only as best-effort fallback, not authoritative parallel file evidence.\n- [ ] Add a state JSON round-trip test proving the verified start path and authoritative bit survive serialization. Add lifecycle tests proving a stop without a path retains the start path and a non-empty verified stop path replaces it.\n- [ ] On marked Final=false end, require the matching live record, reject missing/ended parent state, first fill only the stop event's empty metadata fields from start, and complete exactly once. This makes every non-empty stop value authoritative without losing start-only fields.\n- [ ] Extend `strategy.applyTaskRecordCompletion` to write each non-empty merged completion value (`SubagentType`, `TaskDescription`, `AgentID`, and declared path) onto the live record, plus token usage and the authoritative bit. Keep the existing behavior for unmarked producers whose completion fields are empty.\n- [ ] Reuse/refactor existing completion machinery with `bypassNoChangesSkip: true`, an event-files-only option, and a no-layout-fallback option derived from the marker. For marked Copilot completion, accept only adapter-populated `Event.ModifiedFiles`; do not run the path-based `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset` analyzer or a whole-worktree scan.\n- [ ] In `completeSubagentTaskRecord`, do not call `ResolveAgentTranscriptPath` or reopen the transcript for marked authoritative events. In `materializeTaskRecords`, when the persisted authoritative bit is set, try only `DeclaredTranscriptPath`; if it is empty, missing, or unreadable, emit the existing path-free unavailability reason and do not call `resolveTaskTranscriptPath`.\n- [ ] Add a narrow authoritative-task reader in condensation that opens the agent's store with `agent.OpenSessionStore(ag, state.WorktreePath)`, converts the declared path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the captured Copilot layout, and reads with `SessionStore.ReadFile` (no-follow). Never pass authoritative paths to `readFirstTranscript` or unrestricted `agent.ReadTranscriptFile`.\n- [ ] Add race-regression tests that replace the child file with a symlink after parse/before dispatch and again immediately before condensation. Dispatch may retain files/usage already derived from the safely read original bytes, but it must perform no second read and must not attribute data found only in the symlink target; condensation stores the existing path-free transcript-unavailable reason and never the target bytes.\n- [ ] Keep existing unmarked foreground PostToolUse behavior and existing Final=true background behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`, `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test.*TaskRecord.*(Metadata|Authoritative|Fallback)' -count=1`, and `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_Subagent' -count=1`; make all green.\n\n### Task 5: Preserve subordinate-session safety\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend the existing phantom-session characterization test with both observed historical prefixes, `toolu_` and `tooluse_`, plus a real UUID parent session.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession' -count=1` and verify `tooluse_` fails.\n- [ ] Replace the single-prefix assumption with the narrowest predicate justified by captured current and historical evidence; do not classify arbitrary non-UUID user input as a child unless Copilot guarantees parent IDs are UUIDs.\n- [ ] Verify subordinate session lifecycle hooks remain suppressed while native parent-scoped subagent hooks still produce normalized events.\n- [ ] Re-run the exact focused command and make it green.\n\n### Task 6: Wire exact child files and usage without guessing\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify if evidence supports a canonical child file: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] If Task 1 proves a canonical child JSONL file, add a fixture proving the existing analyzer extracts only that child's files and an exact full-child token total only when that child file contains an authoritative `session.shutdown` record with non-empty `modelMetrics`.\n- [ ] Add an exact-only helper returning `(usage, exact)` (or equivalent) that never invokes the existing assistant-message fallback. Keep the public parent/session `TokenCalculator` behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Add `TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_ExactChildUsage` and `...PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil`, including assertions that parent/session aggregate fields are not copied into the child record and a child transcript containing only `assistant.message.outputTokens` yields nil usage.\n- [ ] Add path-confinement tests for a declared path outside Copilot's session store, a symlink inside the store, and a syntactically plausible but wrong-layout file. Each must yield nil child usage and an empty declared child transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_(ExactChildUsage|PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil)|Test.*ChildTranscript' -count=1` red.\n- [ ] Add one Copilot helper that canonicalizes the hook path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the exact captured `<session-store>/<child-session>/events.jsonl` layout, and reads it with `SessionStore.ReadFile`. The rooted no-follow read rejects symlinks and later replacements; do not call unrestricted `os.ReadFile` on hook input.\n- [ ] From that one safely read byte slice, populate `Event.ModifiedFiles` through the existing Copilot JSONL parsing helpers and set `Event.TokenUsage` only when the authoritative completion aggregate is present. A readable transcript with only fallback message tokens is not exact and leaves usage nil.\n- [ ] If per-agent usage exists only in a requested `--usage-output-file`, do not depend on it because Entire does not launch the user's Copilot process.\n- [ ] If no canonical child transcript exists, retain metadata with the existing unavailable reason, leave child usage nil, and do not reconstruct a transcript from response text.\n- [ ] Run the same focused command green.\n\n### Task 7: Prove durable per-child capture through simulated hooks\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/copilot_subagent_test.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/testenv.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n\n- [ ] Write one integration test that initializes an isolated repo, starts a Copilot parent session, sends two captured-shape native starts with the same agent type, creates one child transcript per native contract, and sends stops in reverse order.\n- [ ] Commit one child-owned file through normal prepare-commit-msg/post-commit hooks and assert two distinct `tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` records in the permanent checkpoint.\n- [ ] Assert each record retains its own `agent_id`, labels, disjoint file list, completion state, exact usage when the child fixture includes an authoritative aggregate, and child transcript or the existing path-free unavailability reason.\n- [ ] Include one read-only child in the same fixture and assert it remains a distinct durable record.\n- [ ] Include duplicate stop, unmatched stop, and post-ended-session stop in the same lifecycle setup only where assertions remain readable; otherwise rely on Task 4's direct tests rather than duplicating them.\n- [ ] Treat this as a green end-to-end characterization after Tasks 2-6, not as a false red TDD step. Tasks 4 and 6 supply the focused red/green proof for shared lifecycle and exact child evidence.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1` and make it green.\n- [ ] Make only adapter-level or narrowly necessary shared changes if the characterization exposes a gap; do not duplicate materialization or add Copilot-specific checkpoint storage.\n\n### Task 8: Pin `general-purpose` and update documentation\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify only if Task 1 proves deterministic fallback evidence: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n\n- [ ] Add a fixture matching Task 1's `general-purpose` evidence and verify it cannot create a phantom top-level session.\n- [ ] If capture exposes a stable parent session, globally unique task ID, true completion, and canonical child evidence, first add a failing parallel same-type correlation test, then implement the narrow fallback.\n- [ ] If any invariant is absent, keep fallback out of production and document the upstream exception and capability boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] Remove stale claims that Copilot has no `subagentStart`; document current payload roles, minimum verified version, native-agent coverage, correlation invariant, ordering, transcript availability, and historical subordinate-session behavior.\n- [ ] Update the agent guide's Copilot event matrix so it matches installed native start/stop behavior.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession|TestParseHookEvent_GeneralPurpose|TestHookNames' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 9: Strengthen the existing E2E scenario without duplicating it\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go`\n- Modify: `e2e/testutil/repo.go`\n- Reuse: `e2e/testutil` checkpoint readers\n\n- [ ] Add a small Copilot fixture helper in `e2e/testutil/repo.go` that writes both `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `.github/agents/entire-e2e-subagent.agent.md`, then commits them before `entire.Enable`, hook installation, and construction of `RepoState` (`HeadBefore`/`CheckpointBefore`). Its agent frontmatter uses `name: entire-e2e-subagent`, a required description, and minimal file-writing instructions.\n- [ ] For `s.Agent.Name() == \"copilot-cli\"`, explicitly prompt the parent to delegate to `entire-e2e-subagent`; do not rely on inference or the built-in `general-purpose` agent.\n- [ ] Keep existing cross-agent file/checkpoint assertions. Add Copilot-specific committed `tasks/` assertions keyed by the discovered single task directory: one task, expected child-created file, non-empty safe `agent_id`, and transcript presence/unavailability matching Task 1's proven contract.\n- [ ] Ensure the committed custom-agent fixture predates capture and is absent from child `files` attribution.\n- [ ] Assert `HeadBefore` already includes the fixture commit and the fixture commit did not advance `CheckpointBefore`; this protects the measured checkpoint baseline from setup contamination.\n- [ ] Update Vogon's prompt parsing only if the minimally changed Copilot wording breaks the existing canary.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow` and make it green.\n- [ ] Do not add a second Copilot-only E2E scenario unless the shared test cannot express a required assertion.\n\n### Task 10: Verify size, correctness, and real end-user behavior\n\n**Files:** All modified files plus a disposable smoke-test repository.\n\n- [ ] Run `mise run fmt` and inspect every rewrite.\n- [ ] Run `mise run lint` after the final format pass.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` against the complete working tree and remove accidental duplication rather than suppressing it.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check`.\n- [ ] Run `git diff --check` and compare production/test additions with the 450-700 line target; pause for redesign if additions exceed roughly 800.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit authorization for each real Copilot validation phase, including the E2E invocation and separate smoke; plan approval alone is insufficient.\n- [ ] With authorization, run `mise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli TestSubagentCommitFlow` using a current Copilot binary.\n- [ ] Before the separate smoke, build a wrapper-free candidate `entire` into a dedicated temporary bin directory with a unique `versioninfo.Version` stamp containing the source commit/dirty marker. Record its SHA-256, construct a fixed `PATH` with that bin directory first, and use `whence -a entire` (or platform equivalent) to prove no other reachable `entire` precedes or shadows it. Record `command -v entire`, `entire version`, and the installed hook command before launch; stop on any mismatch.\n- [ ] In a separate disposable end-user repository, set isolated `COPILOT_HOME`, `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`; pass authentication only through already-present supported environment variables. Do not copy credential files or the user's Copilot/GitHub config, and stop if isolated authentication cannot be supplied.\n- [ ] With that isolated environment, enable Copilot hooks, provision and commit the named custom agent before capture, run a real child that creates a distinctive file, and commit normally. Tie the resulting hook log session ID to the checkpoint, then assert the checkpoint metadata's `cli_version` equals the unique candidate stamp; this proves the task artifact came from that binary without adding runtime logging. Inspect for exactly one correlated child task, exact child evidence when available, and no phantom session/shadow branch.\n- [ ] Preserve only a credential-free structural smoke report and remove disposable artifacts.\n- [ ] Commit only after required local gates pass; push only when authorized, then follow all repository/PR gates to terminal status without merging.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788501460223,"completed_at_ms":1788501460223}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:57:40.272Z","ordinal":10592,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a06afe-8530-7892-9e75-aa4f7c0f00d2","call_id":"call_NxKPFBVV1rGoqO5qh4KUkQNx","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 21020)\nTotal output lines: 1708\n\npackage copilotcli\n\n// CopilotHooksFile represents the .github/hooks/entire.json structure.\n// Copilot CLI uses a flat JSON file with version and hooks sections.\n// All JSON files in .github/hooks/ are auto-discovered by the Copilot CLI.\n//\n\ntype CopilotHooksFile struct {\n\tVersion int          `json:\"version\"`\n\tHooks   CopilotHooks `json:\"hooks\"`\n}\n\n// CopilotHooks contains all hook configurations using camelCase keys.\n//\n\ntype CopilotHooks struct {\n\tUserPromptSubmitted []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"userPromptSubmitted,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionStart        []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"sessionStart,omitempty\"`\n\tAgentStop           []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"agentStop,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionEnd          []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"sessionEnd,omitempty\"`\n\tSubagentStop        []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"subagentStop,omitempty\"`\n\tPreToolUse          []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"preToolUse,omitempty\"`\n\tPostToolUse         []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"postToolUse,omitempty\"`\n\tErrorOccurred       []CopilotHookEntry `json:\"errorOccurred,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// CopilotHookEntry represents a single hook command.\n// Copilot CLI hooks have a type field (\"command\") and a bash field for the command string.\n// Optional fields (cwd, timeoutSec, env, comment) are preserved on round-trip.\n\ntype CopilotHookEntry struct {\n\tType       string            `json:\"type\"`\n\tBash       string            `json:\"bash\"`\n\tComment    string            `json:\"comment,omitempty\"`\n\tCwd        string            `json:\"cwd,omitempty\"`\n\tTimeoutSec int               `json:\"timeoutSec,omitempty\"`\n\tEnv        map[string]string `json:\"env,omitempty\"`\n}\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n)\n\n// HooksFileName is the hooks file managed by Entire for Copilot CLI.\nconst HooksFileName = \"entire.json\"\n\n// hooksDir is the directory within the repo where Copilot CLI looks for hook configs.\nconst hooksDir = \".github/hooks\"\n\n// hookConfigKey maps our kebab-case hook names to camelCase JSON keys.\nvar hookConfigKey = map[string]string{\n\tHookNameUserPromptSubmitted: \"userPromptSubmitted\",\n\tHookNameSessionStart:        \"sessionStart\",\n\tHookNameAgentStop:           \"agentStop\",\n\tHookNameSessionEnd:          \"sessionEnd\",\n\tHookNameSubagentStop:        \"subagentStop\",\n\tHookNamePreToolUse:          \"preToolUse\",\n\tHookNamePostToolUse:         \"postToolUse\",\n\tHookNameErrorOccurred:       \"errorOccurred\",\n}\n\n// copilotHookConfig returns .github/hooks/entire.json for the current worktree,\n// opened through the worktree's root. That directory lives in the working tree,\n// which arrives by clone, so a checked-in symlink at `.github` or\n// `.github/hooks` must not be something Entire creates directories under and\n// writes through. See agent.HookConfigFile.\nfunc copilotHookConfig(ctx context.Context) (*agent.HookConfigFile, error) {\n\tworktreeRoot, err := paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\t// Not a repository (tests, and `enable` before `git init`): the process\n\t\t// directory is the only candidate, and it is a directory the caller\n\t\t// chose rather than one derived from anything read off disk.\n\t\tworktreeRoot = \".\"\n\t}\n\treturn agent.OpenHookConfig(worktreeRoot, (&CopilotCLIAgent{}).HookConfigRelPath()) //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n}\n\n// InstallHooks installs Copilot CLI hooks in .github/hooks/entire.json.\n// If force is true, removes existing Entire hooks before installing.\n// Returns the number of hooks installed.\n// Unknown top-level fields and hook types are preserved on round-trip.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) InstallHooks(ctx context.Context, force bool) (int, error) {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\n\t// Use raw maps to preserve unknown fields on round-trip\n\tvar rawFile map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tvar rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage\n\n\texistingData, readErr := cfg.Read()\n\tswitch {\n\tcase readErr == nil:\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(existingData, &rawFile); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse existing %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif hooksRaw, ok := rawFile[\"hooks\"]; ok {\n\t\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(hooksRaw, &rawHooks); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse hooks in %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, ok := rawFile[\"version\"]; !ok {\n\t\t\trawFile[\"version\"] = json.RawMessage(`1`)\n\t\t}\n\tcase errors.Is(readErr, os.ErrNotExist):\n\t\trawFile = map[string]json.RawMessage{\n\t\t\t\"version\": json.RawMessage(`1`),\n\t\t}\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read %s: %w\", HooksFileName, readErr)\n\t}\n\n\tif rawHooks == nil {\n\t\trawHooks = make(map[string]json.RawMessage)\n\t}\n\n\t// Parse existing entries for each hook type we manage\n\thookEntries := make(map[string][]CopilotHookEntry)\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tvar entries []CopilotHookEntry\n\t\tif err := parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, &entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\thookEntries[hookName] = entries\n\t}\n\n\t// If force, remove existing Entire hooks first\n\tif force {\n\t\tfor hookName, entries := range hookEntries {\n\t\t\thookEntries[hookName] = removeEntireHooks(entries)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Define command prefix\n\tconst cmdPrefix = \"entire hooks copilot-cli \"\n\n\tcount := 0\n\n\t// Sync each hook to its desired command. Entire-owned entries carrying any\n\t// other command are dropped first, even without --force: a hook written by\n\t// an older version would otherwise survive alongside the one added below and\n\t// keep firing, which for the removed local-dev mode means a script inside\n\t// the working tree still runs on every agent turn.\n\tstaleDropped := false\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tcmd := agent.WrapProductionSilentHookCommand(cmdPrefix + hookName)\n\t\tentries := hookEntries[hookName]\n\n\t\t// Keep the matching entry rather than remove-and-re-add: entry-level\n\t\t// fields (cwd, timeoutSec, env) live on the existing entry and a freshly\n\t\t// constructed one would discard them.\n\t\tkept, dropped := agent.DropStaleManagedHooks(entries, hookEntryBash, []string{cmd})\n\t\tif dropped {\n\t\t\tstaleDropped = true\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries = kept\n\n\t\tif !hookBashExists(entries, cmd) {\n\t\t\tentries = append(entries, CopilotHookEntry{\n\t\t\t\tType:    \"command\",\n\t\t\t\tBash:    cmd,\n\t\t\t\tComment: \"Entire CLI\",\n\t\t\t})\n\t\t\tcount++\n\t\t}\n\t\thookEntries[hookName] = entries\n\t}\n\n\t// staleDropped forces a write even when nothing was added: a file holding\n\t// both a stale and a current hook adds nothing, and returning early here\n\t// would leave the stale hook on disk.\n\tif count == 0 && !staleDropped {\n\t\treturn 0, nil\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal modified hook types back into rawHooks\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tif err := marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, hookEntries[hookName]); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal hooks and update raw file\n\thooksJSON, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(rawHooks)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hooks: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\trawFile[\"hooks\"] = hooksJSON\n\n\t// Write to file\n\toutput, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(rawFile, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tif err := cfg.Write(output, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n\t}\n\n\treturn count, nil\n}\n\n// UninstallHooks removes Entire hooks from Copilot CLI's entire.json.\n// Unknown top-level fields and hook types are preserved on round-trip.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) UninstallHooks(ctx context.Context) error {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := cfg.Read()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treturn nil // No hooks file means nothing to uninstall\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to read %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar rawFile map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &rawFile); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage\n\tif hooksRaw, ok := rawFile[\"hooks\"]; ok {\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(hooksRaw, &rawHooks); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse hooks in %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif rawHooks == nil {\n\t\trawHooks = make(map[string]json.RawMessage)\n\t}\n\n\t// Parse and remove Entire hooks from each hook type we manage\n\tfor _, hookName := range c.HookNames() {\n\t\tkey := hookConfigKey[hookName]\n\t\tvar entries []CopilotHookEntry\n\t\tif err := parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, &entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tentries = removeEntireHooks(entries)\n\t\tif err := marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks, key, entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s hooks: %w\", key, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Marshal hooks back (preserving unknown hook types)\n\tif len(rawHooks) > 0 {\n\t\thooksJSON, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(rawHooks)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hooks: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\trawFile[\"hooks\"] = hooksJSON\n\t} else {\n\t\tdelete(rawFile, \"hooks\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Write back\n\toutput, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(rawFile, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal %s: %w\", HooksFileName, err)\n\t}\n\n\tif err := cfg.Write(output, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err //nolint:wrapcheck // agent.HookConfigFile already names the file in its error\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// AreHooksInstalled checks if Entire hooks are installed in the Copilot CLI\n// config.\n//\n// A missing config file is an answer — no hooks — while an unreadable or\n// malformed one is an error: \"we could not tell\" and \"there are none\" are\n// different things to a caller deciding whether hooks can be left alone.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) AreHooksInstalled(ctx context.Context) (bool, error) {\n\tcfg, err := copilotHookConfig(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn false, err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := cfg.Read()\n\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn false, nil\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"copilot-cli: failed to read hooks file\", \"path\", cfg.Path(), \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"read %s: %w\", cfg.Path(), err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar hooksFile CopilotHooksFile\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &hooksFile); err != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"copilot-cli: failed to parse hooks file\", \"path\", cfg.Path(), \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"parse %s: %w\", cfg.Path(), err)\n\t}\n\n\treturn hasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.UserPromptSubmitted) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SessionStart) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.AgentStop) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SessionEnd) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.SubagentStop) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.PreToolUse) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.PostToolUse) ||\n\t\thasEntireHook(hooksFile.Hooks.ErrorOccurred), nil\n}\n\n// GetSupportedHooks returns the normalized lifecycle events this agent supports.\n// Note: HookNames() returns 8 hooks but GetSupportedHooks() returns only 6.\n// The two not listed here are:\n//   - subagentStop: handled by ParseHookEvent (returns SubagentEnd), but there is no\n//     HookType constant for subagent events (they use EventType instead).\n//   - errorOccurred: pass-through hook with no lifecycle action (ParseHookEvent returns nil).\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) GetSupportedHooks() []agent.HookType {\n\treturn []agent.HookType{\n\t\tagent.HookSessionStart,\n\t\tagent.HookSessionEnd,\n\t\tagent.HookUserPromptSubmit,\n\t\tagent.HookStop,\n\t\tagent.HookPreToolUse,\n\t\tagent.HookPostToolUse,\n\t}\n}\n\n// parseCopilotHookType parses a specific hook type from rawHooks into the target slice.\nfunc parseCopilotHookType(rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage, hookType string, target *[]CopilotHookEntry) error {\n\tif data, ok := rawHooks[hookType]; ok {\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, target); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid JSON for hook type %s: %w\", hookType, err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// marshalCopilotHookType marshals a hook type back into rawHooks.\n// If the slice is empty, removes the key from rawHooks.\nfunc marshalCopilotHookType(rawHooks map[string]json.RawMessage, hookType string, entries []CopilotHookEntry) error {\n\tif len(entries) == 0 {\n\t\tdelete(rawHooks, hookType)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tdata, err := jsonutil.MarshalWithNoHTMLEscape(entries)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to marshal hook type %s: %w\", hookType, err)\n\t}\n\trawHooks[hookType] = data\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// hookBashExists checks if a hook with the given bash command already exists.\nfunc hookBashExists(entries []CopilotHookEntry, bash string) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif entry.Bash == bash {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// isEntireHook checks if a hook entry's bash command belongs to Entire.\n// hookEntryBash reads the command off a hook entry for the shared helpers.\n// Copilot CLI stores it under `bash`, not `command`.\nfunc hookEntryBash(e CopilotHookEntry) string { return e.Bash }\n\nfunc isEntireHook(bash string) bool {\n\treturn agent.IsManagedHookCommand(bash)\n}\n\n// hasEntireHook checks if any entry in the slice is an Entire hook.\nfunc hasEntireHook(entries []CopilotHookEntry) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif isEntireHook(entry.Bash) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// removeEntireHooks removes all Entire hooks from the slice.\nfunc removeEntireHooks(entries []CopilotHookEntry) []CopilotHookEntry {\n\tresult := make([]CopilotHookEntry, 0, len(entries))\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif !isEntireHook(entry.Bash) {\n\t\t\tresult = append(result, entry)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn result\n}\n\n// HookConfigRelPath implements agent.HookConfigLocator.\nfunc (c *CopilotCLIAgent) HookConfigRelPath() string { return hooksDir + \"/\" + HooksFileName }\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n)\n\n// testSessionID is the UUID used in captured Copilot CLI hook payloads.\nconst testSessionID = \"b0ff98c0-8e01-4b73-bf92-9649b139931b\"\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Prompt != \"hi\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected prompt 'hi', got %q\", event.Prompt)\n\t}\n\tif event.Timestamp.IsZero() {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected non-zero timestamp\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted_TranscriptRef(t *testing.T) {\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tt.Setenv(\"ENTIRE_TEST_COPILOT_SESSION_DIR\", \"/test/sessions\")\n\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081360,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"test-sess-id\",\"prompt\":\"hello\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\texpected := \"/test/sessions/test-sess-id/events.jsonl\"\n\tif event.SessionRef != expected {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected SessionRef %q, got %q\", expected, event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_UserPromptSubmitted_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"transcript_path\":\"/tmp/transcript.json\",\"prompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameUserPromptSubmitted, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Prompt != \"hi\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected prompt 'hi', got %q\", event.Prompt)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != \"/tmp/transcript.json\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionStart(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480081383,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"source\":\"new\",\"initialPrompt\":\"hi\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.Timestamp.IsZero() {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected non-zero timestamp\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_SessionStart_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameSessionStart, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.SessionStart {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.SessionStart, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\ttranscriptPath := \"/home/user/.copilot/session-state/\" + testSessionID + \"/events.jsonl\"\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":1771480085412,\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"transcriptPath\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef != transcriptPath {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected transcript path in SessionRef, got %q\", event.SessionRef)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseHookEvent_AgentStop_VSCodePayload(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tag := &CopilotCLIAgent{}\n\ttranscriptPath := \"/tmp/transcript.json\"\n\tinput := `{\"timestamp\":\"2026-02-09T10:30:00.000Z\",\"cwd\":\"/path/to/repo\",\"sessionId\":\"` + testSessionID + `\",\"hookEventName\":\"Stop\",\"transcript_path\":\"` + transcriptPath + `\",\"stopReason\":\"end_turn\"}`\n\n\tevent, err := ag.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNameAgentStop, strings.NewReader(input))\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\trequire.NotNil(t, event, \"expected event, got nil\")\n\tif event.Type != agent.TurnEnd {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected event type %v, got %v\", agent.TurnEnd, event.Type)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionID != testSessionID {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"expected session_id %q, got %q\", testSessionID, event.SessionID)\n\t}\n\tif event.SessionRef !=…11020 tokens truncated…t/copilotcli/hooks.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend existing hook-name/install table tests to expect `subagent-start`; run them red because only eight hooks are installed.\n- [ ] Add upgrade coverage proving a pre-feature `entire.json` remains recognized as installed while reinstall adds exactly the missing managed hook and preserves user entries/unknown fields.\n- [ ] Add `CheckHookConfig` tests for absent and user-only files (`HooksAbsent`), exact current configuration (`HooksCurrent`), missing `subagentStart`, stale managed commands, malformed JSON, and unreadable files (`HooksOutdated` once any managed ownership is present or currentness cannot be proven).\n- [ ] Run the new upgrade/freshness tests red.\n- [ ] Add `HookNameSubagentStart`, the `subagentStart` config key/field, and the managed hook entry through the existing install/uninstall loops.\n- [ ] Implement read-only `agent.HookFreshness` behavior without changing `AreHooksInstalled`'s ownership/presence semantics.\n- [ ] Include native and compatible `SubagentStart` in event validation without weakening VS Code mismatch rejection.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestInstallHooks|TestUninstallHooks|TestHookNames|TestCheckHookConfig' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 3: Parse complete native subagent payloads\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add one table-driven test covering captured camelCase start/stop and compatible snake_case start/stop, asserting session, stable correlation, child ID, labels, and transcript roles.\n- [ ] Add only distinct failure contracts: missing/ambiguous correlation, nullable transcript, and mismatched compatible event name.\n- [ ] Run the new tests red and confirm failures come from discarded fields/missing start handling.\n- [ ] Extend `hookEnvelope` with only captured/documented fields required for normalized events (`agentId`, agent type/name/display/description, and the proven correlation input).\n- [ ] Implement one correlation helper from Task 1's proven invariant and validate its result through existing tool-use ID rules. If identity is path-derived, first normalize and validate the path as the exact canonical store-relative child layout at both start and stop, then digest that canonical name—never the raw hook string.\n- [ ] Add path-derived correlation tests proving equivalent absolute/relative/cleaned spellings map identically, distinct same-type concurrent child paths remain distinct, and outside-store, wrong-layout, missing, or symlinked paths return no normalized event and create no marker.\n- [ ] Map start to `agent.SubagentStart` and stop to `agent.SubagentEnd` with identical `ToolUseID`; map stop `agentId` to `SubagentID`.\n- [ ] Keep Copilot stop `Final: false`; it is a single true-completion end event, not Claude Code's launch-stub-plus-later-final pair.\n- [ ] Set `SessionRef` and `SubagentTranscriptPath` according to captured parent/child path roles; never treat response text as a canonical transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent|TestParseHookEnvelope' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 4: Add marker-backed native lifecycle completion\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/event.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_git.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add failing lifecycle tests named `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentStart_MarkerBackedRegistersLiveRecord`, `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentEnd_MarkerBackedReadOnlyCompletes`, `...ConcurrentReverseStopsStayDisjoint`, `...DuplicateStopIsNoOp`, `...UnmatchedStopIsNoOp`, and `...MissingOrEndedParentIsNoOp`.\n- [ ] In the concurrent test, use two same-type tasks, reverse completion order, distinct child transcripts/files, and assert neither record receives the other's evidence.\n- [ ] Add a red metadata-merge test where start supplies the type but omits the description, stop supplies the description and agent ID, and the completed record retains all three. Stop values win when non-empty; each missing stop field falls back independently to start.\n- [ ] Add a red authoritative-path test where the declared child path disappears before condensation while a coincidental generic-layout `agent-<id>.jsonl` exists; assert the payload records transcript unavailability and never stores the generic file.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1` and verify the tests fail against the existing foreground path.\n- [ ] Add one narrowly named normalized-event marker for native start/stop lifecycles whose completion must claim a start-created record. Set it only on Copilot's proven native events.\n- [ ] Add `TaskRecord.DeclaredTranscriptAuthoritative` (name may be adjusted for clarity) so the no-fallback contract survives state persistence. Mark every native Copilot task authoritative even when its verified declared path is empty.\n- [ ] On marked start, mutate only an existing active parent state and add a live `TaskRecord` containing the proven `ToolUseID`, labels, start time, verified start `DeclaredTranscriptPath`, and authoritative-transcript bit; do not call `EnsureSessionExists` and do not resurrect ended state. Capture pre-task state only as best-effort fallback, not authoritative parallel file evidence.\n- [ ] Add a state JSON round-trip test proving the verified start path and authoritative bit survive serialization. Add lifecycle tests proving a stop without a path retains the start path and a non-empty verified stop path replaces it.\n- [ ] On marked Final=false end, require the matching live record, reject missing/ended parent state, first fill only the stop event's empty metadata fields from start, and complete exactly once. This makes every non-empty stop value authoritative without losing start-only fields.\n- [ ] Extend `strategy.applyTaskRecordCompletion` to write each non-empty merged completion value (`SubagentType`, `TaskDescription`, `AgentID`, and declared path) onto the live record, plus token usage and the authoritative bit. Keep the existing behavior for unmarked producers whose completion fields are empty.\n- [ ] Reuse/refactor existing completion machinery with `bypassNoChangesSkip: true`, an event-files-only option, and a no-layout-fallback option derived from the marker. For marked Copilot completion, accept only adapter-populated `Event.ModifiedFiles`; do not run the path-based `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset` analyzer or a whole-worktree scan.\n- [ ] In `completeSubagentTaskRecord`, do not call `ResolveAgentTranscriptPath` or reopen the transcript for marked authoritative events. In `materializeTaskRecords`, when the persisted authoritative bit is set, try only `DeclaredTranscriptPath`; if it is empty, missing, or unreadable, emit the existing path-free unavailability reason and do not call `resolveTaskTranscriptPath`.\n- [ ] Add a narrow authoritative-task reader in condensation that opens the agent's store with `agent.OpenSessionStore(ag, state.WorktreePath)`, converts the declared path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the captured Copilot layout, and reads with `SessionStore.ReadFile` (no-follow). Never pass authoritative paths to `readFirstTranscript` or unrestricted `agent.ReadTranscriptFile`.\n- [ ] Add race-regression tests that replace the child file with a symlink after parse/before dispatch and again immediately before condensation. Dispatch may retain files/usage already derived from the safely read original bytes, but it must perform no second read and must not attribute data found only in the symlink target; condensation stores the existing path-free transcript-unavailable reason and never the target bytes.\n- [ ] Keep existing unmarked foreground PostToolUse behavior and existing Final=true background behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`, `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test.*TaskRecord.*(Metadata|Authoritative|Fallback)' -count=1`, and `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_Subagent' -count=1`; make all green.\n\n### Task 5: Preserve subordinate-session safety\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend the existing phantom-session characterization test with both observed historical prefixes, `toolu_` and `tooluse_`, plus a real UUID parent session.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession' -count=1` and verify `tooluse_` fails.\n- [ ] Replace the single-prefix assumption with the narrowest predicate justified by captured current and historical evidence; do not classify arbitrary non-UUID user input as a child unless Copilot guarantees parent IDs are UUIDs.\n- [ ] Verify subordinate session lifecycle hooks remain suppressed while native parent-scoped subagent hooks still produce normalized events.\n- [ ] Re-run the exact focused command and make it green.\n\n### Task 6: Wire exact child files and usage without guessing\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify if evidence supports a canonical child file: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] If Task 1 proves a canonical child JSONL file, add a fixture proving the existing analyzer extracts only that child's files and an exact full-child token total only when that child file contains an authoritative `session.shutdown` record with non-empty `modelMetrics`.\n- [ ] Add an exact-only helper returning `(usage, exact)` (or equivalent) that never invokes the existing assistant-message fallback. Keep the public parent/session `TokenCalculator` behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Add `TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_ExactChildUsage` and `...PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil`, including assertions that parent/session aggregate fields are not copied into the child record and a child transcript containing only `assistant.message.outputTokens` yields nil usage.\n- [ ] Add path-confinement tests for a declared path outside Copilot's session store, a symlink inside the store, and a syntactically plausible but wrong-layout file. Each must yield nil child usage and an empty declared child transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_(ExactChildUsage|PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil)|Test.*ChildTranscript' -count=1` red.\n- [ ] Add one Copilot helper that canonicalizes the hook path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the exact captured `<session-store>/<child-session>/events.jsonl` layout, and reads it with `SessionStore.ReadFile`. The rooted no-follow read rejects symlinks and later replacements; do not call unrestricted `os.ReadFile` on hook input.\n- [ ] From that one safely read byte slice, populate `Event.ModifiedFiles` through the existing Copilot JSONL parsing helpers and set `Event.TokenUsage` only when the authoritative completion aggregate is present. A readable transcript with only fallback message tokens is not exact and leaves usage nil.\n- [ ] If per-agent usage exists only in a requested `--usage-output-file`, do not depend on it because Entire does not launch the user's Copilot process.\n- [ ] If no canonical child transcript exists, retain metadata with the existing unavailable reason, leave child usage nil, and do not reconstruct a transcript from response text.\n- [ ] Run the same focused command green.\n\n### Task 7: Prove durable per-child capture through simulated hooks\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/copilot_subagent_test.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/testenv.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n\n- [ ] Write one integration test that initializes an isolated repo, starts a Copilot parent session, sends two captured-shape native starts with the same agent type, creates one child transcript per native contract, and sends stops in reverse order.\n- [ ] Commit one child-owned file through normal prepare-commit-msg/post-commit hooks and assert two distinct `tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` records in the permanent checkpoint.\n- [ ] Assert each record retains its own `agent_id`, labels, disjoint file list, completion state, exact usage when the child fixture includes an authoritative aggregate, and child transcript or the existing path-free unavailability reason.\n- [ ] Include one read-only child in the same fixture and assert it remains a distinct durable record.\n- [ ] Include duplicate stop, unmatched stop, and post-ended-session stop in the same lifecycle setup only where assertions remain readable; otherwise rely on Task 4's direct tests rather than duplicating them.\n- [ ] Treat this as a green end-to-end characterization after Tasks 2-6, not as a false red TDD step. Tasks 4 and 6 supply the focused red/green proof for shared lifecycle and exact child evidence.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1` and make it green.\n- [ ] Make only adapter-level or narrowly necessary shared changes if the characterization exposes a gap; do not duplicate materialization or add Copilot-specific checkpoint storage.\n\n### Task 8: Pin `general-purpose` and update documentation\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify only if Task 1 proves deterministic fallback evidence: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n\n- [ ] Add a fixture matching Task 1's `general-purpose` evidence and verify it cannot create a phantom top-level session.\n- [ ] If capture exposes a stable parent session, globally unique task ID, true completion, and canonical child evidence, first add a failing parallel same-type correlation test, then implement the narrow fallback.\n- [ ] If any invariant is absent, keep fallback out of production and document the upstream exception and capability boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] Remove stale claims that Copilot has no `subagentStart`; document current payload roles, minimum verified version, native-agent coverage, correlation invariant, ordering, transcript availability, and historical subordinate-session behavior.\n- [ ] Update the agent guide's Copilot event matrix so it matches installed native start/stop behavior.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession|TestParseHookEvent_GeneralPurpose|TestHookNames' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 9: Strengthen the existing E2E scenario without duplicating it\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go`\n- Modify: `e2e/testutil/repo.go`\n- Reuse: `e2e/testutil` checkpoint readers\n\n- [ ] Add a small Copilot fixture helper in `e2e/testutil/repo.go` that writes both `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `.github/agents/entire-e2e-subagent.agent.md`, then commits them before `entire.Enable`, hook installation, and construction of `RepoState` (`HeadBefore`/`CheckpointBefore`). Its agent frontmatter uses `name: entire-e2e-subagent`, a required description, and minimal file-writing instructions.\n- [ ] For `s.Agent.Name() == \"copilot-cli\"`, explicitly prompt the parent to delegate to `entire-e2e-subagent`; do not rely on inference or the built-in `general-purpose` agent.\n- [ ] Keep existing cross-agent file/checkpoint assertions. Add Copilot-specific committed `tasks/` assertions keyed by the discovered single task directory: one task, expected child-created file, non-empty safe `agent_id`, and transcript presence/unavailability matching Task 1's proven contract.\n- [ ] Ensure the committed custom-agent fixture predates capture and is absent from child `files` attribution.\n- [ ] Assert `HeadBefore` already includes the fixture commit and the fixture commit did not advance `CheckpointBefore`; this protects the measured checkpoint baseline from setup contamination.\n- [ ] Update Vogon's prompt parsing only if the minimally changed Copilot wording breaks the existing canary.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow` and make it green.\n- [ ] Do not add a second Copilot-only E2E scenario unless the shared test cannot express a required assertion.\n\n### Task 10: Verify size, correctness, and real end-user behavior\n\n**Files:** All modified files plus a disposable smoke-test repository.\n\n- [ ] Run `mise run fmt` and inspect every rewrite.\n- [ ] Run `mise run lint` after the final format pass.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` against the complete working tree and remove accidental duplication rather than suppressing it.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check`.\n- [ ] Run `git diff --check` and compare production/test additions with the 450-700 line target; pause for redesign if additions exceed roughly 800.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit authorization for each real Copilot validation phase, including the E2E invocation and separate smoke; plan approval alone is insufficient.\n- [ ] With authorization, run `mise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli TestSubagentCommitFlow` using a current Copilot binary.\n- [ ] Before the separate smoke, build a wrapper-free candidate `entire` into a dedicated temporary bin directory with a unique `versioninfo.Version` stamp containing the source commit/dirty marker. Record its SHA-256, construct a fixed `PATH` with that bin directory first, and use `whence -a entire` (or platform equivalent) to prove no other reachable `entire` precedes or shadows it. Record `command -v entire`, `entire version`, and the installed hook command before launch; stop on any mismatch.\n- [ ] In a separate disposable end-user repository, set isolated `COPILOT_HOME`, `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`; pass authentication only through already-present supported environment variables. Do not copy credential files or the user's Copilot/GitHub config, and stop if isolated authentication cannot be supplied.\n- [ ] With that isolated environment, enable Copilot hooks, provision and commit the named custom agent before capture, run a real child that creates a distinctive file, and commit normally. Tie the resulting hook log session ID to the checkpoint, then assert the checkpoint metadata's `cli_version` equals the unique candidate stamp; this proves the task artifact came from that binary without adding runtime logging. Inspect for exactly one correlated child task, exact child evidence when available, and no phantom session/shadow branch.\n- [ ] Preserve only a credential-free structural smoke report and remove disposable artifacts.\n- [ ] Commit only after required local gates pass; push only when authorized, then follow all repository/PR gates to terminal status without merging.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788501460.272817}}}
