{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T08:11:19.435Z","ordinal":10981,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a7bc72c3487d08390d5cdd2a62080","status":"completed","call_id":"call_duOsuBDKTXhnYlMasNAOI5iK","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Delete File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788509126.081434}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T08:11:19.554Z","ordinal":10982,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-ce5b5a7e-718b-4ea6-85f5-08a447fd7cea","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md":{"type":"delete","content":"# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Implementation Plan\n\n> **Execution constraint:** Implement this plan sequentially in the primary session. Do not launch implementation subagents. Follow the red/green checkpoints task-by-task; checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax records progress.\n\n**Goal:** Track each hook-emitting Copilot CLI subagent as its own durable Entire task with correct identity, files, transcript availability, and exact token usage when natively available.\n\n**Architecture:** Upgrade the Copilot adapter to consume native `subagentStart` and the complete `subagentStop` payload, then feed those events into a narrow marker-backed path in Entire's existing task-record lifecycle. A real-current-Copilot evidence gate must prove collision-free correlation, event ordering, and transcript availability before production mapping is chosen; ambiguous `general-purpose` behavior stays fail-closed rather than heuristic.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, Cobra hook commands, Copilot CLI JSON hooks/JSONL sessions, testify, Entire integration harness, mise.\n\n**Design:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md`\n\n---\n\n### Task 0: Refresh the clean feature branch\n\n**Files:** None\n\n- [ ] Confirm `git status --short` has no tracked changes and record `git rev-parse HEAD` plus `git rev-parse origin/main`.\n- [ ] Run `git fetch origin main`. If this feature branch still has no unique commits, fast-forward it with `git merge --ff-only origin/main`; if it has diverged, stop and inspect rather than rewriting history.\n- [ ] Re-run the relevant Copilot adapter tests on the refreshed base before starting the evidence capture.\n\n### Task 1: Capture the current Copilot subagent contract\n\n**Files:**\n- Use: `/tmp` disposable repository and capture directory only\n- Reference: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md`\n- Reference: historical `scripts/test-copilot-cli-agent-integration.sh`\n\n- [ ] Obtain explicit user authorization for the real Copilot invocations in this task; do not treat plan approval as paid-E2E approval.\n- [ ] Record the candidate and installed Copilot versions; use an isolated official Copilot CLI 1.0.82-or-newer binary without replacing the user's installed binary.\n- [ ] Create a disposable git repository with isolated Entire config/cache/token-store paths. Keep Copilot authentication available without modifying the user's Copilot configuration; if an isolated `COPILOT_HOME` cannot authenticate, stop rather than copy credentials into artifacts.\n- [ ] Register capture-only `subagentStart`, `subagentStop`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `agentStop`, `sessionEnd`, and subordinate session lifecycle hooks; restrict tool hooks to the task tool when matchers support it.\n- [ ] Provision and commit `.github/agents/entire-evidence-subagent.agent.md` with a lowercase stable name, required `description`, and minimal instructions. Create it before the measured session so it is not attributed to a child.\n- [ ] Run two same-type native children concurrently: one creates a distinctive file and one is read-only. Concurrency is mandatory if transcript path is considered as correlation evidence.\n- [ ] Run one built-in `general-purpose` child to confirm the documented hook exception and observe subordinate lifecycle/event evidence.\n- [ ] Capture only hook names, payload key names/types, IDs, timestamps, event ordering, transcript paths, transcript event types, file existence/identity, and usage field structure; do not preserve prompts, responses, file contents, credentials, or tokens.\n- [ ] Prove start/stop order relative to parent `agentStop` and `sessionEnd`, when child transcript bytes become readable, and whether they remain readable through normal commit-time condensation.\n- [ ] Prove whether `transcriptPath` is parent or child, stable across start/stop, and unique across the concurrent same-type children.\n- [ ] Select the correlation mapping and record it in `AGENT.md` before production code:\n  - native child ID present at both boundaries: use it directly for `ToolUseID`;\n  - stable unique child transcript path at both boundaries: use a deterministic path-safe digest and retain stop `agentId` as `SubagentID`;\n  - no one-to-one invariant: stop and revise the design; never match by description, timestamp proximity, or latest state.\n- [ ] If parent `sessionEnd` can precede native child stop, stop and revise the lifecycle design before Task 4; the current SessionEnd sweep cannot safely synthesize missing stop metadata.\n- [ ] Determine whether a canonical child transcript or exact per-agent machine-readable usage persists without requiring Entire to launch Copilot with special flags.\n- [ ] Remove the disposable repository and retain only a credential-free structural report outside the product diff.\n\n### Task 2: Install, preserve, and diagnose `subagentStart`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/types.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend existing hook-name/install table tests to expect `subagent-start`; run them red because only eight hooks are installed.\n- [ ] Add upgrade coverage proving a pre-feature `entire.json` remains recognized as installed while reinstall adds exactly the missing managed hook and preserves user entries/unknown fields.\n- [ ] Add `CheckHookConfig` tests for absent and user-only files (`HooksAbsent`), exact current configuration (`HooksCurrent`), missing `subagentStart`, stale managed commands, malformed JSON, and unreadable files (`HooksOutdated` once any managed ownership is present or currentness cannot be proven).\n- [ ] Run the new upgrade/freshness tests red.\n- [ ] Add `HookNameSubagentStart`, the `subagentStart` config key/field, and the managed hook entry through the existing install/uninstall loops.\n- [ ] Implement read-only `agent.HookFreshness` behavior without changing `AreHooksInstalled`'s ownership/presence semantics.\n- [ ] Include native and compatible `SubagentStart` in event validation without weakening VS Code mismatch rejection.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestInstallHooks|TestUninstallHooks|TestHookNames|TestCheckHookConfig' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 3: Parse complete native subagent payloads\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add one table-driven test covering captured camelCase start/stop and compatible snake_case start/stop, asserting session, stable correlation, child ID, labels, and transcript roles.\n- [ ] Add only distinct failure contracts: missing/ambiguous correlation, nullable transcript, and mismatched compatible event name.\n- [ ] Run the new tests red and confirm failures come from discarded fields/missing start handling.\n- [ ] Extend `hookEnvelope` with only captured/documented fields required for normalized events (`agentId`, agent type/name/display/description, and the proven correlation input).\n- [ ] Implement one correlation helper from Task 1's proven invariant and validate its result through existing tool-use ID rules. If identity is path-derived, first normalize and validate the path as the exact canonical store-relative child layout at both start and stop, then digest that canonical name—never the raw hook string.\n- [ ] Add path-derived correlation tests proving equivalent absolute/relative/cleaned spellings map identically, distinct same-type concurrent child paths remain distinct, and outside-store, wrong-layout, missing, or symlinked paths return no normalized event and create no marker.\n- [ ] Map start to `agent.SubagentStart` and stop to `agent.SubagentEnd` with identical `ToolUseID`; map stop `agentId` to `SubagentID`.\n- [ ] Keep Copilot stop `Final: false`; it is a single true-completion end event, not Claude Code's launch-stub-plus-later-final pair.\n- [ ] Set `SessionRef` and `SubagentTranscriptPath` according to captured parent/child path roles; never treat response text as a canonical transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent|TestParseHookEnvelope' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 4: Add marker-backed native lifecycle completion\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/event.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_git.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Add failing lifecycle tests named `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentStart_MarkerBackedRegistersLiveRecord`, `TestHandleLifecycleSubagentEnd_MarkerBackedReadOnlyCompletes`, `...ConcurrentReverseStopsStayDisjoint`, `...DuplicateStopIsNoOp`, `...UnmatchedStopIsNoOp`, and `...MissingOrEndedParentIsNoOp`.\n- [ ] In the concurrent test, use two same-type tasks, reverse completion order, distinct child transcripts/files, and assert neither record receives the other's evidence.\n- [ ] Add a red metadata-merge test where start supplies the type but omits the description, stop supplies the description and agent ID, and the completed record retains all three. Stop values win when non-empty; each missing stop field falls back independently to start.\n- [ ] Add a red authoritative-path test where the declared child path disappears before condensation while a coincidental generic-layout `agent-<id>.jsonl` exists; assert the payload records transcript unavailability and never stores the generic file.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1` and verify the tests fail against the existing foreground path.\n- [ ] Add one narrowly named normalized-event marker for native start/stop lifecycles whose completion must claim a start-created record. Set it only on Copilot's proven native events.\n- [ ] Add `TaskRecord.DeclaredTranscriptAuthoritative` (name may be adjusted for clarity) so the no-fallback contract survives state persistence. Mark every native Copilot task authoritative even when its verified declared path is empty.\n- [ ] On marked start, mutate only an existing active parent state and add a live `TaskRecord` containing the proven `ToolUseID`, labels, start time, verified start `DeclaredTranscriptPath`, and authoritative-transcript bit; do not call `EnsureSessionExists` and do not resurrect ended state. Capture pre-task state only as best-effort fallback, not authoritative parallel file evidence.\n- [ ] Add a state JSON round-trip test proving the verified start path and authoritative bit survive serialization. Add lifecycle tests proving a stop without a path retains the start path and a non-empty verified stop path replaces it.\n- [ ] On marked Final=false end, require the matching live record, reject missing/ended parent state, first fill only the stop event's empty metadata fields from start, and complete exactly once. This makes every non-empty stop value authoritative without losing start-only fields.\n- [ ] Extend `strategy.applyTaskRecordCompletion` to write each non-empty merged completion value (`SubagentType`, `TaskDescription`, `AgentID`, and declared path) onto the live record, plus token usage and the authoritative bit. Keep the existing behavior for unmarked producers whose completion fields are empty.\n- [ ] Reuse/refactor existing completion machinery with `bypassNoChangesSkip: true`, an event-files-only option, and a no-layout-fallback option derived from the marker. For marked Copilot completion, accept only adapter-populated `Event.ModifiedFiles`; do not run the path-based `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset` analyzer or a whole-worktree scan.\n- [ ] In `completeSubagentTaskRecord`, do not call `ResolveAgentTranscriptPath` or reopen the transcript for marked authoritative events. In `materializeTaskRecords`, when the persisted authoritative bit is set, try only `DeclaredTranscriptPath`; if it is empty, missing, or unreadable, emit the existing path-free unavailability reason and do not call `resolveTaskTranscriptPath`.\n- [ ] Add a narrow authoritative-task reader in condensation that opens the agent's store with `agent.OpenSessionStore(ag, state.WorktreePath)`, converts the declared path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the captured Copilot layout, and reads with `SessionStore.ReadFile` (no-follow). Never pass authoritative paths to `readFirstTranscript` or unrestricted `agent.ReadTranscriptFile`.\n- [ ] Add race-regression tests that replace the child file with a symlink after parse/before dispatch and again immediately before condensation. Dispatch may retain files/usage already derived from the safely read original bytes, but it must perform no second read and must not attribute data found only in the symlink target; condensation stores the existing path-free transcript-unavailable reason and never the target bytes.\n- [ ] Keep existing unmarked foreground PostToolUse behavior and existing Final=true background behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`, `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test.*TaskRecord.*(Metadata|Authoritative|Fallback)' -count=1`, and `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_Subagent' -count=1`; make all green.\n\n### Task 5: Preserve subordinate-session safety\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] Extend the existing phantom-session characterization test with both observed historical prefixes, `toolu_` and `tooluse_`, plus a real UUID parent session.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession' -count=1` and verify `tooluse_` fails.\n- [ ] Replace the single-prefix assumption with the narrowest predicate justified by captured current and historical evidence; do not classify arbitrary non-UUID user input as a child unless Copilot guarantees parent IDs are UUIDs.\n- [ ] Verify subordinate session lifecycle hooks remain suppressed while native parent-scoped subagent hooks still produce normalized events.\n- [ ] Re-run the exact focused command and make it green.\n\n### Task 6: Wire exact child files and usage without guessing\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify if evidence supports a canonical child file: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n\n- [ ] If Task 1 proves a canonical child JSONL file, add a fixture proving the existing analyzer extracts only that child's files and an exact full-child token total only when that child file contains an authoritative `session.shutdown` record with non-empty `modelMetrics`.\n- [ ] Add an exact-only helper returning `(usage, exact)` (or equivalent) that never invokes the existing assistant-message fallback. Keep the public parent/session `TokenCalculator` behavior unchanged.\n- [ ] Add `TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_ExactChildUsage` and `...PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil`, including assertions that parent/session aggregate fields are not copied into the child record and a child transcript containing only `assistant.message.outputTokens` yields nil usage.\n- [ ] Add path-confinement tests for a declared path outside Copilot's session store, a symlink inside the store, and a syntactically plausible but wrong-layout file. Each must yield nil child usage and an empty declared child transcript.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop_(ExactChildUsage|PartialOrUnavailableChildUsageIsNil)|Test.*ChildTranscript' -count=1` red.\n- [ ] Add one Copilot helper that canonicalizes the hook path with `SessionStore.Name`, validates the exact captured `<session-store>/<child-session>/events.jsonl` layout, and reads it with `SessionStore.ReadFile`. The rooted no-follow read rejects symlinks and later replacements; do not call unrestricted `os.ReadFile` on hook input.\n- [ ] From that one safely read byte slice, populate `Event.ModifiedFiles` through the existing Copilot JSONL parsing helpers and set `Event.TokenUsage` only when the authoritative completion aggregate is present. A readable transcript with only fallback message tokens is not exact and leaves usage nil.\n- [ ] If per-agent usage exists only in a requested `--usage-output-file`, do not depend on it because Entire does not launch the user's Copilot process.\n- [ ] If no canonical child transcript exists, retain metadata with the existing unavailable reason, leave child usage nil, and do not reconstruct a transcript from response text.\n- [ ] Run the same focused command green.\n\n### Task 7: Prove durable per-child capture through simulated hooks\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/copilot_subagent_test.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/testenv.go`\n- Reuse: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n\n- [ ] Write one integration test that initializes an isolated repo, starts a Copilot parent session, sends two captured-shape native starts with the same agent type, creates one child transcript per native contract, and sends stops in reverse order.\n- [ ] Commit one child-owned file through normal prepare-commit-msg/post-commit hooks and assert two distinct `tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` records in the permanent checkpoint.\n- [ ] Assert each record retains its own `agent_id`, labels, disjoint file list, completion state, exact usage when the child fixture includes an authoritative aggregate, and child transcript or the existing path-free unavailability reason.\n- [ ] Include one read-only child in the same fixture and assert it remains a distinct durable record.\n- [ ] Include duplicate stop, unmatched stop, and post-ended-session stop in the same lifecycle setup only where assertions remain readable; otherwise rely on Task 4's direct tests rather than duplicating them.\n- [ ] Treat this as a green end-to-end characterization after Tasks 2-6, not as a false red TDD step. Tasks 4 and 6 supply the focused red/green proof for shared lifecycle and exact child evidence.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1` and make it green.\n- [ ] Make only adapter-level or narrowly necessary shared changes if the characterization exposes a gap; do not duplicate materialization or add Copilot-specific checkpoint storage.\n\n### Task 8: Pin `general-purpose` and update documentation\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify only if Task 1 proves deterministic fallback evidence: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go`\n\n- [ ] Add a fixture matching Task 1's `general-purpose` evidence and verify it cannot create a phantom top-level session.\n- [ ] If capture exposes a stable parent session, globally unique task ID, true completion, and canonical child evidence, first add a failing parallel same-type correlation test, then implement the narrow fallback.\n- [ ] If any invariant is absent, keep fallback out of production and document the upstream exception and capability boundary explicitly.\n- [ ] Remove stale claims that Copilot has no `subagentStart`; document current payload roles, minimum verified version, native-agent coverage, correlation invariant, ordering, transcript availability, and historical subordinate-session behavior.\n- [ ] Update the agent guide's Copilot event matrix so it matches installed native start/stop behavior.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -run 'TestParseHookEvent_SubagentSession|TestParseHookEvent_GeneralPurpose|TestHookNames' -count=1` and make it green.\n\n### Task 9: Strengthen the existing E2E scenario without duplicating it\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go`\n- Modify: `e2e/testutil/repo.go`\n- Reuse: `e2e/testutil` checkpoint readers\n\n- [ ] Add a small Copilot fixture helper in `e2e/testutil/repo.go` that writes both `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `.github/agents/entire-e2e-subagent.agent.md`, then commits them before `entire.Enable`, hook installation, and construction of `RepoState` (`HeadBefore`/`CheckpointBefore`). Its agent frontmatter uses `name: entire-e2e-subagent`, a required description, and minimal file-writing instructions.\n- [ ] For `s.Agent.Name() == \"copilot-cli\"`, explicitly prompt the parent to delegate to `entire-e2e-subagent`; do not rely on inference or the built-in `general-purpose` agent.\n- [ ] Keep existing cross-agent file/checkpoint assertions. Add Copilot-specific committed `tasks/` assertions keyed by the discovered single task directory: one task, expected child-created file, non-empty safe `agent_id`, and transcript presence/unavailability matching Task 1's proven contract.\n- [ ] Ensure the committed custom-agent fixture predates capture and is absent from child `files` attribution.\n- [ ] Assert `HeadBefore` already includes the fixture commit and the fixture commit did not advance `CheckpointBefore`; this protects the measured checkpoint baseline from setup contamination.\n- [ ] Update Vogon's prompt parsing only if the minimally changed Copilot wording breaks the existing canary.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow` and make it green.\n- [ ] Do not add a second Copilot-only E2E scenario unless the shared test cannot express a required assertion.\n\n### Task 10: Verify size, correctness, and real end-user behavior\n\n**Files:** All modified files plus a disposable smoke-test repository.\n\n- [ ] Run `mise run fmt` and inspect every rewrite.\n- [ ] Run `mise run lint` after the final format pass.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestHandleLifecycleSubagent(Start|End)_MarkerBacked' -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `GOCACHE=/private/tmp/entire-go-cache go test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test -run TestCopilotSubagent -count=1`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run test:e2e:canary TestSubagentCommitFlow`.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` against the complete working tree and remove accidental duplication rather than suppressing it.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check`.\n- [ ] Run `git diff --check` and compare production/test additions with the 450-700 line target; pause for redesign if additions exceed roughly 800.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit authorization for each real Copilot validation phase, including the E2E invocation and separate smoke; plan approval alone is insufficient.\n- [ ] With authorization, run `mise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli TestSubagentCommitFlow` using a current Copilot binary.\n- [ ] Before the separate smoke, build a wrapper-free candidate `entire` into a dedicated temporary bin directory with a unique `versioninfo.Version` stamp containing the source commit/dirty marker. Record its SHA-256, construct a fixed `PATH` with that bin directory first, and use `whence -a entire` (or platform equivalent) to prove no other reachable `entire` precedes or shadows it. Record `command -v entire`, `entire version`, and the installed hook command before launch; stop on any mismatch.\n- [ ] In a separate disposable end-user repository, set isolated `COPILOT_HOME`, `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`, `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH`, and `ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE`; pass authentication only through already-present supported environment variables. Do not copy credential files or the user's Copilot/GitHub config, and stop if isolated authentication cannot be supplied.\n- [ ] With that isolated environment, enable Copilot hooks, provision and commit the named custom agent before capture, run a real child that creates a distinctive file, and commit normally. Tie the resulting hook log session ID to the checkpoint, then assert the checkpoint metadata's `cli_version` equals the unique candidate stamp; this proves the task artifact came from that binary without adding runtime logging. Inspect for exactly one correlated child task, exact child evidence when available, and no phantom session/shadow branch.\n- [ ] Preserve only a credential-free structural smoke report and remove disposable artifacts.\n- [ ] Commit only after required local gates pass; push only when authorized, then follow all repository/PR gates to terminal status without merging.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nD /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788509479480,"completed_at_ms":1788509479554}}
