{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:06:07.251Z","ordinal":11543,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9afa7bcd3887d09c912772830f376a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The reviewer finding was resolved at the adapter boundary: a child `agentStop` is identifiable because its `sessionId` is the child UUID while `transcriptPath` names the parent UUID. Entire converts that signal into cleanup for the transient child state and never analyzes the parent transcript as the child’s own session.\n- This keeps the solution small and avoids a global child registry or scanning every Copilot transcript. The authoritative task record still comes from the parent-scoped `subagentStop`, where both child UUID and parent transcript are explicitly available.\n- The concurrent join remains exact: `agentId → subagent.started.toolCallId → child tool events`. No ordering, “latest task,” or description matching enters production code.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788541563825,"completed_at_ms":1788541567251}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:06:07.254Z","ordinal":11544,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9afa7bcd3887d09c912772830f376a","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The reviewer finding was resolved at the adapter boundary: a child `agentStop` is identifiable because its `sessionId` is the child UUID while `transcriptPath` names the parent UUID. Entire converts that signal into cleanup for the transient child state and never analyzes the parent transcript as the child’s own session.\n- This keeps the solution small and avoids a global child registry or scanning every Copilot transcript. The authoritative task record still comes from the parent-scoped `subagentStop`, where both child UUID and parent transcript are explicitly available.\n- The concurrent join remains exact: `agentId → subagent.started.toolCallId → child tool events`. No ordering, “latest task,” or description matching enters production code.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788541558.958235,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
