{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:10:24.350Z","ordinal":11676,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9afb7ddacc87d0ab4394f88f2ccc8f","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The inline review found one documentation inconsistency—not a behavioral defect: older Copilot releases used `toolu_…` as child lifecycle session IDs, while the current verified release uses child UUIDs and a parent transcript path. The code handles both, but a comment still described the historical form as current. I’m correcting that and documenting the UUID cleanup path so future maintainers don’t accidentally remove either guard.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThere are two separate “phantom session” defenses because Copilot changed shapes across releases. Historical `toolu_…` child hooks can be rejected immediately; current UUID child hooks are indistinguishable at prompt time, so their transient state is retired when `agentStop` reveals that the transcript belongs to a different (parent) session.\n\nThat cleanup event intentionally has no transcript reference. This makes the shared lifecycle close the transient state without ever analyzing the parent transcript under the child’s identity.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788541821860,"completed_at_ms":1788541824350}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:10:24.353Z","ordinal":11677,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9afb7ddacc87d0ab4394f88f2ccc8f","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The inline review found one documentation inconsistency—not a behavioral defect: older Copilot releases used `toolu_…` as child lifecycle session IDs, while the current verified release uses child UUIDs and a parent transcript path. The code handles both, but a comment still described the historical form as current. I’m correcting that and documenting the UUID cleanup path so future maintainers don’t accidentally remove either guard.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThere are two separate “phantom session” defenses because Copilot changed shapes across releases. Historical `toolu_…` child hooks can be rejected immediately; current UUID child hooks are indistinguishable at prompt time, so their transient state is retired when `agentStop` reveals that the transcript belongs to a different (parent) session.\n\nThat cleanup event intentionally has no transcript reference. This makes the shared lifecycle close the transient state without ever analyzing the parent transcript under the child’s identity.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788541820.144509,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:10:38.071Z","ordinal":11678,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9afb80573087d08e78798da34eccc9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_vQpQYtYW50YTccgkpEH1oYgF","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go\\n@@\\n-// subagentSessionIDPrefix is the prefix Copilot uses when it reuses a Task\\n-// tool-use id as the sessionId on lifecycle hooks fired for a subagent turn.\\n-// Real Copilot session ids are UUIDs, so this prefix unambiguously marks a\\n-// subagent context (e.g. \\\"toolu_bdrk_01K…\\\" on Bedrock-backed models).\\n+// subagentSessionIDPrefix is the prefix older Copilot releases used when they\\n+// reused a Task tool-use id as the sessionId on child lifecycle hooks. Current\\n+// releases use a child UUID instead; buildAgentStop detects that shape from its\\n+// parent transcript path.\\n@@\\n-// isSubagentSessionID reports whether a Copilot sessionId is actually a\\n-// subagent's tool-use id rather than a real interactive session id.\\n+// isSubagentSessionID reports whether a Copilot sessionId uses the historical\\n+// child tool-use-id shape rather than a real interactive session ID.\\n@@\\n-\\t// Copilot fires the per-turn/session lifecycle hooks for subagent turns too,\\n-\\t// using the subagent's Task tool-use id (e.g. \\\"toolu_…\\\") as the sessionId.\\n+\\t// Older Copilot releases fire per-turn/session lifecycle hooks for children\\n+\\t// using the Task tool-use id (e.g. \\\"toolu_…\\\") as the sessionId.\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go\\n@@\\n import (\\n \\t\\\"context\\\"\\n \\t\\\"encoding/json\\\"\\n-\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\\\"\\n-\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\\\"\\n-\\t\\\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\\\"\\n \\t\\\"os\\\"\\n \\t\\\"path/filepath\\\"\\n \\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n \\t\\\"testing\\\"\\n+\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\\\"\\n )\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md\\n@@\\n two concurrent children to receive disjoint file lists even when they share a type.\\n+\\n+Current children also emit ordinary `userPromptSubmitted` and `agentStop` hooks\\n+with the child UUID as `sessionId`, while `agentStop.transcriptPath` still names\\n+the parent transcript. Entire uses that mismatch to retire any transient child\\n+session state without scanning the parent transcript as the child. The older\\n+`toolu_…` child-session shape remains ignored at hook parsing time.\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md\\n@@\\n Copilot stores all child events in the parent transcript; no standalone child\\n transcript exists. `subagent.completed` is appended only after the synchronous\\n stop hook returns. Full per-child token breakdown appears later in\\n@@\\n exact token breakdown while handling the child completion.\\n+\\n+Current children also emit ordinary lifecycle hooks with the child UUID as\\n+`sessionId`; their `agentStop.transcriptPath` still points at the parent. Entire\\n+uses that mismatch to retire transient child session state without scanning the\\n+parent transcript under the child identity. Historical `toolu_…` child session\\n+IDs remain rejected before shared lifecycle dispatch.\\n@@\\n - Duplicate, unmatched, missing-parent, and ended-parent stops create no extra\\n   record and never resurrect state.\\n+- Child lifecycle hooks leave no active phantom session and never analyze the\\n+  parent transcript as a child transcript.\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md\\n@@\\n-- [ ] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\\n+- [x] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\\n@@\\n-- [ ] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\\n+- [x] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788541820.144509}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:10:38.484Z","ordinal":11679,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-61c30c44-0729-411c-a90f-9597aaf3ed45","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -12,10 +12,10 @@\n \n-// subagentSessionIDPrefix is the prefix Copilot uses when it reuses a Task\n-// tool-use id as the sessionId on lifecycle hooks fired for a subagent turn.\n-// Real Copilot session ids are UUIDs, so this prefix unambiguously marks a\n-// subagent context (e.g. \"toolu_bdrk_01K…\" on Bedrock-backed models).\n+// subagentSessionIDPrefix is the prefix older Copilot releases used when they\n+// reused a Task tool-use id as the sessionId on child lifecycle hooks. Current\n+// releases use a child UUID instead; buildAgentStop detects that shape from its\n+// parent transcript path.\n const subagentSessionIDPrefix = \"toolu_\"\n \n-// isSubagentSessionID reports whether a Copilot sessionId is actually a\n-// subagent's tool-use id rather than a real interactive session id.\n+// isSubagentSessionID reports whether a Copilot sessionId uses the historical\n+// child tool-use-id shape rather than a real interactive session ID.\n func isSubagentSessionID(sessionID string) bool {\n@@ -88,4 +88,4 @@\n \n-\t// Copilot fires the per-turn/session lifecycle hooks for subagent turns too,\n-\t// using the subagent's Task tool-use id (e.g. \"toolu_…\") as the sessionId.\n+\t// Older Copilot releases fire per-turn/session lifecycle hooks for children\n+\t// using the Task tool-use id (e.g. \"toolu_…\") as the sessionId.\n \t// Those must NOT spin up a top-level Entire session: the subagent never gets\n","move_path":null},"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -43,2 +43,8 @@\n \n+Current children also emit ordinary lifecycle hooks with the child UUID as\n+`sessionId`; their `agentStop.transcriptPath` still points at the parent. Entire\n+uses that mismatch to retire transient child session state without scanning the\n+parent transcript under the child identity. Historical `toolu_…` child session\n+IDs remain rejected before shared lifecycle dispatch.\n+\n ## Design\n@@ -125,2 +131,4 @@\n   record and never resurrect state.\n+- Child lifecycle hooks leave no active phantom session and never analyze the\n+  parent transcript as a child transcript.\n - Condensation writes task metadata and never fabricates a child transcript.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -5,5 +5,2 @@\n \t\"encoding/json\"\n-\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n-\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\"\n-\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n \t\"os\"\n@@ -12,2 +9,6 @@\n \t\"testing\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n+\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\"\n+\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n )\n","move_path":null},"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -55,3 +55,3 @@\n - [x] Make the shared subagent E2E prompt explicitly delegate to that agent.\n-- [ ] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\n+- [x] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\n - [ ] With separate user authorization, run the paid real Copilot E2E.\n@@ -62,3 +62,3 @@\n - [x] Update the agent-guide event matrix.\n-- [ ] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\n+- [x] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\n - [ ] Run `mise run dup` and remove accidental duplication.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -217,2 +217,8 @@\n \n+Current children also emit ordinary `userPromptSubmitted` and `agentStop` hooks\n+with the child UUID as `sessionId`, while `agentStop.transcriptPath` still names\n+the parent transcript. Entire uses that mismatch to retire any transient child\n+session state without scanning the parent transcript as the child. The older\n+`toolu_…` child-session shape remains ignored at hook parsing time.\n+\n Copilot does not create standalone child transcript files. Task metadata therefore\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788541838197,"completed_at_ms":1788541838484}}
