{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:43:33.125Z","ordinal":12092,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9b0342ee1887d089cbdc4fcb5f1da3","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The adjusted all-package race suite passed every package, including integration and `redact`; the only omitted test is the unrelated fixture that is mechanically invalid in any checkout path containing spaces. No source workaround was added for that baseline issue.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe final design reuses Entire’s durable `TaskRecord` pipeline instead of inventing Copilot-specific checkpoint storage. Copilot contributes only the missing identity/file evidence and a truthful “no standalone transcript” bit; shared lifecycle still owns exactly-once completion and condensation.\n\nThe maintainability refactor also sharpened that boundary: `subagentTranscriptAndFiles` now centralizes the choice between a real child transcript and adapter-supplied child-scoped files, making it harder for a future agent integration to accidentally scan a parent transcript.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788543810947,"completed_at_ms":1788543813125}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:43:33.131Z","ordinal":12093,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9b0342ee1887d089cbdc4fcb5f1da3","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The adjusted all-package race suite passed every package, including integration and `redact`; the only omitted test is the unrelated fixture that is mechanically invalid in any checkout path containing spaces. No source workaround was added for that baseline issue.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe final design reuses Entire’s durable `TaskRecord` pipeline instead of inventing Copilot-specific checkpoint storage. Copilot contributes only the missing identity/file evidence and a truthful “no standalone transcript” bit; shared lifecycle still owns exactly-once completion and condensation.\n\nThe maintainability refactor also sharpened that boundary: `subagentTranscriptAndFiles` now centralizes the choice between a real child transcript and adapter-supplied child-scoped files, making it harder for a future agent integration to accidentally scan a parent transcript.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788543807.73665,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
