{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T20:37:12.541Z","ordinal":12351,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a082bc-1971-70f0-aecc-959aea46ada6","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa071f4833087d089fb2ff0e23cb67c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The paid E2E did invoke `copilot -p`, but through the Go E2E harness. I can also run a wrapper-free smoke test by calling `copilot -p` directly in a fresh repository, with the candidate Entire binary installing hooks, then commit and inspect the resulting checkpoint/task record manually.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe distinction is orchestration, not Copilot mode: both use non-interactive prompt mode. The direct smoke removes the Go test harness, retries, and assertions from the execution path, making it closer to what an end user actually types.\n\nI’ll keep the smoke isolated under `/private/tmp` and inspect the checkpoint for a real `tasks/.../task.json`, not just the created file.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788899829221,"completed_at_ms":1788899832541}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T20:37:12.544Z","ordinal":12352,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa071f4833087d089fb2ff0e23cb67c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The paid E2E did invoke `copilot -p`, but through the Go E2E harness. I can also run a wrapper-free smoke test by calling `copilot -p` directly in a fresh repository, with the candidate Entire binary installing hooks, then commit and inspect the resulting checkpoint/task record manually.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe distinction is orchestration, not Copilot mode: both use non-interactive prompt mode. The direct smoke removes the Go test harness, retries, and assertions from the execution path, making it closer to what an end user actually types.\n\nI’ll keep the smoke isolated under `/private/tmp` and inspect the checkpoint for a real `tasks/.../task.json`, not just the created file.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a082bc-1971-70f0-aecc-959aea46ada6","create_time":1788899820.285637,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
