{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T20:37:15.147Z","ordinal":12355,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa071f77e6487d0b345759285a6edaf","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2eR9wKgPZlUl5HkfQUkBpp02","name":"exec","input":"const results=await Promise.all([\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n -A45 \\\"func Enable\\\" e2e/entire e2e/testutil && ./entire enable --help | sed -n '1,180p'\",workdir:\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:12000}),\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"./entire status --help | sed -n '1,180p' && ./entire checkpoint list --help | sed -n '1,180p'\",workdir:\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:10000}),\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh auth status\",workdir:\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:5000})\n]);for(const r of results){text(r.output);text(`\\n[exit ${r.exit_code}]\\n`)}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a082bc-1971-70f0-aecc-959aea46ada6","create_time":1788899820.285637}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T20:37:15.337Z","ordinal":12356,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a082bc-1971-70f0-aecc-959aea46ada6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2f9fccbd-dda9-49b0-995f-7a73b0bcf8a5","process_id":"56713","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -A45 \"func Enable\" e2e/entire e2e/testutil && ./entire enable --help | sed -n '1,180p'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -A45 \"func Enable\" e2e/entire e2e/testutil && ./entire enable --help | sed -n '1,180p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Enable Entire with session tracking for your AI agent workflows.\n\nIf Entire is not yet configured, this runs the full configuration flow.\nIf Entire is already configured but disabled, this re-enables it.\n\nIf the current directory is not a git repository, Entire can initialize one\nfor you and (optionally) create a matching GitHub repository via the gh CLI.\n\nUsage:\n  entire enable [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --absolute-git-hook-path               Embed full binary path in git hooks (for GUI git clients that don't source shell profiles)\n      --agent string                         Agent to set up hooks for (e.g., claude-code, codex, copilot-cli, cursor, factoryai-droid, gemini, opencode, pi; external agents on $PATH are also available). Enables non-interactive mode.\n      --agent-help-skill entire agent-help   Install the stable Entire agent-help skill (points agents at entire agent-help) for selected agent(s)\n      --checkpoint-backend string            Checkpoint storage backend: refs (default; one git ref per checkpoint) or branch (legacy shared entire/checkpoints/v1 branch)\n      --checkpoint-remote string             Checkpoint remote in provider:owner/repo format (e.g., github:org/checkpoints-repo)\n  -f, --force                                Force reinstall hooks (removes existing Entire hooks first)\n  -h, --help                                 help for enable\n      --import-history                       During first-time setup, import the selected agents' existing session history (last 30 days) without prompting\n      --init-repo                            If not a git repo, initialize one non-interactively\n      --initial-commit-message string        Commit message for the initial commit when bootstrapping a new repo\n      --local                                Write settings to .entire/settings.local.json instead of .entire/settings.json\n      --no-github                            Initialize local git repo only; skip creating a GitHub remote\n      --no-init-repo                         If not a git repo, exit instead of prompting to initialize one\n      --project                              Write settings to .entire/settings.json even if it already exists\n      --push                                 When bootstrapping a new repo, push the initial commit to the created GitHub remote (implies creating the remote; without it the repo is created but not pushed)\n      --repo-name string                     GitHub repository name for the new repo (used when bootstrapping)\n      --repo-owner string                    GitHub user or organization login for the new repo\n      --repo-visibility string               GitHub repository visibility: public, private, or internal\n      --search-skill                         Install the optional Entire search skill for selected agent(s)\n      --skip-initial-commit                  Don't create the initial commit when bootstrapping a new repo\n      --skip-push-sessions                   Disable automatic pushing of session logs on git push\n      --telemetry                            Enable anonymous usage analytics (default true)\n  -y, --yes                                  Accept all defaults without prompting (in a non-repo directory: init git, create private GitHub repo, commit, and push; then enable all agents and accept telemetry). Does not import existing agent history — see --import-history\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Enable Entire with session tracking for your AI agent workflows.\n\nIf Entire is not yet configured, this runs the full configuration flow.\nIf Entire is already configured but disabled, this re-enables it.\n\nIf the current directory is not a git repository, Entire can initialize one\nfor you and (optionally) create a matching GitHub repository via the gh CLI.\n\nUsage:\n  entire enable [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --absolute-git-hook-path               Embed full binary path in git hooks (for GUI git clients that don't source shell profiles)\n      --agent string                         Agent to set up hooks for (e.g., claude-code, codex, copilot-cli, cursor, factoryai-droid, gemini, opencode, pi; external agents on $PATH are also available). Enables non-interactive mode.\n      --agent-help-skill entire agent-help   Install the stable Entire agent-help skill (points agents at entire agent-help) for selected agent(s)\n      --checkpoint-backend string            Checkpoint storage backend: refs (default; one git ref per checkpoint) or branch (legacy shared entire/checkpoints/v1 branch)\n      --checkpoint-remote string             Checkpoint remote in provider:owner/repo format (e.g., github:org/checkpoints-repo)\n  -f, --force                                Force reinstall hooks (removes existing Entire hooks first)\n  -h, --help                                 help for enable\n      --import-history                       During first-time setup, import the selected agents' existing session history (last 30 days) without prompting\n      --init-repo                       