{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:38:45.497Z","ordinal":12869,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a08852-be4f-7670-ad56-d6966ac22275","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f5fb20e6-f632-433f-9bd4-ffa5da425737","process_id":"86598","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,260p' /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/committer/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/committer/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/committer/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: committer\ndescription: Prepare clear, scoped commit messages and help organize changes into coherent commits.\n---\n\n# Committer\n\nYou help the user turn working tree changes into clean, understandable commits. Your focus is on commit quality, logical grouping, and clear commit messages.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to help commit changes:\n\n1. Inspect the current changes.\n2. Identify whether the changes should be split into multiple commits.\n3. Group related changes together.\n4. Write commit messages that are:\n   - Specific\n   - Short but meaningful\n   - Scoped to the actual change\n5. If appropriate, suggest a sequence of commits before making them.\n6. Flag mixed concerns or unrelated edits that should not be committed together.\n\n## Output style\n\nBe opinionated and practical. Prefer concise commit messages and clear rationale for grouping.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Preparing a branch for review\n- Splitting a large working tree into smaller commits\n- Writing commit messages\n- Catching unrelated changes before commit\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: committer\ndescription: Prepare clear, scoped commit messages and help organize changes into coherent commits.\n---\n\n# Committer\n\nYou help the user turn working tree changes into clean, understandable commits. Your focus is on commit quality, logical grouping, and clear commit messages.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to help commit changes:\n\n1. Inspect the current changes.\n2. Identify whether the changes should be split into multiple commits.\n3. Group related changes together.\n4. Write commit messages that are:\n   - Specific\n   - Short but meaningful\n   - Scoped to the actual change\n5. If appropriate, suggest a sequence of commits before making them.\n6. Flag mixed concerns or unrelated edits that should not be committed together.\n\n## Output style\n\nBe opinionated and practical. Prefer concise commit messages and clear rationale for grouping.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Preparing a branch for review\n- Splitting a large working tree into smaller commits\n- Writing commit messages\n- Catching unrelated changes before commit\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":1834},"formatted_output":"---\nname: committer\ndescription: Prepare clear, scoped commit messages and help organize changes into coherent commits.\n---\n\n# Committer\n\nYou help the user turn working tree changes into clean, understandable commits. Your focus is on commit quality, logical grouping, and clear commit messages.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to help commit changes:\n\n1. Inspect the current changes.\n2. Identify whether the changes should be split into multiple commits.\n3. Group related changes together.\n4. Write commit messages that are:\n   - Specific\n   - Short but meaningful\n   - Scoped to the actual change\n5. If appropriate, suggest a sequence of commits before making them.\n6. Flag mixed concerns or unrelated edits that should not be committed together.\n\n## Output style\n\nBe opinionated and practical. Prefer concise commit messages and clear rationale for grouping.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Preparing a branch for review\n- Splitting a large working tree into smaller commits\n- Writing commit messages\n- Catching unrelated changes before commit\n"},"started_at_ms":1788993525496,"completed_at_ms":1788993525497}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:38:45.547Z","ordinal":12870,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a08852-d72b-7601-af10-30acb7198e68","call_id":"call_jFCF3wwwofaHz1KjLvlLYt0T","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---\nname: committer\ndescription: Prepare clear, scoped commit messages and help organize changes into coherent commits.\n---\n\n# Committer\n\nYou help the user turn working tree changes into clean, understandable commits. Your focus is on commit quality, logical grouping, and clear commit messages.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to help commit changes:\n\n1. Inspect the current changes.\n2. Identify whether the changes should be split into multiple commits.\n3. Group related changes together.\n4. Write commit messages that are:\n   - Specific\n   - Short but meaningful\n   - Scoped to the actual change\n5. If appropriate, suggest a sequence of commits before making them.\n6. Flag mixed concerns or unrelated edits that should not be committed together.\n\n## Output style\n\nBe opinionated and practical. Prefer concise commit messages and clear rationale for grouping.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Preparing a branch for review\n- Splitting a large working tree into smaller commits\n- Writing commit messages\n- Catching unrelated changes before commit\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08852-be4f-7670-ad56-d6966ac22275","create_time":1788993525.547133}}}
